rence, which lists the texture generator nodes, including the noise family. The helpx pages in the results say documentation has moved to Experience League, and the newer page is the one to use.\n\n**Scope:** Apart from the Atomic nodes, Designer also comes with a library of pre-made Graph Instances, divided up into many categories. The library holds more than 200 of them, and the reference notes that MDL nodes are missing, these might be added in the future.\n\n**Noise nodes:** Under Texture generators > Noises, the list includes 3D Perlin Noise and its fractal variant, 3D Ridged Noise Fractal, 3D Simplex Noise, 3D Voronoi (plus a fractal version), and 3D Worley Noise. It also has Anisotropic Noise, Blue Noise Fast, White Noise, and White Noise Fast. Stylized noise-type generators include Clouds 1–3, Cells 1–4, Crystal 1–2, Creased, Directional Noise 1–3, and BnW Spots 1–3 (the list continues past those entries in the results).\n\n**Related category:** Texture generators also includes a Patterns group, covering items such as Brick, Tile Generator, Gradient, Stripes, Weave, and Splatter nodes.\n\n**Documentation location:** The helpx pages state that Documentation for Substance Designer 3D is now available on Experience League. The same page says After March 14th, HelpX pages will automatically redirect to the equivalent Experience League page. The current version is at experienceleague.adobe.com under substance-3d-designer, in the node library section.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b89f1205-8c72-4507-b5dc-c3f35ab54964","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:18:50.480Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"c2647591-cc7d-4c45-bcab-75c4689a0f2b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":