{"parentUuid":"d766c6be-acf5-4733-80eb-f04f7fd483c1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a9840a94295146d85","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B9hVPRXWVZW8tSL77YUEPv","type":"tool_result","content":"#type:     node\r\n#context:  cop\r\n#internal: remap\r\n#icon:     COP/remap\r\n\r\n= Remap =\r\n\r\n\"\"\"Remaps a layer, VDB, or attribute.\"\"\"\r\n\r\nThis node remaps a layer, VDB, or attribute from an original range to a new range.\r\n\r\n@parameters\r\n\r\nSignature:\r\n    #id: signature\r\n    The layer type that the source accepts.\r\n\r\n    See [Signatures|/copernicus/glossary#signatures] for more information.\r\n\r\n:include /nodes/cop/_parameter_descriptions#mask/:\r\n\r\nOperation:\r\n    #id: op\r\n    The method used to remap the layer, VDB, or attribute.\r\n\r\n    Remap:\r\n        Remap the layer, VDB, or attribute from an input range to an output range.\r\n\r\n    Threshold:\r\n        Remap the layer, VDB, or attribute based on a threshold and a width to an output range. The threshold is equal to the midpoint.\r\n        \r\n        Any values above `0.5` become `1` and any values below `0.5` become `0` if __Threshold When__ is `Greater`, __Threshold__ is `0.5`, __Width__ is `0`, and the output is (`0,1`).\r\n\r\nCompute Range:\r\n    #id: computerange\r\n    Sets the __Input Min__ and __Input Max__ parameters to the minimum and maximum values of the `source` input.\r\n\r\nInput Min:\r\n    #id: inputmin\r\n    When __Operation__ is `Remap`, values lesser than or equal to this value are remapped to be __Output Min__.\r\n\r\n    TIP:\r\n        Click [Smallicon:BUTTONS/layer_sample] and then click on the layer to set the __Input Min__.\r\n\r\nInput Max:\r\n    #id: inputmax\r\n    When __Operation__ is `Remap`, values greater than or equal to this value are remapped to be __Output Max__.\r\n\r\n    TIP:\r\n        Click [Smallicon:BUTTONS/layer_sample] and then click on the layer to set the __Input Max__.\r\n\r\nThreshold When:\r\n    #id: side\r\n    When __Operation__ is `Threshold`, this determines whether to remap values that're higher than, lower than, or equal to the threshold.\r\n\r\n    Greater:\r\n        Remap values greater than the threshold to the higher end of the output range.\r\n\r\n    Greater or Equal:\r\n        Remap values greater than or equal to the threshold to the higher end of the output range.\r\n\r\n    Less:\r\n        Remap values lesser than the threshold to the higher end of the output range.\r\n\r\n    Less or Equal:\r\n        Remap values lesser than or equal to the threshold to the higher end of the output range.\r\n\r\nThreshold:\r\n    #id: threshold\r\n    When __Operation__ is `Threshold`, this is the value of the input range that maps to the midpoint of the output range.\r\n    \r\n    A __Threshold__ of `0.5` with a __Width__ of `0.0` represents an input range of (`0.5,0.5`).\r\n\r\n    TIP:\r\n        Click [Smallicon:BUTTONS/layer_sample] and then click on the layer to set the __Threshold__.\r\n\r\nWidth:\r\n    #id: width\r\n    When __Operation__ is `Threshold`, this is the range on both sides of the threshold that determines the input minimum and maximum.\r\n    \r\n    A __Threshold__ of `0.5` with a __Width__ of `0.2` represents an input range of (`0.4,0.6`).\r\n\r\nOutput Min:\r\n    #id: outputmin\r\n    The lower end of the output range.\r\n\r\nOutput Max:\r\n    #id: outputmax\r\n    The higher end of the output range.\r\n\r\nOutside Range:\r\n    #id: method\r\n    When __Operation__ is `Remap`, this determines how to treat values outside of the input range (__Input Min__ and __Input Max__).\r\n\r\n    Clamp at End:\r\n        Values outside of the input range clamp within the input range.\r\n\r\n    Repeat:\r\n        Values outside of the input range loop through the input range.\r\n\r\n    Extend:\r\n        Values outside of the input range extend the output range.\r\n\r\nUse Ramp:\r\n    #id: useramp\r\n    Applies the __Ramp__ parameter and any connected `ramp` input.\r\n\r\nRamp:\r\n    #id: ramp\r\n    A mono ramp that shapes the remapped output.\r\n\r\n    See [Ramp parameters|/network/ramps] for more information.\r\n\r\n@inputs\r\n    source:\r\n        The original layer, VDB, or attribute to remap.\r\n    \r\n    input_min:\r\n        An optional per-pixel layer, VDB, or attribute of the same type as the source that overrides the `input_min` parameter.\r\n    \r\n    input_max:\r\n        An optional per-pixel layer, VDB, or attribute of the same type as the source that overrides the `input_max` parameter.\r\n    \r\n    output_min:    \r\n        An optional per-pixel layer, VDB, or attribute of the same type as the source that overrides the `output_min` parameter.\r\n    \r\n    output_max:\r\n        An optional per-pixel layer, VDB, or attribute of the same type as the source that overrides the `output_max` parameter.\r\n\r\n    ramp:\r\n        An optional per-pixel remap ramp for the input, which overrides the __Ramp__ parameter.\r\n\r\n    :include /nodes/cop/_input_descriptions#mask/:\r\n\r\n@outputs\r\n    remap:\r\n        The remapped source layer, VDB, or attribute.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"017fda0b-b8e8-4e94-a9db-8a1f60eaaa7e","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:20:46.557Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5529d26e-da50-4bbe-92a2-99459447d721","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d766c6be-acf5-4733-80eb-f04f7fd483c1","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
