tomono | SDF to Mono | Converts an SDF field to a mono image layer.\n   in : sdf | out: mono\n   par: Background Value; Iso Range; Number of Cycles; Remap Ramp; Draw Shape; Shape Value; Iso Distance; Remap Ramp; Draw Outline; Outline Value; Outline Width; Alignment; Draw Shadowing; Shadow Density; Shadow Falloff; Shadow Value; Iso Offset; Onion Skin; Smooth; Anti-Aliasing; Invert\n## weave | Weave | Generates a woven fabric pattern of interlacing fibers.\n   in : size_ref, pattern | out: weave, uv, id\n   par: Rows; Columns; Weave Multiplier; NOTE; Every Nth Column; Every Nth Tile; Checkerboard; Row Inset; Column Inset; Edge Gradient; Overlap Gradient; Overlap Gradient Ramp; Fiber Scale; Fiber Strength\n## knit | Knit | Generates a grid of knitted fabric stitches.\n   in : size_ref, jitter, direction, angle, scale, stretch, color, alpha, flip | out: height, color, id, uv\n   par: Preset; Seed; Rows; Columns; Row Offset; Column Offset; Jitter Layer Mask; Jitter; Jitter Type {Per-Component Controls}; Jitter Scale; Scale Layer Mask; Scale; Scale Mode {Uniform/Variance/Min/Max}; Scale Variance; Min Value; Max Value; Stretch Layer Mask; Stretch Mode {Uniform/Variance/Min/Max}; Stretch X; Stretch Y; Stretch Variance; Min Value; Max Value; Angle Layer Mask; Direction Layer Mask; Angle; Angle Mode {Uniform/Variance/Min/Max}; Angle Variance; Min Value; Max Value; Round to Multiples; Knit Shape Type {Purl/Knit}; Width; Bulge Scale; Softness; Wrinkles; Wrinkle Size; Edge \n## hextile | Hex Tile | Randomly tiles texture.\n   in :  | out: \n   par: Size; Scale; Scale Random; Rotate; Rotate Random; Random Seed; Contrast; Falloff; Weight Exp\n#type:     node\n#context:  cop\n#internal: posmap\n#icon:     COP/posmap\n\n= Position Map =\n\n\"\"\"Generates a position map.\"\"\"\n\nThis node generates a position map, which is an RGB layer where each pixel represents a location in 3D space. You can use a position map as the reference location for noises, such as [Fractal Noise 3D|Node:/cop/fractalnoise3d].\n\nThe __X Border__, __Y Border__, and __Z Border__ parameters let you control how to map values outside the canonical 3D shape, which is a cube with sides of size `2`. This allows for the formation of periodic values. See [Border types|/copernicus/glossary#border] for more information.\n\n@parameters\n\nSignature:\n    #id: signature\n    \n    The layer type that the source accepts.\n\n    See [Signatures|/copernicus/glossary#signatures] for more information.\n\nSource Position:\n    #id: source\n\n    What location to use as the source position for a pixel.\n\n    Position:\n        The pixels location in world space is used.\n    Camera Origin:\n        The origin of the layer's camera in world space is used.  Note\n        this varies per pixel for othographic cameras.\n    View Direction:\n        The view direction for the pixel, a normalized vector pointing\n        away from the camera origin.\n\nX Border:\n    #id: xborder\n\n    The method used to map values outside the cube.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b7a34e7e-1f72-487a-a3ea-915160b7e069","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:40.052Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"794d727e-1900-4058-ab7a-08e0c3866e0b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"be032dba-1cb2-4db5-8044-556f4767f5a1","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
