 Noise 1.\ncop: @grunge_moisture with a different {Seed} and {Density}; look match UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## messy-fibers-1\nname: Messy Fibers 1\nsrc: /noises/messy-fibers-1/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Structured noise of tangled threads with adjustable direction and thread density.\nk: Scale | Grid subdivision of the noise tiles.\nk: Angle | Direction of the threads, in turns from horizontal right.\nk: Angle random | Maximum random variation of the angle.\nk: Lines number | Tiling of the base threads; higher gives denser, thinner lines.\nk: Disorder | Displaces the ingredients.\nuse: Fabric weave breakup, hair, moss threads, paper fibre relief.\ncop: @streakblur on @randommono or sparse noise at several {Angle} values merged with @blend ({Mode}=Maximum), or @shapescatter with thin line stamps and random {Angle}.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## messy-fibers-2\nname: Messy Fibers 2\nsrc: /noises/messy-fibers-2/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Second variation of Messy Fibers with the same controls.\nk: Scale | Grid subdivision of the noise tiles.\nk: Angle | Direction of the threads, in turns.\nk: Lines number | Density of the base threads.\nuse: Same roles as Messy Fibers 1.\ncop: Same as Messy Fibers 1 (@streakblur or @shapescatter); look match UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## messy-fibers-3\nname: Messy Fibers 3\nsrc: /noises/messy-fibers-3/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Third variation of Messy Fibers, with per-thread luminance randomisation instead of a line count.\nk: Scale | Grid subdivision of the noise tiles.\nk: Angle | Direction of the threads, in turns.\nk: Luminance random | Range of random darkening per thread (1 is the full range).\nuse: Same roles as Messy Fibers 1 with more tonal variation between fibres.\ncop: Same as Messy Fibers 1 plus {Stamp Color} set to Variance on @shapescatter, or per-strand values from @randommono; UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## voronoi\nname: Voronoi\nsrc: /noises/voronoi/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: 3D Voronoi noise projected to a 2D image with a Z-down orthographic projection, offering many distance styles (F1, F2, F2-F1, edges, random colour); GPU engine only.\nk: Scale | Scale of the noise (stepped when tiling is on).\nk: Size | Per-axis size of the noise in X, Y and Z.\nk: Offset | Offset of the noise position in X, Y and Z.\nk: Disorder | Random offset of each point in X, Y and Z.\nk: Distortion Intensity | Strength of a warp applied to the noise.\nk: Rounded Curve | Rounds the slope around each point so the cells become convex.\nk: Distance Scale | Scales the distance gradient around each point.\nk: Distance Mode | Metric: Euclidean, Manhattan, Chebyshev or Minkowski.\nk: Style | Which Voronoi quantity is drawn: F1, F2, F2-F1, F1*F2, F1/F2, Edge or Random color.\nk: Edge Thickness | Thickness of cell edges (Edge style only).\nk: Random Color Seed Mode | Seed source for the per-cell random colour.\nk: Non Square Expansion | Compensates squash and stretch on non-square ratios.\nuse: Cracked ground, stone plates and cell relief; the Edge style gives crack masks and F1 gives rounded pebbles.\ncop: @worleynoise: {o:dist1} is F1, {o:dist2} is F2, {o:border} is the Edge distance, {o:id} gives per-cell random values; {Metric} (Euclidean, Manhattan, Chebyshev), {Jitter} is Disorder, {Round Border} rounds the cell walls. F2-F1 and F1*F2 are computed by @blend or @wrangle from the two distance outputs.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## voronoi-fractal\nname: Voronoi Fractal\nsrc: /noises/voronoi-fractal/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Fractal (multi-octave) version of the Voronoi node, same projection and styles plus octave range, roughness, lacunarity and a blend mode between overlapping cells.\nk: Min Level | Lowest fractal repetition level.\nk: Max Level | Highest fractal repetition level.\nk: Roughness | Balance between low and high repetition levels.\nk: Lacunarity | How the fractal pattern fills space; higher gives fewer gaps.\nk: Global Opacity | Range of the fractal values around zero.\nk: Blend Mode | How overlapping cells combine across levels: Add, Max or Min.\nk: Style | Which Voronoi quantity is drawn (F1, F2, F2-F1, F1*F2, F1/F2, Edge, Random color).\nk: Distance Mode | Metric used for the distance gradient.\nuse: Complex crazed cracks, scaly layered rock and multi-scale cell relief in one node.\ncop: Several @worleynoise passes at growing {Element Size}/shrinking amplitude merged with @blend ({Mode} Add or Maximum / Minimum), or @fractalnoise with {Noise Type}=Worley Cellular F1 and {Fractal Type} chosen to match the Blend Mode; per-level control is manual (UNVERIFIED).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## 3d-voronoi\nname: 3D Voronoi\nsrc: /noises/3d-voronoi/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: low\npurpose: Voronoi noise evaluated in 3D from a Position Map input, so the pattern is continuous across a mesh surface.\nk: Scale | Scale of the noise (stepped when tiling is on).\nk: Size | Per-axis size in X, Y and Z.\nk: Offset | Offset of the noise position.\nk: Disorder | Random offset of each point in X, Y and Z.\nk: Distortion Intensity | Strength of the warp.\nk: Rounded Curve | Rounds the slope around each point.\nk: Distance Mode | Euclidean, Manhattan, Chebyshev or Minkowski.\nk: Style | F1, F2, F2-F1, F1*F2, F1/F2, Edge or Random color.\nk: Edge Thickness | Edge thickness (Edge style only).\nk: Enable Tiling | Makes the 3D pattern repeat along X, Y and Z.\nuse: Mesh-baked crack and stone masks that must be seamless across UV seams; rarely used for flat height tiles.\ncop: Feed @posmap (or a baked position layer; the {Z Border}/{X Border}/{Y Border} wrap modes give periodic positions) into @worleynoise3d (outputs {o:dist1}, {o:dist2}, {o:border}, {o:id}).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## 3d-voronoi-fractal\nname: 3D Voronoi Fractal\nsrc: /noises/3d-voronoi-fractal/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: low\npurpose: Fractal version of 3D Voronoi: several octaves of 3D Voronoi combined with Add, Max or Min.\nk: Min Level | Lowest fractal repetition level.\nk: Max Level | Highest fractal repetition level.\nk: Roughness | Balance between levels (available with Add blend mode).\nk: Lacunarity | How the pattern fills space.\nk: Blend Mode | Add, Max or Min between levels.\nk: Style | Voronoi quantity drawn.\nuse: Multi-scale cell relief continuous across mesh seams.\ncop: @posmap into several @worleynoise3d passes with different {Element Size}, merged with @blend; or @fractalnoise3d with {Noise Type}=Worley Cellular F1.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## 3d-worley-noise\nname: 3D Worley Noise\nsrc: /noises/3d-worley-noise/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: low\npurpose: Versatile Worley noise in 3D from a Position Map, with many metrics and combination styles.\nk: Scale | Global scale (1 to 64).\nk: Size | Per-axis scaling in X, Y and Z.\nk: Mode | Distance metric: Euclidean, Manhattan, Chebyshev, Minkowski.\nk: Minkowski Number | Blends between metric types (Minkowski only).\nk: Style | Metric combination: F1, F2, F2-F1, Border or Random Color.\nk: Border Width | Width of the border when the Border style is active.\nk: Roundess | Mid-level roundness for F1, F2 and F2-F1 styles.\nk: Invert | Inverts the result.\nuse: Mesh-baked cell masks, pebble relief on curved surfaces.\ncop: @posmap into @worleynoise3d: {Metric}, {Round Border}, outputs {o:dist1}, {o:dist2}, {o:border}, {o:center}, {o:id}.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## 3d-perlin-noise\nname: 3D Perlin Noise\nsrc: /noises/3d-perlin-noise/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: low\npurpose: Perlin noise evaluated in 3D from a Position Map, ensuring continuity across a mesh.\nk: Scale | Scale of the 3D noise.\nk: Size | Per-axis size (non-uniform values stretch or squash it).\nk: Offset | Position offset in X, Y and Z.\nk: Distortion Intensity | Strength of the warp applied to the noise.\nk: Baseline | Offset of the baseline luminance of the value distribution.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the noise.\nk: Absolute | Uses absolute values, which mirrors the distribution below 0.5.\nk: Enable Tiling | Repeats the pattern along X, Y and Z.\nuse: Seamless mesh-space breakup for dirt masks and large relief across UV seams.\ncop: @posmap into @fractalnoise3d with {Noise Type}=Perlin and {Fractal Type}=None; {Center} is the baseline, {Noise Contrast} the contrast, {Fold} (Post Processing) corresponds to Absolute, {Complement} to Invert.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## 3d-perlin-noise-fractal\nname: 3D Perlin Noise Fractal\nsrc: /noises/3d-perlin-noise-fractal/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: low\npurpose: Fractal (multi-octave) 3D Perlin noise from a Position Map.\nk: Min Level | Lowest fractal level.\nk: Max Level | Highest fractal level.\nk: Roughness | Balance between low and high levels (0 behaves differently from small values).\nk: Lacunarity | Spacing of the levels; higher gives denser noise.\nk: Global Opacity | Range of values around the baseline.\nk: Absolute | Uses absolute values.\nuse: Mesh-space base height variation.\ncop: @posmap into @fractalnoise3d: {Fractal Type}=Terrain, {Max Octaves}, {Lacunarity}, {Roughness}, {Octave Offset}.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## 3d-ridged-noise-fractal\nname: 3D Ridged Noise Fractal\nsrc: /noises/3d-ridged-noise-fractal/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: low\npurpose: Fractal ridged noise in 3D from a Position Map, producing sharp crest lines.\nk: Min Level | Lowest fractal level.\nk: Max Level | Highest fractal level.\nk: Roughness | Balance between levels.\nk: Lacunarity | Spacing of the levels.\nk: Distortion Intensity | Warp strength.\nuse: Mesh-space ridges for mountains, bark and rock veins across seams.\ncop: @posmap into @fractalnoise3d with {Fractal Type}=Sharp (ridged-style crest, UNVERIFIED) or Hybrid Terrain.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## 3d-simplex-noise\nname: 3D Simplex Noise\nsrc: /noises/3d-simplex-noise/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: low\npurpose: Faster and simpler cousin of 3D Perlin noise for use with a Position Map on the GPU engine.\nk: Scale | Global scale (0 to 64).\nk: Size | Per-axis non-uniform scaling (0 to 2).\nuse: Cheap mesh-space noise when performance matters.\ncop: @posmap into @fractalnoise3d with {Noise Type}=Simplex (available in the 3D node).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-concrete\nname: Grunge Concrete\nsrc: /noises/grunge-concrete/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: high\npurpose: Grunge map resembling the height of a concrete surface, with base noise, dirt specks and scratches.\nk: Balance | Shifts the grunge towards dark or light.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Base Noisiness | Strength of the base noise layer.\nk: Dirt Specks Opacity | Opacity of the dirt specks layer.\nk: Scratches Opacity | Opacity of the scratches layer.\nk: Large Variation Intensity | Strength of large-scale variation.\nk: Sharpen | Sharpening amount.\nuse: Concrete, plaster and cast-stone heights.\ncop: @grunge_layerednoise as the base ({Base Cells}, {Secondary Noise}) plus @grunge_moldspots for specks, merged with @blend; concrete pores via @bubblenoise. Match approximate and UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-damas\nname: Grunge Damas\nsrc: /noises/grunge-damas/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Grunge map resembling a Damascus steel pattern of wavy layered bands.\nk: Balance | Shifts the grunge towards dark or light.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Distortion | Strength of the band distortion.\nk: Divisions | Number of band divisions.\nk: Waves | Number of waves.\nk: Details | Amount of fine detail.\nk: Rotation Random | Random rotation variation.\nuse: Pattern-welded steel, wood grain layers and water-worn strata.\ncop: @ramp ({Type}=Horizontal, {Number of Cycles}) distorted by @distort using @fractalnoise, then @quantize or Post Processing {Fold} for the folded bands.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-galvanic-large\nname: Grunge Galvanic Large\nsrc: /noises/grunge-galvanic-large/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Grunge map resembling the large-spangle pattern of galvanised steel.\nk: Warp Intensity | Strength of the warp on the crystal pattern.\nk: Ridge Detail Opacity | Opacity of ridge details.\nk: Sharpen Intensity | Sharpening amount.\nk: Balance | Shifts the grunge towards dark or light.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nuse: Galvanised sheet metal heights and masks.\ncop: @grunge_galvanizedsteel ({Distort Size}, {Distort Angle}, {Distort Scale}, {Secondary Distort Size}, {Secondary Distort Roughness}).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-galvanic-small\nname: Grunge Galvanic Small\nsrc: /noises/grunge-galvanic-small/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Grunge map resembling densely galvanised steel with fine spangles.\nk: Crispness | Sharpness of the pattern edges.\nk: Dirt | Amount of dirt layered on top.\nk: Micro Distortion | Fine distortion of the pattern.\nk: Balance | Shifts the grunge towards dark or light.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nuse: Fine galvanised metal heights and masks.\ncop: @grunge_galvanizedsteel with a small {Element Size}.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-leaks\nname: Grunge Leaks\nsrc: /noises/grunge-leaks/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Grunge map resembling drips running across a greasy surface.\nk: Drip Length | Length of the drips.\nk: Shape Contrast | Contrast of the drip shapes.\nk: Drip Crispness | Edge sharpness of the drips.\nk: Sharpen Intensity | Sharpening amount.\nk: Balance | Shifts the grunge towards dark or light.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nuse: Vertical dirt streaks and grease runs as masks; very shallow relief.\ncop: @grunge_drips ({Density}, {Distortion}, {Primary Trailing}, {Secondary Trailing}).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-leaky-paint\nname: Grunge Leaky Paint\nsrc: /noises/grunge-leaky-paint/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Grunge map resembling paint dripping through leaks.\nk: Leak Intensity | Strength of the leaks.\nk: Leak Scale | Scale of the leaks.\nk: Leak Angle Random | Random variation of the leak angle.\nk: Leak Crispness | Edge sharpness.\nk: Balance | Shifts the grunge towards dark or light.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nuse: Paint runs, rust streaks below fasteners, as masks and shallow relief.\ncop: @grunge_leakingstreaks ({Primary Distortion}, {Primary Roughness}, {Secondary Mask}, {Tertiary Mask}).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-rough-dirty\nname: Grunge Rough Dirty\nsrc: /noises/grunge-rough-dirty/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Grunge map resembling a rough dirty surface with fine parallel scratches.\nk: Main Grunge Intensity | Strength of the main grunge layer.\nk: Invert Scratches | Inverts the scratch layer.\nk: Scratches Intensity | Strength of the scratches.\nk: Grain Intensity | Strength of the grain.\nk: Balance | Shifts the grunge towards dark or light.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nuse: Worn, dirty surfaces where grain and scratches both read.\ncop: @grunge_rustysurface for the main layer ({Primary Roughness}, {Secondary Roughness}, {Cracks Mask}) plus @streakblur on sparse noise for the parallel scratches; merge with @blend.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-rust-fine\nname: Grunge Rust Fine\nsrc: /noises/grunge-rust-fine/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Grunge map resembling a fine rust overlay.\nk: Base Grunge Contrast | Contrast of the base layer.\nk: Base Warp Intensity | Warp of the base layer.\nk: Streaks Intensity | Strength of rust streaks.\nk: Noise Intensity | Strength of the noise layer.\nk: Sharpen Intensity | Sharpening amount.\nuse: Rust mask or very fine corroded relief on metal.\ncop: @grunge_rust ({Coverage}, {Softness}, {Rust}, {Rust Size}).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-scratches-dirty\nname: Grunge Scratches Dirty\nsrc: /noises/grunge-scratches-dirty/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Grunge map resembling a finely scratched dirty surface.\nk: Base Grunge Intensity | Strength of the dirty base.\nk: Scratches Intensity | Strength of the scratches.\nk: Balance | Shifts the grunge towards dark or light.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nuse: Dirty worn metal and plastic, as a mask or subtle groove height.\ncop: @grunge_layerednoise for the dirt base blended with scratches from @shapescatter (thin line stamps with random {Angle}) or @streakblur on sparse noise.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-scratches-fine\nname: Grunge Scratches Fine\nsrc: /noises/grunge-scratches-fine/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Grunge map resembling finely scratched clean surface.\nk: Scratches Amount | Number of scratches.\nk: Sharpen Intensity | Sharpening amount.\nk: Scratch Value Bias | Bias on scratch brightness values.\nk: Balance | Shifts the grunge towards dark or light.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nuse: Fine hairline scratches for polished metal, glass or painted plastic heights.\ncop: @shapescatter with thin line stamps ({Stamps}, random {Angle}, {Stretch X}), or @streakblur of sparse @randommono dots with a small {Length}.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-scratches-rough\nname: Grunge Scratches Rough\nsrc: /noises/grunge-scratches-rough/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Grunge map resembling a roughly scratched dusty surface.\nk: Scratch Quantity | Amount of scratches.\nk: Scratch Tiling | Tiling of the scratch pattern.\nk: Scratch Blur | Blur of the scratches.\nk: Scratch Width | Width of the scratches.\nk: Scratch Length | Length of the scratches.\nk: Scratch Masking | Masks scratches with a noise.\nk: Scratch Dirtiness | Dirt within the scratches.\nk: Double Scratch | Doubled scratch lines.\nk: Dust Intensity | Strength of the dust layer.\nk: Dust Tiling | Tiling of the dust layer.\nuse: Heavily worn surfaces such as scuffed metal or road paint.\ncop: @shapescatter line stamps ({Scatter Seed}, {Angle}, {Stretch X}) plus @grunge_moldspots for dust; merge with @blend.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-shavings\nname: Grunge Shavings\nsrc: /noises/grunge-shavings/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: low\npurpose: Grunge map resembling shavings scattered on a surface.\nk: Scratch Spots Amount | Amount of shaving-like marks.\nk: Scratch Spots Tiling | Tiling of the marks.\nk: Dust Intensity | Strength of the dust.\nk: Sharpen Intensity | Sharpening amount.\nuse: Workshop floors, machined metal debris.\ncop: @shapescatter with short curved or line stamps, {Blend Method}=Maximum.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-splashes-dusty\nname: Grunge Splashes Dusty\nsrc: /noises/grunge-splashes-dusty/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: low\npurpose: Grunge map resembling liquid splashes on a dirty surface.\nk: Splashes Quantity | Number of splashes.\nk: Splashes Distortion | Distortion of splash shapes.\nk: Splash/Dirt Ratio | Balance between splash and dirt layers.\nk: Dirt Spread | How far the dirt spreads.\nuse: Splatter masks for paint, mud and blood-like stains.\ncop: @shapescatter with disc stamps then @distort using noise; or @grunge_moldspots; match approximate.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-spots-dirty\nname: Grunge Spots Dirty\nsrc: /noises/grunge-spots-dirty/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Grunge map resembling spots of dirt.\nk: Coverage | Amount of the image covered by spots.\nk: Scale | Scale of the spots.\nuse: Dirty-spot masks over walls and floors.\ncop: @grunge_moldspots ({Spread}, {Primary Size}, {Secondary Size}).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-spots\nname: Grunge Spots\nsrc: /noises/grunge-spots/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Grunge map resembling fine splattered spots.\nk: Details | Amount of fine detail.\nk: Coverage | Amount of coverage.\nk: Coverage Contrast | Contrast of the coverage.\nuse: Fine speckle masks and shallow pitting.\ncop: @grunge_moldspots with small sizes.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-map-001\nname: Grunge Map 001\nsrc: /noises/grunge-map-001/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Complex combined noise map, useful as a detailed procedural mask but performance-intensive.\nk: Balance | Shifts the map towards dark or light.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the map.\nk: Brush Pattern | Strength of the brush-like pattern in the mix.\nk: Invert | Inverts the result.\nuse: Generic dirt and wear mask. A common practice is to bake the node once to an image and reuse it.\ncop: No direct COP node. Use @grunge_layerednoise as the nearest procedural stand-in, or bake the Substance output to a bitmap and read it with @file. Exact reproduction is UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-map-002\nname: Grunge Map 002\nsrc: /noises/grunge-map-002/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Complex combined noise map (same controls as Grunge Map 001, different look).\nk: Balance | Shifts the map towards dark or light.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the map.\nk: Brush Pattern | Strength of the brush-like pattern.\nuse: Generic dirt and wear mask.\ncop: As Grunge Map 001 (@grunge_layerednoise or a baked bitmap through @file).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-map-003\nname: Grunge Map 003\nsrc: /noises/grunge-map-003/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Complex combined noise map (same controls as Grunge Map 001).\nk: Balance | Shifts the map towards dark or light.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the map.\nk: Brush Pattern | Strength of the brush-like pattern.\nuse: Generic dirt and wear mask.\ncop: As Grunge Map 001.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-map-004\nname: Grunge Map 004\nsrc: /noises/grunge-map-004/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Complex combined noise map (same controls as Grunge Map 001).\nk: Balance | Shifts the map towards dark or light.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the map.\nk: Brush Pattern | Strength of the brush-like pattern.\nuse: Generic dirt and wear mask.\ncop: As Grunge Map 001.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-map-005\nname: Grunge Map 005\nsrc: /noises/grunge-map-005/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Complex combined noise map with an extra Disorder control.\nk: Balance | Shifts the map towards dark or light.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the map.\nk: Disorder | Displaces the ingredients of the map.\nk: Brush Pattern | Strength of the brush-like pattern.\nuse: Generic dirt and wear mask with variation control.\ncop: As Grunge Map 001.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-map-006\nname: Grunge Map 006\nsrc: /noises/grunge-map-006/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Complex combined noise map (same controls as Grunge Map 001).\nk: Balance | Shifts the map towards dark or light.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the map.\nk: Brush Pattern | Strength of the brush-like pattern.\nuse: Generic dirt and wear mask.\ncop: As Grunge Map 001.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-map-007\nname: Grunge Map 007\nsrc: /noises/grunge-map-007/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Complex combined noise map (same controls as Grunge Map 001).\nk: Balance | Shifts the map towards dark or light.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the map.\nk: Brush Pattern | Strength of the brush-like pattern.\nuse: Generic dirt and wear mask.\ncop: As Grunge Map 001.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-map-008\nname: Grunge Map 008\nsrc: /noises/grunge-map-008/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Complex combined noise map (same controls as Grunge Map 001).\nk: Balance | Shifts the map towards dark or light.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the map.\nk: Brush Pattern | Strength of the brush-like pattern.\nuse: Generic dirt and wear mask.\ncop: As Grunge Map 001.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grunge-map-009\nname: Grunge Map 009\nsrc: /noises/grunge-map-009/\ncat: Texture generators > Noises\nrel: medium\npurpose: Complex combined