{"parentUuid":"c06b9137-6915-4865-a0c0-cb3c62f6e8a0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a9840a94295146d85","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0111nYTQR18zSdN6rmgrFqu9","type":"tool_result","content":"#type:     node\n#context:  cop\n#internal: tilepattern\n#icon:     COP/tilepattern\n\n= Tile Pattern =\n\n\"\"\"Generates rectangular tiles for texture patterns.\"\"\"\n\n== Overview ==\n\nThis node generates rectangular shapes to create various texture patterns.\n\nIt has various predefined pattern types that can be accessed from the __Pattern Type__ menu. Optionally, `Custom Pattern`\ngives controls to create more customized patterns.\n\n@parameters\n\n== Pattern ==\n\n=== Pattern ===\n\nPattern Size:\n    #id: tiledsize\n    Controls the size of the pattern that tiles must cover. Usually this should be the size of the image.\n\nClip to Size:\n    #id: cliptosize\n    When __Pattern Size__ is smaller than the image size, use this to control the tiles that have a centroid outside the given area.\n\nPattern Type:\n    #id: patterntype\n    Sets various pre-defined pattern types. Choose `Custom Pattern` to create a new pattern. Use the menu to the right side of this parameter\n    to control the amount of tiles in the selected pattern.\n\n    Stack Bond:\n        The tiles are laid directly on top of one another with all joints aligned\n\n    Header Bond:\n        The pattern is laid with the header course sitting halfway over the joints of the courses in the row below.\n\n    Stretcher Bond:\n        The pattern is laid with the stretcher course sitting halfway over the joints of the courses in the row below.\n\n    Flemish Bond:\n        Flemish bond is another traditional pattern where stretchers and headers are laid alternately in a single course.\n\n    American Bond:\n        American Bond also referred to as Common Bond is a variation of the running bond patterns with a course of full headers at regular intervals.\n\n    Monk Bond:\n       The monk bond is a variant of the Flemish bond and involves two stretchers between the headers in each course.\n       The headers are centered over the joint between the two stretchers in the course below.\n\n    English Bond:\n        A course of stretchers alternates with a course of headers. The stretcher course is each time started with a three-quarter brick.\n\n    Double English Bond:\n        The pattern is made up of two alternating courses between headers and stretchers.\n\n    Windmill:\n        Windmill Pattern requires a square tile enclosed by four rectangular tiles that are double the size of the square.\n        The repetition results in a grid-like look.\n\n    Cross Hatch:\n        In each tile lines are placed at an angle to one another.\n\n    Basketwave:\n        Groups of warp and weft threads are interfaced so that they form a simple criss-cross pattern.\n\n    Hopscotch:\n         Hopscotch is a modular tile pattern that is laid in a specific arrangement with two sizes of square tiles.\n\n    Herringbone N:1:\n        The herringbone pattern is an arrangement of rectangles used for floor tilings and road pavement, so named for a fancied resemblance to the bones of a fish such as a herring.\n        Use the parameter __N__ to change the block edge length ratios for this pattern.\n\n    Herringbone 3:2:\n        The herringbone pattern is an arrangement of rectangles used for floor tilings and road pavement, so named for a fancied resemblance to the bones of a fish such as a herring.\n        This is a less common variation where the block edge length ratio is 3:2.\n\n    French Pattern:\n        French Pattern or Versailles Pattern is a modular interlocking pattern that is reminiscent of a stone floor from the historic European palaces.\n\n    Custom Pattern:\n        Provides controls to create a custom pattern.\n\n        The overall pattern is generated by defining tiles for the first row, which is located at the bottom of the pattern. The defined tiles repeat horizontally\n        until they fill the row. You can also define multiple rows, and each row also repeats vertically until they fill the pattern.\n\n\nMode:\n    #id: patternmode\n    Controls the mode by which to define the number of tiles in the pattern.\n\n    Seamless:\n        Using the __Divisions__ parameter the generated pattern is always tileable. A pattern that can be repeated seamlessly along a surface, creating the illusion of a larger and more detailed material.\n\n    Tile Count:\n        In this mode, the size of the tiles are calculated based on the __Rows__ and __Columns__ parameters.\n\n    Tile Size:\n        In this mode, __Tile Width__ and __Tile Height__ provide direct control over the size of the tiles.\n\nDivisions:\n    #id: stackbond_div, headerbond_div, stretcherbond_div, flemishbond_div, americanbond_div, monkbond_div, monkbond_div, englishbond_div, denglishbond_div, windmill_div, crosshatch_div, basketwave_div, hopscotch_div, herringbonen1_div, herringbone32_div, frenchpattern_div\n    When __Seamless__ mode is selected, it controls the size of the tiles making up the pattern.\n\nRows:\n    #id: stackbond_rows, headerbond_rows, stretcherbond_rows, flemishbond_rows, americanbond_rows, monkbond_rows, englishbond_rows, denglishbond_rows, windmill_rows, crosshatch_rows, basketwave_rows, hopscotch_rows, frenchpattern_rows\n    When __Tile Count__ mode is selected, it controls the number of rows in the pattern.\n\nColumns:\n    #id: stackbond_cols, headerbond_cols, stretcherbond_cols, flemishbond_cols, americanbond_cols, monkbond_cols, englishbond_cols, denglishbond_cols, windmill_cols, crosshatch_cols, basketwave_cols, hopscotch_cols, frenchpattern_cols\n    When __Tile Count__ mode is selected, it controls the number of columns in the pattern.\n\nTile Width:\n    #id: stackbond_tilewidth, headerbond_tilewidth, stretcherbond_tilewidth, flemishbond_tilewidth, americanbond_tilewidth, monkbond_tilewidth, englishbond_tilewidth, denglishbond_tilewidth, windmill_tilewidth, crosshatch_tilewidth, basketwave_tilewidth, hopscotch_tilewidth, fren\n    When __Tile Size__ mode is selected, it controls the horizontal size of the tiles.\n\nTile Height:\n    #id: stackbond_tileheight, headerbond_tileheight, stretcherbond_tileheight, flemishbond_tileheight, americanbond_tileheight, monkbond_tileheight, englishbond_tileheight, denglishbond_tileheight, windmill_tileheight, crosshatch_tileheight, basketwave_tileheight, hopscotch_tile\n    When __Tile Size__ mode is selected, it controls the vertical size of the tiles.\n\nIris:\n    #id: windmill_iris\n    When __Windmill__ is set, this controls the ratio between the central square and the four surrounding tiles. Increase this value to make the central tile larger.\n\nRow Divisions:\n    #id: crosshatch_rowdiv\n    When __Cross Hatch__ is set, this controls the number of tile divisions where the tile is divided horizontally.\n\nColumn Divisions:\n    #id: crosshatch_coldiv\n    When __Cross Hatch__ is set, this controls the number of tile divisions where the tile is divided vertically.\n\nRow Thickness:\n    #id: basketwave_rowthickness\n    When __Basketwave__ is set, this controls the thickness of the tiles oriented horizontally.\n\nColumn Thickness:\n    #id: basketwave_colthickness\n    When __Basketwave__ is set, this controls the thickness of the tiles oriented vertically.\n\nDraw Square Bonds:\n    #id: basketwave_drawsquarebonds\n    When __Basketwave__ is set, this controls whenever to draw the square tiles between the waves.\n\nTile Count:\n    #id: herringbonen1_tilecount, herringbone32_tilecount\n    When __Herringbone N:1__ or __Herringbone 3:2__ and __Tile Count__ mode are selected, it controls the number of tiles in the pattern.\n\nTile Size:\n    #id: herringbonen1_tilesize, herringbone32_tilesize\n    When __Herringbone N:1__ or __Herringbone 3:2__ and __Tile Size__ mode are selected, it controls the size of the tiles.\n\nN:\n    #id: herringbonen1_ration\n    When __Herringbone N:1__ is set, this is the ratio that controls the thickness of the tile relative to the length. Increase this value to make the tiles thinner and elongated.\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#flippattern:\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#useexpr:\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#expr:\n\n\n=== Number of Rows ===\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#rowvisibility#:\n\n=== Row # ===\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#rowoffset#:\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#rowreflect#:\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#rowslideoffset#:\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#rowheight#:\n\n=== Number of Columns ===\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#colvisibility#_#:\n\n=== Column #.# ===\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#colwidth#_#:\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#colheight#_#:\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#coloffset#_#:\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#colrot#_#:\n\n=== Shape ===\n\nControls the shape placed over the tiles.\n\n:include /nodes/cop/sdfshape#shapeclass:\n\nStretch Shape:\n    #id: useaspectratio\n    Stretches the shape according to the tile ratio. Turn this off to not stretch the shape.\n\n:include /nodes/cop/sdfshape#basictype:\n\n:include /nodes/cop/sdfshape#markertype:\n\n:include /nodes/cop/sdfshape#compoundtype:\n\n=== Basic Shapes ===\n\n:include /nodes/cop/sdfshape#circle_radius:\n\n:include /nodes/cop/sdfshape#circle_arc:\n\n:include /nodes/cop/sdfshape#circle_thickness:\n\n:include /nodes/cop/sdfshape#circle_roundends:\n\n:include /nodes/cop/sdfshape#circle_quadratic:\n\n:include /nodes/cop/sdfshape#diamond_size:\n\n:include /nodes/cop/sdfshape#line_length:\n\n:include /nodes/cop/sdfshape#line_pt0:\n\n:include /nodes/cop/sdfshape#line_pt1:\n\n:include /nodes/cop/sdfshape#line_addthickness:\n\n:include /nodes/cop/sdfshape#line_sthickness:\n\n:include /nodes/cop/sdfshape#line_ethickness:\n\n:include /nodes/cop/sdfshape#line_bulge:\n\n:includ