{"parentUuid":"20011c5f-059f-47d8-9f1c-2939fa46e640","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a9840a94295146d85","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B3bxfpnZKzJJ1tDcSKDSRN","type":"tool_result","content":"    Radial:\n        Ramp is circular with points extending radially.\n    Concentric:\n        Ramp is circular with points at varying distances from\n        the center.\n\nGradient Ramp:\n    #id: gradientramp\n    #contentfrom: /nodes/cop/ramp#rampmono\n\n    Draws the shape as a gradient ramp.\n    \n    For more information about using ramps, see [Ramp parameters|/network/ramps].\n\n:include /nodes/cop/sdftomono#outlinewidth:\n\n=== Stamping ===\n\n:include /nodes/cop/stamppoint#filter:\n\n:include /nodes/cop/stamppoint#blend:\n\nRandomize Stamp Order:\n    #id: randstamporderseed\n    Randomly varies the point order by which the points are stamped into the image. Change the value if the current variation is undesirable.\n\n=== Value ===\n\nTile Value:\n    #id: value\n    Controls the value of the shape inside the tile.  Set __Uniform__ to __Set Varying__ on the right side of this parameter to randomize the value per tile.\n\nVariation:\n    #id: value_var\n    The maximum allowed variation for the tiles. The value of `0` means no variation from __Tile Value__.\n\nSeed:\n    #id: value_seed\n    Controls random selection for variation. Change the value of the __Seed__ if the current variation is undesirable.\n\nBackground Value:\n    #id: bgvalue\n    Controls the value outside of the shape.\n\n=== Position ===\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#rowoffset:\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#coloffset:\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#rowslideoffset:\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#rowslideoffset_var:\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#rowslideoffset_seed:\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#posjitter:\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#hposjitter:\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#vposjitter:\n\n:include /nodes/sop/planartiles#posjitterseed:\n\n=== Rotate ===\n\nRotate Pattern:\n    #id: grotate\n    Rotates the pattern based on the value in degrees.\n\nRotate Tile:\n    #id: rotate\n    Rotates each tile from its center in degrees.\n\nRotate Variation:\n    #id: rotate_var\n    Sets the maximum allowed variation in degrees. Rotated angles will be between `Rotate Tile - Rotate Variation` and `Rotate Tile + Rotate Variation`.\n\nSeed:\n    #id: rotate_seed\n    Controls random selection for variation. Change the value of the __Seed__ if the current variation is undesirable.\n\nCheckerboard Rotate:\n    #id: rotate_chb\n    Rotates the tiles that the rotation alternates between `0` and `90` degrees.\n\nOrient Tiles:\n    #id: orienttiles\n    Sets the orientation attribute for the tiles. This ensures that using __Horizontal Scale__ and __Vertical Scale__ always scale the right edge of the tiles.\n    Especially when the pattern consists of tiles that are both longer than wider and wider than longer.\n\n=== Size ===\n\nUniform Scale:\n    #id: scale\n    Sets the scale for the tiles. Set __Uniform__ to __Set Varying__ on the right side of this parameter to randomize the scale per tile.\n    The amount of scale depends on the size of each tile. If you need to dilate the tiles with equal amounts use __Inset__ instead.\n\nVariation:\n    #id: scale_var\n    Sets the maximum allowed variation. The value of `0` means that there is no variation from __Uniform Scale__.\n\nSeed:\n    #id: scale_seed, hscale_seed, vscale_seed, inset_seed\n    Controls random selection for variation. Change the value of the __Seed__ if the current variation is undesirable.\n\nHorizontal Scale:\n    #id: hscale\n    Sets the horizontal scale for the tiles. Set __Uniform__ to __Set Varying__ on the right side of this parameter to randomize the scale per tile.\n\nVariation:\n    #id: hscale_var\n    Sets the maximum allowed variation. The value of `0` means that there is no variation from __Horizontal Scale__.\n\nVertical Scale:\n    #id: vscale\n    Sets the vertical scale for the tiles. Set __Uniform__ to __Set Varying__ on the right side of this parameter to randomize the scale per tile.\n\nVariation:\n    #id: vscale_var\n    Sets the maximum allowed variation. The value of `0` means that there is no variation from __Vertical Scale__.\n\nInset:\n    #id: inset\n    Dilates the edges of the tiles regardless of the height or width of each tile. Set __Uniform__ to __Set Varying__ on the right side of this parameter to randomize the inset per tile.\n\nVariation:\n    #id: inset_var\n    Sets the maximum allowed variation. The value of `0` means that there is no variation from __Inset__.\n\n== Prune Tiles ==\n\n=== Tile Selection ===\n\nBy Tile Order:\n    #id: tileorder\n    This menu controls the order by which the tiles are removed. If you turned on __Row Offset__ or __Column Offset__ or if you use a custom pattern, the first tile might not be the tile at the bottom left position.\n\n    Default:\n        The ordering of the tiles is unchanged. As __Threshold__ increases more and more tiles are removed starting from the bottom left corner of the pattern.\n\n    Reverse:\n        The ordering of the tiles are reversed. As __Threshold__ increases more and more tiles are removed starting from the top right corner of the pattern.\n\n    Random:\n        The tiles are randomized.\n\n    Shift:\n        The ordering of the tiles is unchanged. However, this method provides a control to shift the tile order.\n\nThreshold:\n    #id: tilethreshold\n    Controls the number of tiles to be removed. This is a normalized value, `0` does not remove any tiles, while the value of `1` removes all tiles in the pattern.\n    Turn on __Negate Selection__ on the right side of this parameter to reverse the selection.\n\nNegate Selection:\n    #id: reversethresholdselection, reverseidselection, reverserowidselection, reversecolumnidselection, reversecheckerboard, negate\n    When turned on, instead of deleting anything selected, it will delete anything not selected.\n\nSeed:\n    #id: thresholdrandseed\n    When __Random__ tile order is selected, controls random selection for variation. Change the value of the __Seed__ if the current variation is undesirable.\n\nOffset:\n    #id: thresholdshiftoffset\n    When __Shift__ tile order is selected, offsets the tiles that are removed.\n\n\nEvery Nth Tile:\n    #id: idselection\n    When this is turned on, deletes every (number of the parameter) tile. Turn on __Negate Selection__ on the right side of this parameter to reverse the selection.\n\nEvery Nth Row:\n    #id: rowidselection\n    When this is turned on, deletes every (number of the parameter) row. Turn on __Negate Selection__ on the right side of this parameter to reverse the selection.\n\nEvery Nth Column:\n    #id: columnidselection\n    When this is turned on, deletes every (number of the parameter) column. Turn on __Negate Selection__ on the right side of this parameter to reverse the selection.\n\nCheckerboard:\n    #id: docheckerboard\n    The removal alternates across the pattern.\n\n== Split Tiles ==\n\n=== Split Tiles ===\n\nSplit Tiles:\n    #id: splittiles\n    When this is turned on, tiles can be split according to various rules.\n\nIterations:\n    #id: nsplititers\n    When this is turned on, tiles that already split have a chance to split again iteratively. This number controls the maximum number of times\n    a tile can be split.\n\nArea Threshold:\n    #id: areathreshold\n    When this is turned on, any tile that has an area smaller than this value will not be split. Use this parameter to limit splitting small tiles.\n\nSplit Treshold:\n    #id: splittreshold\n    Controls the number of tiles to be split. This is a normalized value, `0` does not split any tiles, while the value of `1` splits all tiles in the pattern.\n\nNumber of Splits:\n    #id: nsplits\n    When a tile is selected for split, this controls the number of splits for a tile. Set __Uniform__ to __Set Varying__ on the right side of this parameter to randomize the number of splits per tile.\n\nVariation:\n    #id: nsplits_var\n    Sets the maximum allowed variation. The value of `0` means that there is no variation from __Number of Splits__. While the value of `1` means that a tile can split `1` or __Number of Splits__`-1` times.\n\nSeed:\n    #id: nsplits_seed, splitjitter_seed, splittresholdseed\n    Controls random selection for variation. Change the value of the __Seed__ if the current variation is undesirable.\n\nJitter Scale:\n    #id: splitjitter\n    Controls the split position of the tiles. Set __Uniform__ to __Set Varying__ on the right side of this parameter to further randomize the number of splits per tile.\n\nVariation:\n    #id: splitjitter_var\n    Sets the maximum allowed variation. The value of `0` means that there is no variation from __Jitter Scale__.\n\nOrient Ratio:\n    #id: split_orientratio\n    Controls whenever the tiles should be split horizontally or vertically. The value of `0` means that all tiles are split horizontally, and the value of `1` means that all tiles are split 'vertically'.\n    The value of `0.5` will split tiles both horizontally and vertically in equal ratio.\n\n@inputs\n    :include /nodes/cop/_input_descriptions#size_ref/:\n\n    pointmask:\n        An optional mask amount for points.\n\n    stamp0:\n        An optional scaling amount for stamping.\n\n@outputs\n    tiles:\n        The tiled layer.\n\n    id:\n        An ID layer storing the ID values.\n\n    uv:\n        A UV layer storing the UV values.\n\n@related\n- [Planar Tiles|Node:sop/planartiles]\n- [SDF Shape|Node:cop/sdfshape]\n- [SDF To Mono|Node:cop/sdftomono]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"145ed4f0-a162-49f5-94ca-f48cc4d785af","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:31:43.095Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6bdaa90b-6960-41af-8737-4e268b09c548","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.cl