{"parentUuid":"9049c062-f742-45f1-8dd9-d1d6f0a71ab3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a9840a94295146d85","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MQB6f9fBewBCynKvXiVVbd","type":"tool_result","content":"#type: node\n#context: cop\n#internal: ramp\n#icon: COP/ramp\n\n= Ramp =\n\n\"\"\"Generates linear and radial ramps.\"\"\"\n\nThis node generates a variety of linear and radial ramps, for which you can set keyframes. You can use any number of points to define the ramp. The __Type__ parameter shapes the gradient, and you can use the other parameters to further configure that gradient \n\nThe Ramp Mono COP adds a ramp node that's default is a floating point ramp, where __Signature__ is set to `Mono`. The Ramp RGB COP adds a ramp node that's default is a color ramp, where __Signature__ is set to `RGB`. For example, use a Ramp Mono COP for masks \n\nSee [Ramp parameters|/network/ramps] for more information about how to use ramp parameters.\n\nTIP:\n    If you want to recolor a mono image, use the [Mono To RGB COP|Node:/cop/monotorgb].\n\n@parameters\n\nSignature:\n    #id: signature\n    \n    The layer type that the ramp generates.\n\n    See [Signatures|/copernicus/glossary#signatures] for more information.\n\nType:\n    #id: rampType\n\n    The type of ramp to generate.\n\n    Horizontal:\n        A linear type ramp with horizontal points.\n\n    Vertical:\n        A linear type ramp with vertical points.\n\n    Radial:\n        A circular ramp with points that radially extend as a line from the center (for example, like a sunbeam).\n\n    Concentric:\n        A circular ramp with points as circles at varying distances from the center (for example, like a ripple effect).\n\nNumber of Cycles:\n    #id: cycles\n\n    The number of cycles to repeat the ramp pattern.\n\nPhase:\n    #id: phase\n\n    The phase to offset the start of the ramp pattern. A value of `0` means the beginning of the ramp pattern is based on the first point.\n\nOutside Range:\n    #id: method\n\n    The behavior of the ramp beyond its start and end points, which the __Ramp__ parameter determines.\n\n    Clamp at End:\n        Clamp the ramp at the start and end points.\n\n    Repeat:\n        Repeat the ramp pattern from the start to the end points.\n        \n    Mirror:\n        Reflect the ramp pattern so it repeats backwards from the end to the start points.\n\nSize Method:\n    #id: sizemethod\n\n    The method used to define the size of the ramp.\n\n    Framed to Display:\n        Frame the ramp to the [display window|/copernicus/transition#data_display].\n    \n    Two Points:\n        Define the ramp with a pair of points.\n\nCenter:\n    #id: center\n\n    When __Type__ is set to `Radial` or `Concentric`, this is the center point of the ramp.\n\n    TIP:\n        Click [Icon:BUTTONS/layer_position_sample] and then click a location in the image to set the __Center__.\n\nRotation:\n    #id: rotation\n\n    When __Type__ is set to `Horizontal` or `Vertical`, this is the rotation (in degrees) of the linear ramp.\n\nStart Position:\n    #id: startpos\n\n    When __Type__ is set to `Horizontal` or `Vertical`, this is the origin of the linear ramp. When __Type__ is set to `Radial` or `Concentric`, this is the center point of the ramp.\n\nEnd Position:\n    #id: endpos\n\n    When __Type__ is set to `Horizontal` or `Vertical`, this is the end of the linear ramp. When __Type__ is set to `Radial`, this is where the crossover of the ramp occurs. When __Type__ is set to `Concentric`, this is the radius of the ramp.\n\nRamp:\n    #id: ramp, rampmono\n\n    An RGB or mono ramp. An RGB ramp varies color along the length of the ramp, creating a gradient. A mono ramp varies a single value, creating a curve.\n\n    See [Ramp parameters|/network/ramps] for more information.\n\nPoint No.:\n    The number of the selected point.\n\nPosition:\n    The position of the selected point in the ramp.\n\nColor:\n    The color of the selected point.\n    \n    See [Using a ramp parameter|/network/ramps#use_ramp] for more information about how to open the color ramp's color editor.\n\nValue:\n    The value of the selected point.\n\nInterpolation:\n    Sets the interpolation of the ramp on a point-by-point basis, which controls how Houdini fills in the values between the selected point and the next point. Instead of this method, it's recommended that you set the __Interpolation for all points__ (see [Ram\n\n@inputs\n    :include /nodes/cop/_input_descriptions#size_ref/:\n\n    pos:\n        An optional UV layer with a value that's used instead of the pixel's image coordinates for the ramp.\n\n    ramp:\n        An optional per-pixel ramp amount for the ramp that overrides the __Ramp__ parameter.\n\n@outputs\n    ramp:\n        The ramp output.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5f7ae046-2f2a-4974-979a-13188c94ea61","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:31:58.912Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"d0fdc8da-d686-4fcf-87a0-d1fb3cf347e3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":25,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9049c062-f742-45f1-8dd9-d1d6f0a71ab3","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953"