{"parentUuid":"203ae6d0-e430-41f6-9ae3-3c15d7032f5e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a9840a94295146d85","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvcb7gBqL5hDtbH3KGf5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015gkvFdKPiWmRHS7e9aXLQx","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-zenray--claude-Memory1/3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953/scratchpad/work/entries/02a_patterns.txt","content":"## tile-generator\nname: Tile Generator\nsrc: /patterns/tile-generator/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: The workhorse pattern node: repeats a chosen shape or up to six custom input patterns on an X by Y grid, with per-tile control of size, offset, rotation, value and masking. It is described as one of the most advanced nodes of the library.\nk: X Amount | Number of tile repetitions along X.\nk: Y Amount | Number of tile repetitions along Y.\nk: Pattern | The tile shape, one of the built-in height profiles or Image Input for custom patterns.\nk: Pattern Specific | Morphs the selected built-in shape (the effect depends on which pattern is chosen).\nk: Size Mode | How tile size is defined (Normal - Interstice, Normal - Size, Keep Ratio, Absolute, Pixel).\nk: Interstice X/Y | Gap between tiles, only in the interstice size mode.\nk: Scale | Global scale of every tile.\nk: Scale Random | Random scale variation per tile.\nk: Offset | Incremental shift applied row after row (or column after column), which gives running-bond brick layouts.\nk: Position Random | Random per-tile displacement, with separate X and Y control.\nk: Rotation@Rotation | Free rotation applied to all tiles.\nk: Rotation Random@Rotation | Random free rotation per tile.\nk: Luminance/Color Random | Per-tile luminance variation, i.e. random tile heights in a height graph.\nk: Checker Mask | Hides every other tile in a checkerboard fashion.\nk: Random Mask | Randomly hides a proportion of tiles.\nk: Blending Mode | How overlapping tiles combine (Add, Max, Add Sub).\nuse: Bricks, tiles, cobblestones, shingles, planks and any repeated module in a height graph; run its output into Flood Fill or Edge Detect to drive per-tile randomisation, bevels and wear.\ncop: @tilepattern. Set {Mode} to Tile Count and fill {Rows}/{Columns} (X Amount, Y Amount), or Seamless with {Divisions} for guaranteed tiling; {Pattern Type}=Stack Bond gives a square grid, Stretcher Bond gives the brick offset (also {Row Slide Offset} with a {Variation}); {Inset} is the interstice; {Draw As} chooses Filled, Distance (bevel-like falloff with {Fade Distance}), Gradient (with {Gradient Ramp} and {Rotate}) or Outline; {Tile Value} with {Variation} is the per-tile luminance; {Uniform Scale} plus {Variation} randomise size; {Rotate Tile} plus {Rotate Variation} randomise rotation; {Uniform Jitter} randomises position; masks are {Every Nth Tile}, {Checkerboard} and the {Threshold} prune group. Custom patterns go into the {i:stamp0} input; outputs are {o:tiles}, {o:id} (per-tile ID for random values) and {o:uv} (per-tile UV).\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## tile-generator-color\nname: Tile Generator Color\nsrc: /patterns/tile-generator/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Colour-input and colour-output version of Tile Generator; the page states it is rarely needed because the grayscale node covers almost every case.\nnote: The documentation page covers Tile Generator and its colour version together; the existence of a separate colour node is inferred from that page text.\nk: X Amount | Number of tile repetitions along X.\nk: Y Amount | Number of tile repetitions along Y.\nk: Blending Mode | How overlapping tiles combine.\nuse: Colour pattern bases (albedo of tiles); rarely used in pure height graphs.\ncop: Same @tilepattern chain; colour is obtained by feeding the {o:id} output into @randomrgb or by tinting {o:tiles} with @monotorgb; or use @shapescatter which has stamp {Stamp Color} controls.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## tile-sampler\nname: Tile Sampler\nsrc: /patterns/tile-sampler/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: Evolved Tile Generator whose scale, position, rotation, colour, mask and pattern choice can each be driven by an external map input, which makes it the tool for map-controlled scattering.\nk: X Amount | Number of tile repetitions along X.\nk: Y Amount | Number of tile repetitions along Y.\nk: Pattern | The tile shape or Pattern Input.\nk: Pattern Input Distribution | How multiple pattern inputs are picked (random, by number, or from a distribution map).\nk: Size Mode | General behaviour of the tile size (Normal, Keep Ratio, Absolute, Pixel).\nk: Scale Random | Random per-tile scale.\nk: Scale Map Multiplier | Strength of the Scale Map input.\nk: Position Random | Random per-tile position over both axes.\nk: Offset Type | Direction of the offset pattern (horizontal or vertical quincunx, or global).\nk: Displacement Map Intensity | Strength of the Displacement Map on the offset.\nk: Rotation Map Multiplier | Strength of the Rotation Map on per-tile rotation.\nk: Mask Map Threshold | Threshold below which the Mask Map hides tiles.\nk: Blending Mode | Blending of tiles on the background (Add/Sub or Max).\nk: Color Parametrization Mode | Source of per-tile colour (Color Input, Scale, Line Index, Row Index, Pattern Index).\nuse: Scattering rocks, pebbles or plates whose size follows a mask, orienting tiles along a vector map, and placing shapes only where a mask allows.\ncop: @shapescatter (SideFX-confirmed): {Stamps X}/{Stamps Y} set the grid, {Jitter} randomises position, {Angle}, {Stretch Mode}, {Scale Mode} give per-stamp variance, and the per-pixel inputs replace Tile Sampler's map slots: {i:scale} (Scale Map), {i:jitter} and {i:direction} (Displacement and Vector maps), {i:angle} (Rotation Map), {i:color} (Color Map), {i:density} or {i:select} (Mask and distribution maps), {i:stamps} (pattern inputs); {Blend Method}=Maximum corresponds to the Max blend; outputs {o:result}, {o:id}, {o:uv}.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## tile-sampler-color\nname: Tile Sampler Color\nsrc: /patterns/tile-sampler/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Colour version of Tile Sampler with alpha blending of coloured tiles and colour map parametrisation.\nnote: The documentation page covers Tile Sampler and its colour version together; the colour node is identified through the colour-only parameter variants in the page tables.\nk: Blending Mode | Blending of tiles (Add/Sub or Alpha Blend in the colour version).\nk: Color Parametrization Mode | Source of per-tile colour, including pattern centre positions in the colour version.\nuse: Colour variation of scattered stones, leaves or tiles; rarely needed for heights.\ncop: @shapescatter with {Stamp Color} (Uniform, Variance, Random from Ramp) and the {i:color} input.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## tile-random\nname: Tile Random\nsrc: /patterns/tile-random/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: Tile Generator variant that randomly splits tiles into smaller ones, giving irregular paving with chaotic tile shapes.\nk: X Amount | Number of base tiles along X.\nk: Y Amount | Number of base tiles along Y.\nk: Mode@Split | Rule for splitting tiles (none, auto, auto horizontal, auto vertical, random h+v).\nk: Threshold@Split | Size threshold above which a tile is split.\nk: Multiplier | How many splits are made; higher splits more.\nk: Amount@Interstice | Gap size between tiles.\nk: Scale Random | Random scale per tile.\nk: Rotation Random@Shape | Random rotation per tile.\nk: Random@Position | Random free position of tiles on X and Y.\nk: Color Random | Random tile luminance.\nuse: Flagstones, crazy paving, irregular tiling and broken stone slabs.\ncop: @tilepattern with {Split Tiles} on: {Iterations}, {Area Threshold}, {Split Treshold} (fraction of tiles split), {Number of Splits}, {Jitter Scale} for the split position and {Orient Ratio} for horizontal versus vertical splits; {Inset} for the interstice and {Tile Value} with {Variation} for random heights; {Uniform Jitter} for position randomness.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## tile-random-color\nname: Tile Random Color\nsrc: /patterns/tile-random/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Colour version of Tile Random with alpha-blend and colour parametrisation options.\nnote: The documentation page covers Tile Random and its colour version together.\nk: Color Parametrisation | Makes colour variation depend on area, size X or size Y.\nk: Blending Mode | Add/Sub, Max or Alpha Blend in the colour version.\nuse: Coloured irregular paving; rarely needed for heights.\ncop: Same @tilepattern chain with colours from @randomrgb driven by the {o:id} output.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## tile-random-2\nname: Tile Random 2\nsrc: /patterns/tile-random-2/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: Generates adjacent tiles of random sizes and aspect ratios, optionally slanted, rounded and bevelled, filling the whole canvas without gaps beyond the interstice.\nk: Amount X | Number of cells along X.\nk: Amount Y | Number of cells along Y.\nk: Random Size Multiplier | Intensity of random cell sizing.\nk: Interstice Thickness | Uniform gap between shapes.\nk: Round Corners Radius | Radius of rounded corners.\nk: Random Slant Multiplier | Intensity of random slanting of the cell sides.\nk: Bevel Distance Mode | How the bevel distance is determined.\nk: Bevel Distance Multiplier | Global bevel distance.\nk: Bevel Rounded Curve | Rounding of the bevel angle.\nk: Scale Multiplier | Shape size as a proportion of its cell.\nk: Mask Random Start | Start of the random masking range.\nk: Mask Random End | End of the random masking range.\nuse: Irregular stone walls, cobbles with varied sizes, slate and rubble relief with natural gaps.\ncop: No single node. @tilepattern with {Split Tiles} and {Jitter Scale} gives variable rectangles; slanted cells come from @cellularnoise with {Metric}=Manhattan or Chebyshev; rounded and bevelled edges from {o:border} (SDF distance) of @cellularnoise with {Gap}, {Bevel} and {Bevel Ramp}, or from @sdfadjust on an SDF of the tiles.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## splatter\nname: Splatter\nsrc: /patterns/splatter/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: Simple random placement of an input image over the canvas with many geometric placement controls; default settings look regular until Disorder parameters are raised.\nk: Pattern Size Width | Number of patterns along X.\nk: Pattern Size Height | Number of patterns along Y.\nk: Rotation | Rotation applied to every pattern.\nk: Rotation Variation | Random rotation of each shape.\nk: Zoom | Scales up the result (breaks tiling).\nk: Gain | Blending gain of each pattern.\nk: Disorder | Randomly shifts the shapes.\nk: Grid Number | Jumps between grid sizes while preserving tiling.\nk: Size Variation | Random scaling per shape.\nk: Luminance Variation | Random luminance per shape (grayscale version).\nuse: Quick scattering of pebbles, leaves, studs or dents without heavy tuning.\ncop: @shapescatter (SideFX lists the Splatter nodes under Scatter Shapes and Scatter on Curves): {Stamps X}/{Stamps Y}, {Jitter}, {Angle} with {Angle Variance}, {Scale Variance}, and stamps via {i:stamps}; {Blend Method}=Maximum or Add.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## splatter-color\nname: Splatter Color\nsrc: /patterns/splatter/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Colour version of Splatter with colour variation instead of luminance variation.\nnote: The documentation page covers Splatter and its colour version together.\nk: Color Variation | Random colour variation (colour version only).\nuse: Coloured scatter such as leaf litter; rarely needed for heights.\ncop: @shapescatter with {Stamp Color} set to Variance and {Hue}, {Saturation}, {Value} ranges.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## splatter-circular\nname: Splatter Circular\nsrc: /patterns/splatter-circular/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Ring-based pattern generator that places shapes or input images around one or several rings (or spirals), like Tile Generator but with circular placement.\nk: Pattern Amount | Number of tiles per ring.\nk: Ring Amount | Number of rings filled.\nk: Pattern | Tile shape or Image Input.\nk: Radius | Radius at which patterns are placed.\nk: Spiral Factor | Turns rings into spirals.\nk: Spread | Number of turns each ring covers.\nk: Center Orientation | Rotates each pattern to face the ring centre.\nk: Size Random | Random size per pattern.\nk: Scale by Ring Number | Makes scale depend on the ring index.\nk: Blending Mode | Blending of overlapping patterns (Add, Max, Add Sub).\nuse: Rosettes, fan patterns, drains, rivet rings, concentric ripples and radial studs.\ncop: @curvescatter along circle curves (from @curve3d or SOP geometry via @sopimport) with {Distribution}=By Count and {Angles Relative to Curve Direction}; or @copyxform with {Total Number}, {Rotate} and {Pivot Translate} to repeat a stamp around a pivot. Equivalence is partial; the SideFX page lists Splatter nodes under Scatter Shapes and Scatter on Curves.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## splatter-circular-color\nname: Splatter Circular Color\nsrc: /patterns/splatter-circular/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Colour-input version of Splatter Circular.\nnote: The documentation page covers Splatter Circular and its colour input variant together.\nk: Pattern Amount | Number of tiles per ring.\nuse: Coloured rosette patterns; rarely needed for heights.\ncop: Same as Splatter Circular with {Stamp Color} controls.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## shape\nname: Shape\nsrc: /patterns/shape/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: Generates precise, high-precision procedural shapes with built-in height profiles; the building block of most procedural height maps when combined with transform nodes.\nk: Pattern | Built-in shape or profile (Square, Disc, Paraboloid, Bell, Gaussian, Thorn, Pyramid, Brick, Gradation, Waves, Half Bell, Ridged Bell, Crescent, Capsule, Cone, Hemisphere).\nk: Pattern Specific | Morphs the selected pattern (effect depends on the pattern).\nk: Scale | Scales the entire shape.\nk: Size | Non-uniform scaling along X or Y.\nk: Angle | Rotation of the shape.\nk: Rotation 45° | Rotates by exactly 45 degrees.\nk: Tiling | Number of times the shape tiles.\nk: Non Square Tiling | Tiles the shape without squashing when Non Square Expansion is on.\nuse: Single stones, bumps, domes, ridges and profile masks that later feed Tile Sampler, Splatter or Flood Fill based chains.\ncop: @sdfshape wired into @sdftomono (SideFX-confirmed). Pick {Shape Class}/{Basic Shapes} (Circle, Rectangle, Regular Polygon, Star and others), then turn the SDF into the profile with {Remap Ramp} and {Iso Range} in @sdftomono; Paraboloid or Bell profiles are ramps over the distance, Hemisphere is a sqrt-shaped ramp (UNVERIFIED).\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## star\nname: Star\nsrc: /patterns/star/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Generates a five-pointed star.\nk: Scale | Uniform scale of the star.\nuse: Decorative stamps and test shapes.\ncop: @sdfshape with {Shape Class}=Basic Shapes and a Star type ({Number of Sides}=5, {Angle Factor}) into @sdftomono.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## starburst\nname: Starburst\nsrc: /patterns/starburst/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Generates a radial starburst with an adjustable number of rays, randomness and softness.\nk: Branches | Number of rays.\nk: Blur Amount | Softness of the result.\nk: Randomness | Random rotation of the rays around the centre.\nk: Size Min | Minimum ray size for variation.\nk: Size Max | Maximum ray size or global scale.\nk: Size Variation | Random scaling per ray.\nk: Tiling | Number of times the pattern tiles.\nuse: Impact cracks, splash patterns, radial scratches and star-shaped dents.\ncop: @ramp with {Type}=Radial (rays) and {Number of Cycles} equal to the branch count, thresholded with @remap and softened by @blur; or @uvtopolar on stripes. Ray randomness would need @distort driven by noise.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## stripes\nname: Stripes\nsrc: /patterns/stripes/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Tiling, angled stripe pattern that automatically adjusts so it stays seamless.\nk: Stripes | Number of stripes (the result is shifted to keep tiling).\nk: Width | Stripe width.\nk: Softness | Softness of the stripe edges.\nk: Shift | Tilts the stripes while keeping continuity.\nk: Align | Pivot of the shift (Edges or Center).\nuse: Grooves, corrugated panels, planks, ribbed surfaces; combine with Warp or noise for wavy grain.\ncop: @ramp ({Type}=Horizontal, {Number of Cycles}=stripe count, {Outside Range}=Repeat, {Rotation} for the tilt) followed by @remap with {Operation}=Threshold and {Width} for softness; or @tilepattern with a single row/column.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## checker-1\nname: Checker 1\nsrc: /patterns/checker-1/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Very simple checker pattern, handy for tests thanks to its obvious tiling and contrast.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nk: Rotate 45 Degrees | Rotates the pattern by 45 degrees.\nuse: Test pattern, tile checks, alternating panel heights.\ncop: @checkerboard ({Rows}, {Columns}, {Even Color}, {Odd Color}, {Offset}); rotate by 45 degrees with @xform2d.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## brick-1\nname: Brick 1\nsrc: /patterns/brick-1/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Simple brick pattern with adjustable smoothness and gap; see Brick Generator or Tile Generator for more options.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nk: Edge Smoothness | Blend between harsh and smooth edges.\nk: Interstice Width | Gap size between bricks.\nuse: Fast brick wall base for heights and masks.\ncop: @tilepattern with {Pattern Type}=Stretcher Bond, {Inset} for the interstice and {Draw As}=Distance with {Fade Distance} for edge smoothness.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## brick-2\nname: Brick 2\nsrc: /patterns/brick-2/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Second simple brick pattern with the same controls as Brick 1.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nk: Edge Smoothness | Blend between harsh and smooth edges.\nk: Interstice Width | Gap size between bricks.\nuse: Fast brick wall base for heights and masks.\ncop: As Brick 1 with another {Pattern Type} (for example Flemish Bond) or different row proportions.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## brick-generator\nname: Brick Generator\nsrc: /patterns/brick-generator/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: Advanced generator for man-made brick patterns with bevel, gap, row offset, per-brick height and slope controls.\nk: Bricks | Number of bricks along both axes.\nk: Bevel | Bevel profile of the bricks (two directions).\nk: Keep Ratio | Ties the bevel profile to the brick size.\nk: Gap | Gap between bricks (bevel adds to it).\nk: Middle Size | Size of every other column or row (running offset).\nk: Height | Height profile modifier, includes luminance variation between bricks.\nk: Slope | Tilts individual bricks as if they lie at an angle.\nk: Offset | Row-wise offset of the bricks.\nuse: Brick walls with per-brick height scatter and chipped feel; the Height and Slope controls replace manual Tile Generator setups.\ncop: @tilepattern with {Pattern Type}=Stretcher Bond or Custom Pattern, {Row Slide Offset} for Offset, {Inset} for Gap, {Draw As}=Distance with {Fade Distance} for Bevel, {Tile Value} with {Variation} for brick height variance, and the {o:uv} output (per-tile UV) combined with a random ID to tilt bricks (Slope) through @wrangle (UNVERIFIED).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## arc-pavement\nname: Arc Pavement\nsrc: /patterns/arc-pavement/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Generates a Parisian arc pavement pattern, a layout that cannot be done with Tile Generator or Tile Sampler.\nk: Scale | Global scale or tiling.\nk: Pattern Amount | Number of bricks in each arc.\nk: Pattern Amount Random | Randomises bricks per arc.\nk: Arcs Amount | Number of arcs stacked vertically (changes brick height).\nk: Pattern | Brick shape or input image.\nk: Pattern Height Decrease | Squashes brick height at arc ends.\nk: Color Random | Random tile colour.\nuse: Cobblestone streets, fan-pattern pavers and fish-scale paving.\ncop: No direct node. Nearest chain: @tilepattern with {Shape Class}=Compound Shapes (Fishscale) on a Stretcher Bond layout, or bricks scattered along arc curves with @curvescatter ({Distribution}=By Count). UNVERIFIED approximation.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## alveolus\nname: Alveolus\nsrc: /patterns/alveolus/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Soft-sphere pattern that can alternatively produce hexagon tiles.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nk: Gradient Filled Cells | Switches to sharp-edged hexagon tiles.\nk: Interstice Width | Gap size when the sharp-edge option is off.\nuse: Honeycomb relief, hex tiles, pebble-like bumps and bubble wrap.\ncop: @cellularnoise with {Lattice Type}=Hexagonal, {Jitter}=0 (perfect lattice), {Gap} for the interstice, {Bevel} and {Smooth Edge} for the soft-sphere profile; the {o:border} output gives a hex-wall mask.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mesh-1\nname: Mesh 1\nsrc: /patterns/mesh-1/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Simple mesh (grid) pattern with thin blocks.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nk: Rotate 45 Degrees | Rotates the result 45 degrees.\nuse: Grates, wire mesh, tiling detail for height and detail maps.\ncop: @tilepattern ({Pattern Type}=Stack Bond with {Inset}) or a pair of @ramp stripes combined with @blend; rotate with {Rotate Pattern}.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mesh-2\nname: Mesh 2\nsrc: /patterns/mesh-2/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Simple mesh pattern with fat blocks.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nk: Rotate 45 Degrees | Rotates the result.\nuse: Grates and coarse mesh detail.\ncop: As Mesh 1 with a smaller {Inset} so blocks look fat.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## weave-1\nname: Weave 1\nsrc: /patterns/weave-1/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Simple woven pattern.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nk: Rotate 45 Degrees | Rotates the pattern.\nuse: Basket weave, cloth and rattan relief.\ncop: @weave ({Rows}, {Columns}, {Weave Multiplier}, {Fiber Scale}, {Fiber Strength}, {Edge Gradient}, {Overlap Gradient}); outputs {o:weave}, {o:uv}, {o:id}.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## weave-2\nname: Weave 2\nsrc: /patterns/weave-2/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Simple weave with randomisation controls; at maximum disorder it behaves like a noise.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nk: Disorder | Shuffles the stitches of the weave.\nuse: Irregular fabric or wicker relief.\ncop: @weave plus {Every Nth Column} and {Every Nth Tile} for irregular skips, or a random merge with @fractalnoise through @blend.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## weave-generator\nname: Weave Generator\nsrc: /patterns/weave-generator/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Weave pattern node with a few controls, producing patterns not reachable with the predefined weaves.\nk: Tile X | Number of blocks along X.\nk: Tile Y | Number of blocks along Y.\nk: Shape | Height profile curve of the stitch.\nk: Weave | Number of stitches per block.\nk: Gap | Gap between stitches along X and Y.\nuse: Cloth, wicker, carbon fibre or basket relief.\ncop: @weave: {Rows} and {Columns} for Tile Y and Tile X, {Weave Multiplier} for stitches per block, {Fiber Scale} and {Fiber Strength} for the stitch profile, {Edge Gradient} for the shape.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## fibers-1\nname: Fibers 1\nsrc: /patterns/fibers-1/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Simple fiber-like pattern suited to rope, mesh or cloth heights and details.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nuse: Rope, cord, thread and mesh relief.\ncop: @weave with strong {Fiber Strength}, or @knit for yarn-like loops.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## fibers-2\nname: Fibers 2\nsrc: /patterns/fibers-2/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Simple cloth-like pattern with larger structure than Fibers 1.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nuse: Coarse cloth, burlap, mesh and organic detail.\ncop: @weave with fewer {Rows}/{Columns}; @knit for knitted cloth.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## gaussian-1\nname: Gaussian 1\nsrc: /patterns/gaussian-1/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Simple tiled gaussian blob pattern.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nuse: Soft round bumps, dents or stipple pattern.\ncop: @tilepattern ({Pattern Type}=Stack Bond, {Draw As}=Distance) followed by @remap with a bell-shaped {Ramp}; or one blob from @sdfshape and @sdftomono repeated with @shapescatter.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## gaussian-2\nname: Gaussian 2\nsrc: /patterns/gaussian-2/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Second tiled gaussian blob pattern.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nuse: Soft round bumps and dents.\ncop: As Gaussian 1 with a different blob width via {Fade Distance} and the ramp shape.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## gradient-linear-1\nname: Gradient Linear 1\nsrc: /patterns/gradient-linear-1/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: Perfectly smooth black to white linear gradient, one of the most used building blocks.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions (sawtooth).\nk: Rotation | Direction of the gradient in 90 degree steps.\nuse: Mask ramps, height slopes, input to Histogram Scan or Warp to build ridges and terraces.\ncop: @ramp ({Type}=Horizontal or Vertical, {Number of Cycles} for Tiling, {Outside Range}=Repeat, {Rotation} for the direction); for the default left to right black to white keep the default two-point mono {Ramp}.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## gradient-linear-2\nname: Gradient Linear 2\nsrc: /patterns/gradient-linear-2/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: Smooth double-sided black to white to black gradient with a rounded, pipe-like profile.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nk: Rotation | Switches the direction between left-right and top-bottom.\nuse: Cylindrical ridges, pipes, grooves and rounded ribs in height maps.\ncop: @ramp with {Outside Range}=Mirror and a smooth (spline) {Ramp} peaking at the centre; or @ramp followed by @function (sin) to create the pipe profile (UNVERIFIED).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## gradient-linear-3\nname: Gradient Linear 3\nsrc: /patterns/gradient-linear-3/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: Advanced linear gradient with a sharp, straight slope and a movable peak.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nk: Position | Where the midpoint or peak lies.\nk: Rotation | Direction of the gradient.\nuse: Roofs, wedges, V-grooves and asymmetric ramps.\ncop: @ramp with a three-point mono {Ramp} (0 at the left, 1 at the {Position} peak, 0 at the right) and linear interpolation.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## gradient-axial\nname: Gradient Axial\nsrc: /patterns/gradient-axial/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Black to white gradient between two custom points, allowing linear gradients at any angle (does not always tile).\nk: Point 1 | Start point (black).\nk: Point 2 | End point (white).\nuse: Directional fades, lighting-like falloff masks and slanted slopes.\ncop: @ramp with {Size Method}=Two Points and {Start Position}/{End Position}.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## gradient-axial-reflected\nname: Gradient Axial Reflected\nsrc: /patterns/gradient-axial-reflected/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Like Gradient Axial but starts and ends black and peaks white in the middle of the transition.\nk: Point 1 | First point (black).\nk: Point 2 | Second point; the transition peaks halfway.\nuse: Symmetric ridges at arbitrary angles.\ncop: @ramp with {Size Method}=Two Points and a three-point mono {Ramp} (0, 1, 0) or {Outside Range}=Mirror.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## gradient-circular\nname: Gradient Circular\nsrc: /patterns/gradient-circular/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Angular sweep gradient revolving around the first point, starting and ending at the second point (never tiles).\nk: Point 1 | Centre of the revolution.\nk: Point 2 | Point where the gradient starts and ends.\nuse: Radial dial sweeps and swirl masks.\ncop: @ramp with {Type}=Radial (rays extending from the centre like a sunbeam) and {Center} at Point 1; {Phase} sets the start direction.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## gradient-radial\nname: Gradient Radial\nsrc: /patterns/gradient-radial/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Distance-based radial gradient from a centre point (white) to a radius point (black), with cone or hemisphere profile.\nk: Shape | Transition profile, Cone (linear) or Hemisphere (rounded).\nk: Point 1 | Centre point (white).\nk: Point 2 | Radius point (black).\nuse: Domes, craters, vignette masks and round bumps in height maps.\ncop: @ramp with {Type}=Concentric, {Center} and {End Position} as the radius; the Hemisphere profile needs a rounded {Ramp} (or @function with sqrt, UNVERIFIED).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## 3d-linear-gradient\nname: 3D Linear Gradient\nsrc: /patterns/3d-linear-gradient/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Volumetric black to white gradient between two points in 3D, evaluated from a Position Map (GPU engine only).\nk: Points Position Mode | Whether the gradient points are given in UV space or in world space.\nk: Point 1 | Start point.\nk: Point 2 | End point.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nuse: Mesh-space height fades such as bottom to top dirt on a baked mesh.\ncop: In UV mode: @ramp using its {i:pos} input fed by a UV layer. In world mode: @wrangle computing the projection of the position layer onto the Point 1 to Point 2 axis, then @remap with {Compute Range}. UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## 3d-volume-mask\nname: 3D Volume Mask\nsrc: /patterns/3d-volume-mask/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Renders a primitive volume (cube, cylinder or sphere) as a mask from a Position map input.\nk: Shape | Cube, Cylinder or Sphere.\nk: Scale | Uniform scale of the primitive.\nk: Size | Size per axis.\nk: Position Input | Whether position is given in UV or world space.\nk: Rotation | Rotation of the primitive in world space.\nk: Feather Width | Width of the fading gradient from the surface inwards.\nuse: Localised dirt, wear or moss masks on a baked mesh.\ncop: No direct node. @wrangle evaluating a box, sphere or cylinder signed distance on the position layer, then @remap to apply the feather; UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## cube-3d\nname: Cube 3D\nsrc: /patterns/cube-3d/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Renders a grayscale 3D cube with shading that doubles as screen depth; very crisp edges at high bit depth.\nk: Orientation Offset | X and Y rotation of the cube.\nk: Size | Non-uniform scaling of the cube.\nk: Scale | Uniform scaling.\nuse: Depth-based 3D test shapes, cut-out of rotated blocks for splatter patterns.\ncop: A cube from SOPs via @sopimport rasterised by @rasterizegeo with Quick Setup Add Depth from Eye; UNVERIFIED chain.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## cube-3d-gbuffers\nname: Cube 3D GBuffers\nsrc: /patterns/cube-3d-gbuffers/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Advanced Cube 3D that also outputs position and normal maps in addition to the height-like depth.\nk: Orientation Offset | X and Y rotation of the cube.\nk: Size | Non-uniform scaling of the cube.\nk: Scale | Uniform scaling.\nuse: Test input for 3D position-based noises and for previewing mesh-space nodes.\ncop: @sopimport (a box) into @rasterizegeo with Quick Setups Add Position, Add Normal and Add Depth from Eye; the position output feeds @fractalnoise3d or @worleynoise3d.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## height-extrude\nname: Height Extrude\nsrc: /patterns/height-extrude/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Renders 3D z-depth from an input grayscale height map with an orbitable camera, useful to build rotated shapes for splatter nodes.\nk: Camera Angle | Euler angles of the camera, in half-turns.\nk: Camera Scale | Global scale of the output.\nk: Height Scale | Global factor on the input height.\nk: Vertical Offset | Moves the output up or down.\nk: Ground | Shows a ground plane or a black background.\nk: Normal Intensity | Strength of the normal map output.\nuse: Make a stone or rock height appear rotated in 3D before scattering it.\ncop: @heightfield_xform (Transform 3D of a height layer) for rotation and scale, or @monotoheightfield then @heightfield_visualize for inspection; @heighttonormal for the normal output.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## shape-extrude\nname: Shape Extrude\nsrc: /patterns/shape-extrude/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Renders a binary 2D shape as a 3D-rotated extruded volume with bevels and optional lathe-style profile gradients.\nk: Extrude Height | Amount of upward extrusion from the centre.\nk: Extrude Depth | Amount of downward extrusion.\nk: Extrude Shape | Built-in cube, cylinder or custom input.\nk: Profile Type | Straight, vertical gradient or mask profile.\nk: Bevel Height | How far the bevel reaches along the extrusion axis.\nk: Bevel Intensity | How much the bevel retracts the outline.\nk: Bevel Curve | Convex or concave bevel curve.\nk: Output Range | Output range [0, 1] or [-1, 1].\nuse: Hard-surface blocks, bolts, buttons and tiles with bevels for splatter patterns.\ncop: @planarinflate (inflates a 2D SDF into a height layer, i.e. extrusion with a rounded profile) after @monotosdf or @sdfshape; 3D rotation via @heightfield_xform. UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## shape-mapper\nname: Shape Mapper\nsrc: /patterns/shape-mapper/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Projects an input image along a circle or polygon outline so it fits an exact number of times with no gaps.\nk: Shape | Circle or polygon.\nk: Pattern amount | Number of repetitions around the shape.\nk: Segments | Number of polygon segments.\nk: Radius | Multiplier of the shape radius.\nk: Width | Multiplier of the pattern width along the shape.\nk: Rotation | Rotation of the shape in turns.\nk: Flip one on two | Flips every other repetition vertically.\nuse: Rings of bolts, gears, circular trims, polygonal borders.\ncop: @uvshape (UV coordinates for common 2D shapes) feeding @sample (UV Sample) to read the input pattern along the outline; @uvtopolar for the circular case.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## polygon-1\nname: Polygon 1\nsrc: /patterns/polygon-1/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Polygon generator with many options such as explode, triangle size and gradient slices.\nk: Sides | Number of sides.\nk: Explode | Moves polygon slices apart.\nk: Gradient | Makes slices gradients instead of solid.\nk: Scale | Scales the shape.\nk: Rotation | Rotates the shape.\nuse: Faceted stones, gems, and tiled polygon relief.\ncop: @sdfshape with a Regular Polygon ({Number of Sides}, {Radius}) into @sdftomono; exploded slices need @tilepattern or a wedge made by @ramp with {Type}=Radial (UNVERIFIED).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## polygon-2\nname: Polygon 2\nsrc: /patterns/polygon-2/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Simpler polygon generator with a smooth gradient profile.\nk: Sides | Number of sides.\nk: Curve | Gradient profile curve.\nk: Gradient | Gradient contrast.\nk: Invert Gradient | Inverts gradient direction.\nuse: Smooth faceted domes and pyramids.\ncop: @sdfshape (Regular Polygon) into @sdftomono with a {Remap Ramp} for the gradient curve.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## scratches-generator\nname: Scratches Generator\nsrc: /patterns/scratches-generator/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: Places random scratch splines with controls for direction, spread, distortion, width and fading.\nk: Spline Number | Number of scratches.\nk: Max Segments Per Spline | Subdivisions along each scratch (smoother curves).\nk: Spline Rotation | Uniform rotation of all splines.\nk: Spline Rotation Random | Random rotation per spline.\nk: Spline Scale | Uniform scale of the splines.\nk: Spline Distortion | Uniform distortion of the splines.\nk: Spline Width | Width of all splines.\nk: Spline Position Random | Random placement of each spline.\nk: Luminance Random (Grayscale version only) | Random brightness per scratch.\nk: Fade Mode | Fade at the start, end or both.\nuse: Scratched metal, wear on coatings; subtract from a height as fine grooves.\ncop: Generate random curves in SOPs, bring them in with @sopimport and draw them with @rasterizecurves; or @curvescatter with line stamps. Distortion by @distort with a noise direction layer. UNVERIFIED chain.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## scratches-generator-normal\nname: Scratches Generator Normal\nsrc: /patterns/scratches-generator/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Version of Scratches Generator that outputs a normal map computed from the depth of the scratches.\nnote: The documentation page covers the grayscale and normal versions together.\nk: Normal Intensity (Normal version only) | Strength of the normal effect for every scratch.\nk: Normal Format (Normal version only) | DirectX or OpenGL green channel convention.\nuse: Scratch detail directly as a normal map.\ncop: Scratch layer as above, then @heighttonormal ({Normal Type}, {Height Scale}); the format toggle corresponds to a green channel flip.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## shape-splatter\nname: Shape Splatter\nsrc: /patterns/shape-splatter/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: Complex scattering node that places shapes onto a background height, driven by maps, and outputs splatter data used by companion nodes to build height, normal and colour consistently.\nk: X Amount | Number of columns of shapes.\nk: Y Amount | Number of rows of shapes.\nk: Pattern Input Number | Number of different patterns used (1 to 8).\nk: Pattern Distribution Mode | How the pattern is chosen (random, by pattern, line or column index).\nk: Scale | Uniform scale of shapes.\nk: Scale Random | Random scale per shape.\nk: Position Random | Random offset of each shape.\nk: Rotation Random | Random rotation per shape.\nk: Rotation from Bg Slope | Rotates shapes with the background slope.\nk: Height Offset | Moves all shapes along the height range.\nk: Height Scale | Scales the height of the shapes.\nk: Conform to Background | Blends shape height with the background surface.\nk: Mask Random | Randomly hides shapes.\nuse: Rocks, twigs and leaves placed on a landscape height and oriented by slope.\ncop: @shapescatter with {Blend Method}=Maximum and the per-pixel inputs {i:angle}, {i:direction}, {i:scale}, {i:density}; the background slope for orientation comes from @slopedir or @heighttonormal and is wired into {i:direction}; per-shape data are available through the {o:id} and {o:uv} outputs. Height conforming to the background has no built-in switch (compose it with @blend and a height offset sampled with @sample, UNVERIFIED).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## shape-splatter-blend\nname: Shape Splatter Blend\nsrc: /patterns/shape-splatter-blend/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Uses Shape Splatter Data to generate colour or grayscale maps from additional pattern inputs.\nk: Pattern Number | Number of patterns used.\nk: HSL/Luminance Adjustment | Global hue/saturation/luminance shift.\nk: HSL/Luminance Random | Random HSL/luminance shift per shape.\nk: Color Input Opacity | Opacity of the colour input.\nuse: Building albedo, roughness or secondary height maps with the same shape placement as the height.\ncop: Run a second @shapescatter with the same {Scatter Seed} and settings but different stamps, or use the {o:id} output as a lookup for per-shape variation via @randommono / @randomrgb.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## shape-splatter-data-extract\nname: Shape Splatter Data Extract\nsrc: /patterns/shape-splatter-data-extract/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Utility that separates Shape Splatter Data into individual channels for inspection or custom calculations.\nnote: The documentation page lists two Splatter Data inputs and no parameters.\nuse: Debugging and custom per-shape computations from the splatter data.\ncop: The equivalents are the {o:id} and {o:uv} outputs of @shapescatter, split with @channelsplit or read with @idtomono.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## shape-splatter-to-mask\nname: Shape Splatter to Mask\nsrc: /patterns/shape-splatter-to-mask/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Converts Shape Splatter Data into a black and white mask selected by pattern ID, with a random hide option.\nk: Pattern ID Start Range | First pattern ID selected.\nk: Pattern ID End Range | Last pattern ID selected.\nk: Random Mask | Share of shapes randomly masked out.\nk: Output | Binary mask, integer mask or grayscale values.\nuse: Isolating one kind of scattered object (for example only large rocks) for separate treatment.\ncop: @idtomask on the {o:id} output of @shapescatter (filter by ID range), with @randommono thresholded for the random hide.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## shape-splatter-v2\nname: Shape Splatter v2\nsrc: /patterns/shape-splatter-v2/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: New in Designer 16.0: scatters 3D shapes (primitives, extruded height maps or SDF shapes) on a background height with collisionless Poisson disc or uniform distribution, density maps and many outputs (height, SDF colour, normal and data).\nk: Position distribution mode | How shapes are distributed in space (2D grid and other modes).\nk: X amount | Columns of the distribution grid.\nk: Y amount | Rows of the distribution grid.\nk: Amount | Number of generated shapes.\nk: Shape type | Type of shape scattered.\nk: Pattern input number | Number of pattern input images.\nk: Enable shape extrude | Extrudes input patterns by interpreting them as heights.\nk: Shape scale | Size of the shape.\nk: Shape scale random | Random downscale of each shape.\nk: Position random | Random XY offset.\nk: 3D rotation random | Random 3D rotation of shapes.\nk: Slope rotation | Rotates shapes to match the background slope.\nk: Conform to background | Deforms shape height to follow the background.\nk: Mask random | Hides a ratio of shapes randomly.\nuse: Realistic scattered rocks, bolts, pebbles and debris with believable overlap behaviour and consistent normals.\ncop: Points from SOP scattering (with relaxation for Poisson-like spacing) via @sopimport, then @configurestamps and @stamppoint ({Blend Method}=Maximum, {Z Falloff}), or @shapescatter with {Jitter}. Normals from @heighttonormal, masks from {o:id}. Collisionless packing is not documented for COP, so the chain is UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## shape-splatter-v2-to-mask\nname: Shape Splatter v2 to Mask\nsrc: /patterns/shape-splatter-v2-to-mask/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Builds a mask from a selection of Shape splatter v2 shapes by unique shape ID, material or pattern ID, or random selection.\nk: Output | Values written for selected shapes in the mask.\nk: Shape ID start range | First shape ID selected.\nk: Shape ID end range | Last shape ID selected.\nk: Shape random mask | Ratio of shapes randomly masked.\nuse: Per-object masks for edge wear, moss or colour on scattered shapes.\ncop: @idtomask applied to the ID layer from the scatter chain, optionally combined with @maskcombine.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## shape-splatter-v2-mapper-grayscale\nname: Shape Splatter v2 Mapper Grayscale\nsrc: /patterns/shape-splatter-v2-mapper-grayscale/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Maps grayscale images onto the shapes scattered by Shape splatter v2 with planar or triplanar projection and per-shape variation.\nk: Projection mode | How images are projected onto shapes.\nk: Image projection | Distribution of input images across the projection planes.\nk: Projection scale | Scale of projected textures.\nk: Input selection mode | How the image for each shape is chosen.\nk: Luminance adjustment | Uniform luminance offset.\nk: Luminance random | Random luminance offset per shape.\nk: Tiling mode | Axes along which the texture repeats.\nk: UV offset | Offset of the mapping.\nuse: Giving scattered shapes their own surface detail (grain on rocks).\ncop: @triplanar (position layer plus textures per axis) or @sample with per-shape UVs from {o:uv} of the scatter node.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## shape-splatter-v2-mapper-color\nname: Shape Splatter v2 Mapper Color\nsrc: /patterns/shape-splatter-v2-mapper-color/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Colour version of the Shape splatter v2 mapper, with HSL adjustments, normal map handling and material ID support.\nk: Projection mode | How images are projected onto shapes.\nk: Is normal map | Treats the inputs as normal maps.\nk: HSL adjustment | Uniform hue, saturation and luminance offset.\nk: HSL random | Random HSL offset per shape.\nk: Tiling mode | Axes along which the texture repeats.\nuse: Colouring scattered shapes for albedo or normals.\ncop: @triplanar or @sample with {Normal Type} set for normal inputs, plus @hsv for the adjustments.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grid-atlas-grayscale\nname: Grid Atlas Grayscale\nsrc: /patterns/grid-atlas-grayscale/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Packs up to 16 grayscale images onto a grid to form an atlas that Shape splatter v2 can sample.\nk: Grid size X | Number of images along X.\nk: Grid size Y | Number of images along Y.\nk: Output size mode | How the atlas size is defined.\nuse: Packing a set of stone or debris height patterns into one input.\ncop: @contactsheet (arranges input layers into a contact sheet) for packing; individual cells are then read through the UV of the scatter nodes.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## grid-atlas-color\nname: Grid Atlas Color\nsrc: /patterns/grid-atlas-color/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Packs up to 16 colour images onto a grid to form an atlas for Shape splatter v2 or its colour mapper.\nk: Grid size X | Number of images along X.\nk: Grid size Y | Number of images along Y.\nk: Output size mode | How the atlas size is defined.\nuse: Atlas of albedo or normal variations for scattered shapes.\ncop: @contactsheet.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## triangle-grid\nname: Triangle Grid\nsrc: /patterns/triangle-grid/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Renders a triangulated surface made of 3D-positioned vertices, with random position, rotation and height offsets, in a Z-down orthographic view.\nk: Color Output | How the triangulated surface is represented.\nk: Triangulation | Which diagonal is used to split quads into triangles.\nk: X Amount | Vertices along X.\nk: Y Amount | Vertices along Y.\nk: Random Position Multiplier | Strength of the random vertex warp.\nk: Height Input Multiplier | Displaces vertices using the Height input.\nk: Blend Mode | How overlapping triangles combine.\nuse: Low-poly faceted terrain looks, crystalline plates and triangular tiling.\ncop: A SOP grid with jittered points and heights imported by @sopimport and drawn with @rasterizegeo; or @cellularnoise with {Lattice Type}=Hexagonal (simplicial grid) as an approximation. UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## panorama-shape\nname: Panorama Shape\nsrc: /patterns/panorama-shape/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Places HDR studio-style light shapes in a panorama with hotspot controls; can be chained.\nk: Shape | Square or disc.\nk: Shape Intensity | HDR intensity of the shape.\nk: Shape Soft Border | Border softness.\nk: Hotspot Intensity | HDR intensity of the hotspot.\nk: Hotspot Size | Size of the hotspot.\nk: Enable Backgound | Fills the background with a solid colour.\nuse: Building custom studio environment maps; not used for heights.\ncop: @sdfshape into @sdftomono, coloured with @monotorgb and scaled above 1.0 (layers are floating point); equirectangular placement through @uvtopolar. UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2882,"cache_read_input_tokens":500223,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2882,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015gkvFdKPiWmRHS7e9aXLQx":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-zenray--claude-Memory1/3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953/scratchpad/work/entries/02a_patterns.txt","content":"## tile-generator\nname: Tile Generator\nsrc: /patterns/tile-generator/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: The workhorse pattern node: repeats a chosen shape or up to six custom input patterns on an X by Y grid, with per-tile control of size, offset, rotation, value and masking. It is described as one of the most advanced nodes of the library.\nk: X Amount | Number of tile repetitions along X.\nk: Y Amount | Number of tile repetitions along Y.\nk: Pattern | The tile shape, one of the built-in height profiles or Image Input for custom patterns.\nk: Pattern Specific | Morphs the selected built-in shape (the effect depends on which pattern is chosen).\nk: Size Mode | How tile size is defined (Normal - Interstice, Normal - Size, Keep Ratio, Absolute, Pixel).\nk: Interstice X/Y | Gap between tiles, only in the interstice size mode.\nk: Scale | Global scale of every tile.\nk: Scale Random | Random scale variation per tile.\nk: Offset | Incremental shift applied row after row (or column after column), which gives running-bond brick layouts.\nk: Position Random | Random per-tile displacement, with separate X and Y control.\nk: Rotation@Rotation | Free rotation applied to all tiles.\nk: Rotation Random@Rotation | Random free rotation per tile.\nk: Luminance/Color Random | Per-tile luminance variation, i.e. random tile heights in a height graph.\nk: Checker Mask | Hides every other tile in a checkerboard fashion.\nk: Random Mask | Randomly hides a proportion of tiles.\nk: Blending Mode | How overlapping tiles combine (Add, Max, Add Sub).\nuse: Bricks, tiles, cobblestones, shingles, planks and any repeated module in a height graph; run its output into Flood Fill or Edge Detect to drive per-tile randomisation, bevels and wear.\ncop: @tilepattern. Set {Mode} to Tile Count and fill {Rows}/{Columns} (X Amount, Y Amount), or Seamless with {Divisions} for guaranteed tiling; {Pattern Type}=Stack Bond gives a square grid, Stretcher Bond gives the brick offset (also {Row Slide Offset} with a {Variation}); {Inset} is the interstice; {Draw As} chooses Filled, Distance (bevel-like falloff with {Fade Distance}), Gradient (with {Gradient Ramp} and {Rotate}) or Outline; {Tile Value} with {Variation} is the per-tile luminance; {Uniform Scale} plus {Variation} randomise size; {Rotate Tile} plus {Rotate Variation} randomise rotation; {Uniform Jitter} randomises position; masks are {Every Nth Tile}, {Checkerboard} and the {Threshold} prune group. Custom patterns go into the {i:stamp0} input; outputs are {o:tiles}, {o:id} (per-tile ID for random values) and {o:uv} (per-tile UV).\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## tile-generator-color\nname: Tile Generator Color\nsrc: /patterns/tile-generator/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Colour-input and colour-output version of Tile Generator; the page states it is rarely needed because the grayscale node covers almost every case.\nnote: The documentation page covers Tile Generator and its colour version together; the existence of a separate colour node is inferred from that page text.\nk: X Amount | Number of tile repetitions along X.\nk: Y Amount | Number of tile repetitions along Y.\nk: Blending Mode | How overlapping tiles combine.\nuse: Colour pattern bases (albedo of tiles); rarely used in pure height graphs.\ncop: Same @tilepattern chain; colour is obtained by feeding the {o:id} output into @randomrgb or by tinting {o:tiles} with @monotorgb; or use @shapescatter which has stamp {Stamp Color} controls.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## tile-sampler\nname: Tile Sampler\nsrc: /patterns/tile-sampler/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: Evolved Tile Generator whose scale, position, rotation, colour, mask and pattern choice can each be driven by an external map input, which makes it the tool for map-controlled scattering.\nk: X Amount | Number of tile repetitions along X.\nk: Y Amount | Number of tile repetitions along Y.\nk: Pattern | The tile shape or Pattern Input.\nk: Pattern Input Distribution | How multiple pattern inputs are picked (random, by number, or from a distribution map).\nk: Size Mode | General behaviour of the tile size (Normal, Keep Ratio, Absolute, Pixel).\nk: Scale Random | Random per-tile scale.\nk: Scale Map Multiplier | Strength of the Scale Map input.\nk: Position Random | Random per-tile position over both axes.\nk: Offset Type | Direction of the offset pattern (horizontal or vertical quincunx, or global).\nk: Displacement Map Intensity | Strength of the Displacement Map on the offset.\nk: Rotation Map Multiplier | Strength of the Rotation Map on per-tile rotation.\nk: Mask Map Threshold | Threshold below which the Mask Map hides tiles.\nk: Blending Mode | Blending of tiles on the background (Add/Sub or Max).\nk: Color Parametrization Mode | Source of per-tile colour (Color Input, Scale, Line Index, Row Index, Pattern Index).\nuse: Scattering rocks, pebbles or plates whose size follows a mask, orienting tiles along a vector map, and placing shapes only where a mask allows.\ncop: @shapescatter (SideFX-confirmed): {Stamps X}/{Stamps Y} set the grid, {Jitter} randomises position, {Angle}, {Stretch Mode}, {Scale Mode} give per-stamp variance, and the per-pixel inputs replace Tile Sampler's map slots: {i:scale} (Scale Map), {i:jitter} and {i:direction} (Displacement and Vector maps), {i:angle} (Rotation Map), {i:color} (Color Map), {i:density} or {i:select} (Mask and distribution maps), {i:stamps} (pattern inputs); {Blend Method}=Maximum corresponds to the Max blend; outputs {o:result}, {o:id}, {o:uv}.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## tile-sampler-color\nname: Tile Sampler Color\nsrc: /patterns/tile-sampler/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Colour version of Tile Sampler with alpha blending of coloured tiles and colour map parametrisation.\nnote: The documentation page covers Tile Sampler and its colour version together; the colour node is identified through the colour-only parameter variants in the page tables.\nk: Blending Mode | Blending of tiles (Add/Sub or Alpha Blend in the colour version).\nk: Color Parametrization Mode | Source of per-tile colour, including pattern centre positions in the colour version.\nuse: Colour variation of scattered stones, leaves or tiles; rarely needed for heights.\ncop: @shapescatter with {Stamp Color} (Uniform, Variance, Random from Ramp) and the {i:color} input.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## tile-random\nname: Tile Random\nsrc: /patterns/tile-random/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: Tile Generator variant that randomly splits tiles into smaller ones, giving irregular paving with chaotic tile shapes.\nk: X Amount | Number of base tiles along X.\nk: Y Amount | Number of base tiles along Y.\nk: Mode@Split | Rule for splitting tiles (none, auto, auto horizontal, auto vertical, random h+v).\nk: Threshold@Split | Size threshold above which a tile is split.\nk: Multiplier | How many splits are made; higher splits more.\nk: Amount@Interstice | Gap size between tiles.\nk: Scale Random | Random scale per tile.\nk: Rotation Random@Shape | Random rotation per tile.\nk: Random@Position | Random free position of tiles on X and Y.\nk: Color Random | Random tile luminance.\nuse: Flagstones, crazy paving, irregular tiling and broken stone slabs.\ncop: @tilepattern with {Split Tiles} on: {Iterations}, {Area Threshold}, {Split Treshold} (fraction of tiles split), {Number of Splits}, {Jitter Scale} for the split position and {Orient Ratio} for horizontal versus vertical splits; {Inset} for the interstice and {Tile Value} with {Variation} for random heights; {Uniform Jitter} for position randomness.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## tile-random-color\nname: Tile Random Color\nsrc: /patterns/tile-random/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Colour version of Tile Random with alpha-blend and colour parametrisation options.\nnote: The documentation page covers Tile Random and its colour version together.\nk: Color Parametrisation | Makes colour variation depend on area, size X or size Y.\nk: Blending Mode | Add/Sub, Max or Alpha Blend in the colour version.\nuse: Coloured irregular paving; rarely needed for heights.\ncop: Same @tilepattern chain with colours from @randomrgb driven by the {o:id} output.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## tile-random-2\nname: Tile Random 2\nsrc: /patterns/tile-random-2/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: Generates adjacent tiles of random sizes and aspect ratios, optionally slanted, rounded and bevelled, filling the whole canvas without gaps beyond the interstice.\nk: Amount X | Number of cells along X.\nk: Amount Y | Number of cells along Y.\nk: Random Size Multiplier | Intensity of random cell sizing.\nk: Interstice Thickness | Uniform gap between shapes.\nk: Round Corners Radius | Radius of rounded corners.\nk: Random Slant Multiplier | Intensity of random slanting of the cell sides.\nk: Bevel Distance Mode | How the bevel distance is determined.\nk: Bevel Distance Multiplier | Global bevel distance.\nk: Bevel Rounded Curve | Rounding of the bevel angle.\nk: Scale Multiplier | Shape size as a proportion of its cell.\nk: Mask Random Start | Start of the random masking range.\nk: Mask Random End | End of the random masking range.\nuse: Irregular stone walls, cobbles with varied sizes, slate and rubble relief with natural gaps.\ncop: No single node. @tilepattern with {Split Tiles} and {Jitter Scale} gives variable rectangles; slanted cells come from @cellularnoise with {Metric}=Manhattan or Chebyshev; rounded and bevelled edges from {o:border} (SDF distance) of @cellularnoise with {Gap}, {Bevel} and {Bevel Ramp}, or from @sdfadjust on an SDF of the tiles.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## splatter\nname: Splatter\nsrc: /patterns/splatter/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: Simple random placement of an input image over the canvas with many geometric placement controls; default settings look regular until Disorder parameters are raised.\nk: Pattern Size Width | Number of patterns along X.\nk: Pattern Size Height | Number of patterns along Y.\nk: Rotation | Rotation applied to every pattern.\nk: Rotation Variation | Random rotation of each shape.\nk: Zoom | Scales up the result (breaks tiling).\nk: Gain | Blending gain of each pattern.\nk: Disorder | Randomly shifts the shapes.\nk: Grid Number | Jumps between grid sizes while preserving tiling.\nk: Size Variation | Random scaling per shape.\nk: Luminance Variation | Random luminance per shape (grayscale version).\nuse: Quick scattering of pebbles, leaves, studs or dents without heavy tuning.\ncop: @shapescatter (SideFX lists the Splatter nodes under Scatter Shapes and Scatter on Curves): {Stamps X}/{Stamps Y}, {Jitter}, {Angle} with {Angle Variance}, {Scale Variance}, and stamps via {i:stamps}; {Blend Method}=Maximum or Add.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## splatter-color\nname: Splatter Color\nsrc: /patterns/splatter/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Colour version of Splatter with colour variation instead of luminance variation.\nnote: The documentation page covers Splatter and its colour version together.\nk: Color Variation | Random colour variation (colour version only).\nuse: Coloured scatter such as leaf litter; rarely needed for heights.\ncop: @shapescatter with {Stamp Color} set to Variance and {Hue}, {Saturation}, {Value} ranges.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## splatter-circular\nname: Splatter Circular\nsrc: /patterns/splatter-circular/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Ring-based pattern generator that places shapes or input images around one or several rings (or spirals), like Tile Generator but with circular placement.\nk: Pattern Amount | Number of tiles per ring.\nk: Ring Amount | Number of rings filled.\nk: Pattern | Tile shape or Image Input.\nk: Radius | Radius at which patterns are placed.\nk: Spiral Factor | Turns rings into spirals.\nk: Spread | Number of turns each ring covers.\nk: Center Orientation | Rotates each pattern to face the ring centre.\nk: Size Random | Random size per pattern.\nk: Scale by Ring Number | Makes scale depend on the ring index.\nk: Blending Mode | Blending of overlapping patterns (Add, Max, Add Sub).\nuse: Rosettes, fan patterns, drains, rivet rings, concentric ripples and radial studs.\ncop: @curvescatter along circle curves (from @curve3d or SOP geometry via @sopimport) with {Distribution}=By Count and {Angles Relative to Curve Direction}; or @copyxform with {Total Number}, {Rotate} and {Pivot Translate} to repeat a stamp around a pivot. Equivalence is partial; the SideFX page lists Splatter nodes under Scatter Shapes and Scatter on Curves.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## splatter-circular-color\nname: Splatter Circular Color\nsrc: /patterns/splatter-circular/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Colour-input version of Splatter Circular.\nnote: The documentation page covers Splatter Circular and its colour input variant together.\nk: Pattern Amount | Number of tiles per ring.\nuse: Coloured rosette patterns; rarely needed for heights.\ncop: Same as Splatter Circular with {Stamp Color} controls.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## shape\nname: Shape\nsrc: /patterns/shape/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: Generates precise, high-precision procedural shapes with built-in height profiles; the building block of most procedural height maps when combined with transform nodes.\nk: Pattern | Built-in shape or profile (Square, Disc, Paraboloid, Bell, Gaussian, Thorn, Pyramid, Brick, Gradation, Waves, Half Bell, Ridged Bell, Crescent, Capsule, Cone, Hemisphere).\nk: Pattern Specific | Morphs the selected pattern (effect depends on the pattern).\nk: Scale | Scales the entire shape.\nk: Size | Non-uniform scaling along X or Y.\nk: Angle | Rotation of the shape.\nk: Rotation 45° | Rotates by exactly 45 degrees.\nk: Tiling | Number of times the shape tiles.\nk: Non Square Tiling | Tiles the shape without squashing when Non Square Expansion is on.\nuse: Single stones, bumps, domes, ridges and profile masks that later feed Tile Sampler, Splatter or Flood Fill based chains.\ncop: @sdfshape wired into @sdftomono (SideFX-confirmed). Pick {Shape Class}/{Basic Shapes} (Circle, Rectangle, Regular Polygon, Star and others), then turn the SDF into the profile with {Remap Ramp} and {Iso Range} in @sdftomono; Paraboloid or Bell profiles are ramps over the distance, Hemisphere is a sqrt-shaped ramp (UNVERIFIED).\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## star\nname: Star\nsrc: /patterns/star/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Generates a five-pointed star.\nk: Scale | Uniform scale of the star.\nuse: Decorative stamps and test shapes.\ncop: @sdfshape with {Shape Class}=Basic Shapes and a Star type ({Number of Sides}=5, {Angle Factor}) into @sdftomono.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## starburst\nname: Starburst\nsrc: /patterns/starburst/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Generates a radial starburst with an adjustable number of rays, randomness and softness.\nk: Branches | Number of rays.\nk: Blur Amount | Softness of the result.\nk: Randomness | Random rotation of the rays around the centre.\nk: Size Min | Minimum ray size for variation.\nk: Size Max | Maximum ray size or global scale.\nk: Size Variation | Random scaling per ray.\nk: Tiling | Number of times the pattern tiles.\nuse: Impact cracks, splash patterns, radial scratches and star-shaped dents.\ncop: @ramp with {Type}=Radial (rays) and {Number of Cycles} equal to the branch count, thresholded with @remap and softened by @blur; or @uvtopolar on stripes. Ray randomness would need @distort driven by noise.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## stripes\nname: Stripes\nsrc: /patterns/stripes/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Tiling, angled stripe pattern that automatically adjusts so it stays seamless.\nk: Stripes | Number of stripes (the result is shifted to keep tiling).\nk: Width | Stripe width.\nk: Softness | Softness of the stripe edges.\nk: Shift | Tilts the stripes while keeping continuity.\nk: Align | Pivot of the shift (Edges or Center).\nuse: Grooves, corrugated panels, planks, ribbed surfaces; combine with Warp or noise for wavy grain.\ncop: @ramp ({Type}=Horizontal, {Number of Cycles}=stripe count, {Outside Range}=Repeat, {Rotation} for the tilt) followed by @remap with {Operation}=Threshold and {Width} for softness; or @tilepattern with a single row/column.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## checker-1\nname: Checker 1\nsrc: /patterns/checker-1/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Very simple checker pattern, handy for tests thanks to its obvious tiling and contrast.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nk: Rotate 45 Degrees | Rotates the pattern by 45 degrees.\nuse: Test pattern, tile checks, alternating panel heights.\ncop: @checkerboard ({Rows}, {Columns}, {Even Color}, {Odd Color}, {Offset}); rotate by 45 degrees with @xform2d.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## brick-1\nname: Brick 1\nsrc: /patterns/brick-1/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Simple brick pattern with adjustable smoothness and gap; see Brick Generator or Tile Generator for more options.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nk: Edge Smoothness | Blend between harsh and smooth edges.\nk: Interstice Width | Gap size between bricks.\nuse: Fast brick wall base for heights and masks.\ncop: @tilepattern with {Pattern Type}=Stretcher Bond, {Inset} for the interstice and {Draw As}=Distance with {Fade Distance} for edge smoothness.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## brick-2\nname: Brick 2\nsrc: /patterns/brick-2/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Second simple brick pattern with the same controls as Brick 1.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nk: Edge Smoothness | Blend between harsh and smooth edges.\nk: Interstice Width | Gap size between bricks.\nuse: Fast brick wall base for heights and masks.\ncop: As Brick 1 with another {Pattern Type} (for example Flemish Bond) or different row proportions.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## brick-generator\nname: Brick Generator\nsrc: /patterns/brick-generator/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: Advanced generator for man-made brick patterns with bevel, gap, row offset, per-brick height and slope controls.\nk: Bricks | Number of bricks along both axes.\nk: Bevel | Bevel profile of the bricks (two directions).\nk: Keep Ratio | Ties the bevel profile to the brick size.\nk: Gap | Gap between bricks (bevel adds to it).\nk: Middle Size | Size of every other column or row (running offset).\nk: Height | Height profile modifier, includes luminance variation between bricks.\nk: Slope | Tilts individual bricks as if they lie at an angle.\nk: Offset | Row-wise offset of the bricks.\nuse: Brick walls with per-brick height scatter and chipped feel; the Height and Slope controls replace manual Tile Generator setups.\ncop: @tilepattern with {Pattern Type}=Stretcher Bond or Custom Pattern, {Row Slide Offset} for Offset, {Inset} for Gap, {Draw As}=Distance with {Fade Distance} for Bevel, {Tile Value} with {Variation} for brick height variance, and the {o:uv} output (per-tile UV) combined with a random ID to tilt bricks (Slope) through @wrangle (UNVERIFIED).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## arc-pavement\nname: Arc Pavement\nsrc: /patterns/arc-pavement/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Generates a Parisian arc pavement pattern, a layout that cannot be done with Tile Generator or Tile Sampler.\nk: Scale | Global scale or tiling.\nk: Pattern Amount | Number of bricks in each arc.\nk: Pattern Amount Random | Randomises bricks per arc.\nk: Arcs Amount | Number of arcs stacked vertically (changes brick height).\nk: Pattern | Brick shape or input image.\nk: Pattern Height Decrease | Squashes brick height at arc ends.\nk: Color Random | Random tile colour.\nuse: Cobblestone streets, fan-pattern pavers and fish-scale paving.\ncop: No direct node. Nearest chain: @tilepattern with {Shape Class}=Compound Shapes (Fishscale) on a Stretcher Bond layout, or bricks scattered along arc curves with @curvescatter ({Distribution}=By Count). UNVERIFIED approximation.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## alveolus\nname: Alveolus\nsrc: /patterns/alveolus/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Soft-sphere pattern that can alternatively produce hexagon tiles.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nk: Gradient Filled Cells | Switches to sharp-edged hexagon tiles.\nk: Interstice Width | Gap size when the sharp-edge option is off.\nuse: Honeycomb relief, hex tiles, pebble-like bumps and bubble wrap.\ncop: @cellularnoise with {Lattice Type}=Hexagonal, {Jitter}=0 (perfect lattice), {Gap} for the interstice, {Bevel} and {Smooth Edge} for the soft-sphere profile; the {o:border} output gives a hex-wall mask.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mesh-1\nname: Mesh 1\nsrc: /patterns/mesh-1/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Simple mesh (grid) pattern with thin blocks.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nk: Rotate 45 Degrees | Rotates the result 45 degrees.\nuse: Grates, wire mesh, tiling detail for height and detail maps.\ncop: @tilepattern ({Pattern Type}=Stack Bond with {Inset}) or a pair of @ramp stripes combined with @blend; rotate with {Rotate Pattern}.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mesh-2\nname: Mesh 2\nsrc: /patterns/mesh-2/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: low\npurpose: Simple mesh pattern with fat blocks.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nk: Rotate 45 Degrees | Rotates the result.\nuse: Grates and coarse mesh detail.\ncop: As Mesh 1 with a smaller {Inset} so blocks look fat.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## weave-1\nname: Weave 1\nsrc: /patterns/weave-1/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Simple woven pattern.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nk: Rotate 45 Degrees | Rotates the pattern.\nuse: Basket weave, cloth and rattan relief.\ncop: @weave ({Rows}, {Columns}, {Weave Multiplier}, {Fiber Scale}, {Fiber Strength}, {Edge Gradient}, {Overlap Gradient}); outputs {o:weave}, {o:uv}, {o:id}.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## weave-2\nname: Weave 2\nsrc: /patterns/weave-2/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Simple weave with randomisation controls; at maximum disorder it behaves like a noise.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nk: Disorder | Shuffles the stitches of the weave.\nuse: Irregular fabric or wicker relief.\ncop: @weave plus {Every Nth Column} and {Every Nth Tile} for irregular skips, or a random merge with @fractalnoise through @blend.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## weave-generator\nname: Weave Generator\nsrc: /patterns/weave-generator/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Weave pattern node with a few controls, producing patterns not reachable with the predefined weaves.\nk: Tile X | Number of blocks along X.\nk: Tile Y | Number of blocks along Y.\nk: Shape | Height profile curve of the stitch.\nk: Weave | Number of stitches per block.\nk: Gap | Gap between stitches along X and Y.\nuse: Cloth, wicker, carbon fibre or basket relief.\ncop: @weave: {Rows} and {Columns} for Tile Y and Tile X, {Weave Multiplier} for stitches per block, {Fiber Scale} and {Fiber Strength} for the stitch profile, {Edge Gradient} for the shape.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## fibers-1\nname: Fibers 1\nsrc: /patterns/fibers-1/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Simple fiber-like pattern suited to rope, mesh or cloth heights and details.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nuse: Rope, cord, thread and mesh relief.\ncop: @weave with strong {Fiber Strength}, or @knit for yarn-like loops.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## fibers-2\nname: Fibers 2\nsrc: /patterns/fibers-2/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Simple cloth-like pattern with larger structure than Fibers 1.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nuse: Coarse cloth, burlap, mesh and organic detail.\ncop: @weave with fewer {Rows}/{Columns}; @knit for knitted cloth.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## gaussian-1\nname: Gaussian 1\nsrc: /patterns/gaussian-1/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Simple tiled gaussian blob pattern.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nuse: Soft round bumps, dents or stipple pattern.\ncop: @tilepattern ({Pattern Type}=Stack Bond, {Draw As}=Distance) followed by @remap with a bell-shaped {Ramp}; or one blob from @sdfshape and @sdftomono repeated with @shapescatter.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## gaussian-2\nname: Gaussian 2\nsrc: /patterns/gaussian-2/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Second tiled gaussian blob pattern.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nuse: Soft round bumps and dents.\ncop: As Gaussian 1 with a different blob width via {Fade Distance} and the ramp shape.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## gradient-linear-1\nname: Gradient Linear 1\nsrc: /patterns/gradient-linear-1/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: Perfectly smooth black to white linear gradient, one of the most used building blocks.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions (sawtooth).\nk: Rotation | Direction of the gradient in 90 degree steps.\nuse: Mask ramps, height slopes, input to Histogram Scan or Warp to build ridges and terraces.\ncop: @ramp ({Type}=Horizontal or Vertical, {Number of Cycles} for Tiling, {Outside Range}=Repeat, {Rotation} for the direction); for the default left to right black to white keep the default two-point mono {Ramp}.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## gradient-linear-2\nname: Gradient Linear 2\nsrc: /patterns/gradient-linear-2/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: Smooth double-sided black to white to black gradient with a rounded, pipe-like profile.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nk: Rotation | Switches the direction between left-right and top-bottom.\nuse: Cylindrical ridges, pipes, grooves and rounded ribs in height maps.\ncop: @ramp with {Outside Range}=Mirror and a smooth (spline) {Ramp} peaking at the centre; or @ramp followed by @function (sin) to create the pipe profile (UNVERIFIED).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## gradient-linear-3\nname: Gradient Linear 3\nsrc: /patterns/gradient-linear-3/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: high\npurpose: Advanced linear gradient with a sharp, straight slope and a movable peak.\nk: Tiling | Number of repetitions.\nk: Position | Where the midpoint or peak lies.\nk: Rotation | Direction of the gradient.\nuse: Roofs, wedges, V-grooves and asymmetric ramps.\ncop: @ramp with a three-point mono {Ramp} (0 at the left, 1 at the {Position} peak, 0 at the right) and linear interpolation.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## gradient-axial\nname: Gradient Axial\nsrc: /patterns/gradient-axial/\ncat: Texture generators > Patterns\nrel: medium\npurpose: Black to white gradient between two custom points, allowing linear gradients at any angle (does not always tile).\nk: Point 1 | Start point (black).\nk: Point 2 | End point (white).\nuse: Directional fades, lighting-like falloff masks and slanted 