x and an HQ blur internally.\nuse: Brushed metal streaks, wind-swept sand, long soft shadows in height maps, directional smoothing.\ncop: @streakblur ({Direction Type}=Angle, {Angle}, {Length}, {Mode}=Blur) is the directional blur (SideFX lists Directional Blur under Streak Blur); mix with a plain @blur through @blend to emulate anisotropy below 1. Relation of Anisotropy to the blend weight is UNVERIFIED.\ngray: Grayscale input and output.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## radial-blur\nname: Radial Blur\nsrc: /blurs/radial-blur/\ncat: Texture filters > Blurs\nrel: low\npurpose: Spinning, motion-type blur around a centre point.\nk: Samples | Quality of the blur (1 to 128).\nk: Angle | Amount of spin.\nk: Center Position | Centre point of the effect.\nuse: Brushed circular metal, lens-like spin streaks, turbine and wheel heights.\ncop: Build a tangent direction field and streak along it: @ramp with {Type}=Concentric at the centre, @slopedir with {Angle}=90 (directions that circle the hill instead of climbing it), then @distort with {Streak}=Blur and {Scale} for the amount. UNVERIFIED chain.\ngray: Grayscale input and output.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## median-filter-color\nname: Median Filter Color\nsrc: /blurs/median-filter-color/\ncat: Texture filters > Blurs\nrel: low\npurpose: Removes noise while preserving edges by replacing each pixel with the median of its neighbourhood (with a more robust MLMAD variant).\nk: Kernel size | Size of the square neighbourhood.\nk: Filter type | Median or MLMAD (median of least median absolute deviation).\nk: Affect alpha | Whether alpha is filtered too.\nuse: Cleaning scanned colour data before extracting heights.\ncop: @median ({Filter Size} 3x3 or 5x5, repeat for a larger kernel).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## median-filter-grayscale\nname: Median Filter Grayscale\nsrc: /blurs/median-filter-grayscale/\ncat: Texture filters > Blurs\nrel: medium\npurpose: Edge-preserving noise removal for grayscale data using the neighbourhood median.\nk: Kernel size | Size of the square neighbourhood.\nk: Filter type | Median or MLMAD.\nuse: Removing spikes and salt-and-pepper noise from scanned or generated heights without rounding sharp ridges.\ncop: @median (grayscale Mono layer), {Filter Size} 3x3 or 5x5; cascade passes for larger kernels.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mlv-color\nname: MLV Color\nsrc: /blurs/mlv-color/\ncat: Texture filters > Blurs\nrel: low\npurpose: Mean of Least Variance filter: finds structuring areas of an image and uses them to sharpen and flatten it at the same time, which can leave steps along wide gradients.\nk: Intensity | Strength of the smoothing into flat areas.\nk: Smoothness | Rounds the structuring areas to reduce stepping.\nk: Criterion | How pixels are grouped into structuring areas.\nk: Gaussian | Uses a Gaussian grouping for smoother areas.\nk: Affect alpha | Also filters alpha.\nk: Iterations | Number of passes.\nuse: Painterly flattening, noise removal that keeps edges crisp.\ncop: @kuwaharafilter (it selects the neighbourhood with the least variance and outputs its mean, the same principle): {Radius}, {Method}=Exact, {Blend to Blur}, repeated passes for Iterations. UNVERIFIED equivalence.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mlv-grayscale\nname: MLV Grayscale\nsrc: /blurs/mlv-grayscale/\ncat: Texture filters > Blurs\nrel: medium\npurpose: Grayscale version of the Mean of Least Variance filter: sharpens edges and flattens noisy areas.\nk: Intensity | Strength of the smoothing.\nk: Smoothness | Rounds the structuring areas.\nk: Criterion | How pixels are grouped.\nk: Gaussian | Gaussian grouping.\nk: Iterations | Number of passes.\nuse: Cleaning a height map while keeping ridges and cliffs, making terraced flat regions.\ncop: @kuwaharafilter on the Mono layer ({Radius}, {Method}=Exact), several passes. UNVERIFIED equivalence.\nstatus: unverified\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"e959b35a-c115-4480-96c9-365db168794e","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfvd1wr3XzEZ9Kt97GU52","requestedModel":"cla