t the sampled results when interpolating between pixels: - Nearest: will sample exa...\n  P: Show Helper {Boolean}: Visualize the extended section as an overlay with arrows showing the direction of the extension.\n=== FXAA  [filters/effects/fxaa]  (Filters > Effects)\nD: Applies an anti aliasing filter based on the FXAA algorithm. You can use this to fix jagged, pixelated edges on shapes. It's especially useful for something like a Disc Shape that has pixelated edges, as it provides a simple, one node solution to Anti-Alias edges. ¶\n=== Glow  [filters/effects/glow]  (Filters > Effects)\nD: Performs an \"Outer Glow\"-type of effect, as seen in other popular image editing software. Essentially adds a fading gradient outline around the input. Keep in mind that this is not intended to work for images with Alpha Channels, as you might expect. Even the color version only expects binary, bl\n  P: Glow Amount {0.0 - 1.0}: Global opacity for the glow effect.\n  P: Clear Amount {0.0 - 1.0}: Treshold for when to cut off the glow effect. Useful for semi-transparent areas.\n  P: Glow Size {0.0 - 20.0}: Controls how far the glow effect reaches.\n  P: Glow Color {(Color value) (Color Version Only)}: Sets the color of the glow effect.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cd8dd077-8f16-47f1-a7f9-f8ae8eda9e27","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:39:57.485Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ce781e57-dd80-4e7c-b2d1-ff6c5d95e56e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":27,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory"