{"parentUuid":"d3051b38-ec07-45fb-a14e-e7d798bc95e1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a9840a94295146d85","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DxmetcCcwLp25NopsYq8s7","type":"tool_result","content":"#nodes 6\n=== Flood Fill Mapper  [filters/effects/flood-fill-mapper]  (Filters > Effects)\nD: Flood Fill Mapper allows remapping of an existing Pattern or Texture onto every single cell from a Flood Fill. It is different from other Flood Fill conversions like Random Grayscale or Gradient in that it does not generate solid colors or values, but allows you to use you own input maps. It can be seen as a sort of combination of Flood Fill and Tile Sampler or Shape Mapper, as it provides quite a few similar cont\nIN: Flood Fill Bbox (Color Input); Pattern Input 1-8 (Grayscale/Color Input); Pattern Distribution Map (Grayscale Input); Scale Map (Grayscale Input); Rotation Map (Grayscale Input); Luminance Offset Map (Grayscale Input)\n  P: Tiling Mode {No Tiling, H+V}: Set wether to use Tiling or not. Only visible if Size or Scale ar set below 1.\n  [Pattern]\n  P: Pattern Input Number {1 - 8}: Set amount of Custom Pattern Inputs to use.\n  P: Pattern Distribution Mode {Random, Shape Size, Distribution Map Input}: Set the method to determine what Pattern is shown in a Cell.\n  P: Pattern Distribution Jittering {0.0 - 1.0}: Allows for a slight varaition or Offset in the Pattern distribution without changing everything through teh Random Seed.\n  [Size]\n  P: Size Mode {Relative to Texture, Relative to Shape BSphere, Relative to Largest Shape, Relative to Smallest Shape, Fit Shape BBox}: Set how the size of the pattern in each cell is determined.\n  P: Size {0.0 - 1.0}: Allows for non-uniform scaling of the Pattern.\n  P: Scale {0.0 - 1.0}: Set the global (uniform) scale for the effect.\n  P: Scale Map Mulitplier {0.0 - 1.0}: Set influence of the optional Scale Map.\n  P: Scale Random {-1.0 - 1.0}: Set the amount of random variation within pattern scale.\n  [Rotation]\n  P: Rotation {0.0 - 1.0}: Set global, uniform rotation for every cell.\n  P: Rotation Map Mulitplier {0.0 - 1.0}: Set influence of the optional Rotation map.\n  P: Rotation Random {0.0 - 1.0}: Set the amount of random rotation for every cell.\n  P: Rotation Autoscale {False/True}: Set if a pattern should adjust its scale to fit within a cell when rotated.\n  [Position]\n  P: Position Offset {0.0 - 1.0}: Set global Position offset for every cell.\n  P: Position Offset Alignment {Texture, Pattern}: Set to either align the offset 0-point to the Pattern cell or to the texture.\n  P: Position Offset Random {0.0 - 1.0}: Set the amount of per-cell Position offset randomisation.\n  [Color (Only for Grayscale version)]\n  P: Luminance Range {0.0 - 1.0}: Sets the global contrast on the texture, where 0 becomes middle gray.\n  P: Luminance Range Random {0.0 - 1.0}: Sets the amount of randomisation for the Luminance Range.\n  P: Luminance Offset {-1.0 - 1.0}: Sets the offset for the Luminance, working as a brightness control.\n  P: Luminance Offset Random {0.0 - 1.0}: Sets the amount of randomisation for the Luminance Offset.\n  P: Luminance Offset Map Mulitplier {0.0 - 1.0}: Sets the influence of the optional Luminance Offset map.\n  P: Background Color {(Grayscale value)}: Sets the background color onto which textures are blended.\n  [Color (Only for Color version)]\n  P: Is Normal Map {False/True}: Set to interpret Pattern Input as a Normal Map. Will compensate and fix Normal Tangent space rotation.\n  P: Normal Format {DirectX, OpenGL}: Switch between different Normal Map formats (inverts the green channel). Only Active when Is Normal Map is True.\n  P: HSL Adjustment {-1.0 - 1.0}: Adjust HSL globally.\n  P: HSL Random {-1.0 - 1.0}: Set HSL randomisation per cell.\n  P: Alpha Adjustment {-1.0 - 1.0}: Set global Alpha adjustment, reduces Alpha contrast.\n  P: Alpha Random {-1.0 - 1.0}: Set Alpha Adjustment randomisation per cell.\n  P: Background Color {(Color value)}: Sets the background color onto which textures are blended.\n=== Flood Fill to BBox Size  [filters/effects/flood-fill-to-bbox-size]  (Filters > Effects)\nD: Generates a grayscale map from a Flood Fill base, with values tied to each tile's individual size. Values are relative to the total canvas size (a full white tile would mean it stretches the entire canvas), so contrast is often low. ¶\n  P: Output {max(X, Y), X, Y}: Sets what metric the value is based on: width, length or both.\n=== Flood Fill to Gradient  [filters/effects/flood-fill-to-gradient]  (Filters > Effects)\nD: Transforms a Flood Fill base into (randomly oriented) gradients. Very useful for creating a Heightmap where tiles are randomly tilted and sloped. ¶\nIN: Flood Fill (Color Input); Angle Input (Grayscale Input); Slope Input (Grayscale Input)\n  P: Angle {0.0 - 1.0}: Sets uniform, global angle/direction for all tiles.\n  P: Angle Variation {0.0 - 1.0}: Randomises the angle for each tile individually. This is the most useful and powerful parameter!\n  P: Multiply by Bounding Box Size {0.0 - 1.0}: Scales the entire linear effect by the tile's individual bounding box size. This means smaller tiles will end up being darker than larger ones.\n  P: Angle Image Input Multiplier {0.0 - 1.0}: Set influence of optional Angle Input map on generated gradient directions\n  P: Slope Image Input Multiplier {0.0 - 1.0}: Set influence of optional Slope Input map on generated gradient slope strength.\n  P: Multiply by Slope Intensity {0.0 - 1.0}: \n  P: Flat Slope Color {(Grayscale value)}: Allows setting of solid value for flat slopes.\n=== Flood Fill to Index  [filters/effects/flood-fill-to-index]  (Filters > Effects)\nD: Flood Fill to Index converts every Flood Fill cell to a value according to its index number, starting with 0 in the top left corner. It can be used to return grayscale tints in a normalised form (0.0 to 1.0, divided by as many cell