{"parentUuid":"ead2bc8d-ba83-45dd-893b-a0535ad846b0","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a9840a94295146d85","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvd9sEh6RURs2vnwh5uD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0137pFFYEZPd4gNXE2iZGh3H","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-zenray--claude-Memory1/3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953/scratchpad/work/entries/05a_effects.txt","content":"## flood-fill\nname: Flood Fill\nsrc: /effects/flood-fill/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Analyses a binary tile map and stores, per connected shape, the data (bounding boxes, positions, sizes) that the other Flood Fill nodes turn into random values, gradients, positions or mapped patterns. It is the starting point of the Flood Fill family and is not meant to be used alone.\nk: Safety/Speed trade-off | Chooses the calculation mode for simple or small shapes versus complex or big ones, or a no-failure mode.\nk: Avanced options | Shows or hides the advanced parameters and outputs.\nk: Override Safety/Speed trade-off | Advanced override of internal behaviour for custom effects and debugging.\nuse: Per-tile randomisation of height, tilt, bevel and wear on bricks, tiles and stones; the input must be a clean binary map where tiles are separated by pure black lines (a Tile Generator output is the ideal source).\ncop: @segmentbyconnectivity (SideFX-confirmed) labels each connected region and gives an {o:id} layer ({Connectivity}=Above Threshold with {Threshold}); @uvmapbyid then derives per-island data ({Mode}=UV Map, Center, Minimum, Maximum or Size) and @statisticsbyid gives per-ID area, minimum and maximum. The per-tile variation nodes below are built from these outputs.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## flood-fill-to-random-grayscale\nname: Flood Fill to Random Grayscale\nsrc: flood-fill-to-random-grayscale.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Gives every Flood Fill tile a random grayscale value.\nnote: The documentation page lists no parameters; the seed comes from the node random seed.\nuse: Random per-tile height offsets for bricks, tiles and cobbles.\ncop: @randommono with the island ID wired into its {i:seed} input and a {Range Values} of Min/Max (SideFX lists Random Mono as the Flood Fill to Random Grayscale equivalent); segmentation from @segmentbyconnectivity.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## flood-fill-to-random-color\nname: Flood Fill to Random Color\nsrc: flood-fill-to-random-color.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Gives every Flood Fill tile a random RGB colour.\nnote: The documentation page lists no parameters.\nuse: ID colour maps for masks and visual checks of tile segmentation.\ncop: @randomrgb driven by the island ID (SideFX lists Random RGB as the equivalent), or @idtorgb on the {o:id} output of @segmentbyconnectivity.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## flood-fill-to-grayscale-color\nname: Flood Fill to Grayscale\nsrc: flood-fill-to-grayscale-color.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Uses Flood Fill data to give each tile a grayscale swatch with controllable bias and variation, optionally starting from a value sampled from an extra input map per tile.\nnote: The documentation page covers the grayscale and colour versions together (two icons).\nk: Luminance/Color Adjustment | Bias or base value of each tile; with an input map it offsets the sampled start value.\nk: Luminance/Color Random | Amount of variation between tiles.\nuse: Controlled per-tile height variation where the base height of each tile comes from a mask or a gradient.\ncop: @uvmapbyid with {Mode}=Center gives the centre of each island; @sample (UV Sample) reads the input map at that centre, @randommono (id into {i:seed}) adds variation, and @blend (Add) combines them.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## flood-fill-to-grayscale-color-colour\nname: Flood Fill to Color\nsrc: flood-fill-to-grayscale-color.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Colour swatch version of the Flood Fill to Grayscale node.\nnote: Shares the documentation page with Flood Fill to Grayscale.\nk: Luminance/Color Adjustment | Bias or base colour of each tile.\nk: Luminance/Color Random | Amount of colour variation.\nuse: Colour variation per tile for albedo; not for heights.\ncop: Same chain as Flood Fill to Grayscale with @sample on an RGB layer and @randomrgb for variation, or @hsv with a per-ID hue shift.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## flood-fill-to-gradient\nname: Flood Fill to Gradient\nsrc: /effects/flood-fill-to-gradient/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Turns every Flood Fill tile into a gradient with a random orientation, ideal for heights where tiles are randomly tilted and sloped.\nk: Angle | Uniform angle of all gradients.\nk: Angle Variation | Random angle per tile; the most useful control.\nk: Multiply by Bounding Box Size | Scales the gradient by the tile bounding box so small tiles are darker.\nk: Angle Image Input Multiplier | Influence of the optional angle map.\nk: Slope Image Input Multiplier | Influence of the optional slope map.\nk: Flat Slope Color | Value of flat slopes.\nuse: Tilted flagstones, slate roofs, wood planks with individual tilt; feed the result into Height Blend or add to the base height with a small amplitude.\ncop: @uvmapbyid ({Mode}=UV Map, {Auto Scale}) supplies per-tile UVs in 0 to 1; rotate them per tile with @uvxform ({Rotate} with a random value from the {i:seed} input, {Uniform Scale}); take the U channel with @rgbtouv or @channelextract and treat it as the gradient. UNVERIFIED chain.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## flood-fill-to-bbox-size\nname: Flood Fill to BBox Size\nsrc: flood-fill-to-bbox-size.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: medium\npurpose: Gives each tile a grayscale value tied to the size of its bounding box (relative to the whole canvas), so contrast is often low.\nk: Output | Metric used: width, height or the maximum of both.\nuse: Making large stones higher than small ones, or driving wear amount by tile size.\ncop: @uvmapbyid with {Mode}=Size (per-island bounding size), then split with @rgbtouv or @channelextract and use the maximum of X and Y with @blend {Mode}=Maximum; @statisticsbyid is an alternative for area based values.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## flood-fill-to-index\nname: Flood Fill to Index\nsrc: /effects/flood-fill-to-index/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Converts every tile to a value from its index (starting at 0 in the top-left corner), either normalised to 0 to 1 or as an unclamped integer count.\nk: Output | Normalised (0 to 1) or Integer (0 to n).\nk: Ignore Shape Smaller Than | Ignores tiny shapes.\nk: Show Flood Fill Data Table | Debug output of the Flood Fill data.\nuse: Sequential tile ordering effects, gradient across tiles, counting tiles.\ncop: @idtomono (the {Conversion} option controls casting versus safe packing) on the ID layer from @segmentbyconnectivity; divide by the count from @statistics ({o:maximum}) for the normalised variant.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## flood-fill-to-position\nname: Flood Fill to Position\nsrc: flood-fill-to-position.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: medium\npurpose: Generates a per-tile position map (tile centre in the red and green channels), meant as a base for further calculations.\nnote: The documentation page lists no parameters.\nuse: Per-tile pivots for rotation, distance from a tile centre, directional gradients per tile.\ncop: @uvmapbyid with {Mode}=Center (the output holds the centre position of each ID island).\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## flood-fill-mapper\nname: Flood Fill Mapper\nsrc: /effects/flood-fill-mapper/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Remaps an existing pattern or texture onto every Flood Fill cell, with pattern choice, scale, rotation, position and luminance randomisation; a mix of Flood Fill and Tile Sampler or Shape Mapper.\nk: Pattern Input Number | Number of custom pattern inputs (1 to 8).\nk: Pattern Distribution Mode | How a pattern is picked for a cell (random, shape size, distribution map).\nk: Size Mode | How the size of the pattern in each cell is determined (relative to texture, shape sphere, largest or smallest shape, or fit shape box).\nk: Scale | Global uniform scale.\nk: Scale Random | Random scale variation.\nk: Rotation Random | Random rotation per cell.\nk: Rotation Autoscale | Rescales the pattern to stay inside the cell when rotated.\nk: Position Offset Random | Random position offset per cell.\nk: Luminance Range | Global contrast of the texture in each cell (grayscale version).\nk: Luminance Offset | Brightness offset (grayscale version).\nuse: Putting a stone texture, grain or detail map onto each tile of a tile graph with per-tile variation, so each stone gets its own surface relief.\ncop: @uvmapbyid ({Mode}=UV Map, {Auto Scale}) gives per-cell UVs, @uvxform adds the per-cell random {Rotate}, {Uniform Scale}, {Translate} (its {i:seed} input takes the ID), and @sample (UV Sample) reads the pattern; luminance randomisation with @randommono and @blend.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## ambient-occlusion-hbao\nname: Ambient Occlusion (HBAO)\nsrc: ambient-occlusion-hbao-filter-node.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Generates an ambient occlusion map from a height map with horizon-based ambient occlusion, an algorithm designed for screen-space real-time AO; fast and simple.\nk: Use World Units | Switches from screen-space scale to world-unit controls.\nk: Height Depth | Global height scale (screen-space mode).\nk: Surface Size | Physical size of the surface (world-unit mode).\nk: Height Scale (cm) | Height scale in centimetres (world-unit mode).\nk: Radius | Spread of the AO.\nk: Quality | Number of samples (4, 8 or 16).\nk: GPU Optimization | Internal speed-up.\nuse: Cavity and crevice shading from procedural heights; AO as a mask for dirt in valleys, moss, and darkened joints; essential to judge heights visually.\ncop: @heighttoambientocclusion (SideFX-confirmed): {Height Scale} (Height Depth), {Space} (Local or World, for the world-units option), {View Radius} (Radius), {Sample Count} (Quality), {Step Scale}, {Sample from Hemisphere}, and a {Remap Ramp} to shape the occlusion falloff.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## ambient-occlusion-rtao\nname: Ambient Occlusion (RTAO)\nsrc: /effects/ambient-occlusion-rtao/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Ray-traced ambient occlusion from a height map; more accurate than HBAO but slower and not meant for the CPU engine.\nk: Use Physical Size | Uses physical size settings to determine the height scale.\nk: Physical Size | Real physical size of the surface.\nk: Samples | Number of rays (more gives smoother results).\nk: Height Scale | Multiplier of the height input.\nk: Distribution | Distribution method, affecting falloff toward shadowed areas.\nk: Maximum Distance | Maximum distance rays can travel to be occluded.\nk: Spread Angle | Spread angle of the rays (1 is a full hemisphere).\nuse: Higher-quality AO for final bakes of procedural heights, ambient shadowing for large relief.\ncop: @heighttoambientocclusion with a high {Sample Count} and a large {View Radius} (the node is described as imagining a sphere per pixel and testing how occluded it is). Ray traced alternatives exist through @raytrace on a mesh version of the height. UNVERIFIED equivalence.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## anisotropic-kuwahara\nname: Anisotropic Kuwahara Color\nsrc: /effects/anisotropic-kuwahara/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Directional blur that conforms to image details so the result appears to flow along shapes, with sharpness controls producing flatter, painterly regions.\nk: Radius | Blur radius.\nk: Smoothness | Blending of colours along the computed direction.\nk: Sharpness | Contrast of the blurred areas (flatter, cleaner areas).\nk: Anisotropy | Contribution of the direction map.\nk: Use input direction map | Uses a supplied direction map instead of computing one.\nk: Tensor smoothness | Smoothing of the computed directions.\nk: Anisotropy angle | Extra rotation of the direction map, in turns.\nuse: Painterly flow smoothing of colour scans; of limited use for heights.\ncop: @kuwaharafilter (the isotropic version); flow-aware streaking can be added with @distort driven by @slopedir. UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## anisotropic-kuwahara-grayscale\nname: Anisotropic Kuwahara Grayscale\nsrc: anisotropic-kuwahara-grayscale.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: medium\npurpose: Grayscale version of Anisotropic Kuwahara; flow-following smoothing with sharpening of flat regions.\nk: Radius | Blur radius.\nk: Smoothness | Blending along the direction.\nk: Sharpness | Flattening and sharpness.\nk: Anisotropy | Contribution of the direction map.\nuse: Smoothing scanned heights along their features while keeping ridges defined.\ncop: @kuwaharafilter on the Mono layer; optionally followed by @distort with a direction layer from @slopedir ({Streak}=Blur). UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## bevel-filter-node\nname: Bevel\nsrc: bevel-filter-node.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Applies an edge bevel to a grayscale height map (ideally a high-contrast binary one) and returns both the bevelled height and the matching normal map; supports exact custom curve profiles.\nk: Distance | How far the bevel reaches (negative values go the other way).\nk: Corner Type | Round or angular profile.\nk: Smoothing | Extra smoothing (blur) after the bevel.\nk: Use Non-Uniform Blur | Smoothing done non-uniformly.\nk: Use Custom Curve | Uses your own height curve for the profile.\nk: Normal Intensity | Strength of the normal output.\nk: Normal Format | DirectX or OpenGL convention.\nuse: Beveled tiles, bricks, stones and metal plates from a binary mask; the single most frequent way to give hard-surface edges to a height.\ncop: @feather (SideFX-confirmed): {Feather Direction}=Circle for Round corners (Diamond or Octagon for Angular), {Distance for Unit Change} as Distance, {Feather from High to Low} to choose inward or outward growth, then a custom profile with @remap ({Use Ramp}); normals with @heighttonormal ({Normal Type}, {Height Scale}). The SD smoothing option is an extra @blur.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## bevel-smooth\nname: Bevel Smooth\nsrc: /effects/bevel-smooth/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Draws a gradient (or flat colour) from the borders of a mask outwards, inwards or both, keeping the gradient of the nearest border where several overlap; the distance can vary along the border with a distance map.\nk: Output mode | Bevel (gradient) or other dilation modes.\nk: Direction | Which side of the border is dilated (in, out or both).\nk: Maximum distance | Distance of the dilation in normalised image space.\nk: Mask smoothness | Radius of the smoothing applied to the mask.\nk: Mask offset | Moves mask borders inwards or outwards.\nk: Mask threshold | Value used to detect the borders of the mask.\nk: Distance map multiplier | Influence of the optional distance map on the maximum distance.\nuse: Clean, smooth bevel gradients on masks without the stepping of other bevel nodes; variable bevel width from a map.\ncop: @monotosdf ({Iso} = mask threshold) then @sdftomono with a {Remap Ramp} for the bevel profile and {Iso Range} for the maximum distance; or @feather. The variable-width map can drive {Iso Range} through a remap of the SDF. UNVERIFIED chain.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## directional-distance\nname: Directional Distance\nsrc: /effects/directional-distance/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: medium\npurpose: Draws a distance gradient from the borders of a mask in a chosen direction, keeping the nearest border where gradients overlap.\nk: Output mode | How the gradient is drawn (for example inverted normalised distance).\nk: Maximum distance | Distance travelled by the gradient.\nk: Angle | Direction of the gradient in turns.\nk: Distance map multiplier | Influence of the distance map.\nk: Angle map multiplier | Influence of the angle map.\nuse: Directional shadows, drips and soft edges that fall off in one direction.\ncop: @streakblur with {Mode}=Maximum, {Direction Type}=Angle, {Length} as Maximum distance and a falling {Streak Weight} ramp (enable {Use Streak Weight}) to create the distance falloff; the per-pixel {i:direction} and {i:scalelength} inputs replace the angle and distance maps. UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## edge-detect\nname: Edge Detect\nsrc: /effects/edge-detect/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Detects contrast in a black and white image and makes a mask of the edges; works best on high-contrast input.\nk: Edge Width | Width of the detected areas around edges (1 to 16).\nk: Edge Roundness | Rounds, blurs and smooths the mask (0 to 16).\nk: Invert | Inverts the result.\nk: Tolerance | Threshold for where edges appear.\nuse: Edge wear masks from a height or tile pattern, outlines for chipping and paint wear; chain with Histogram Scan to control hardness.\ncop: @edgedetect (set {Method} to Sobel, {Blur Before} to soften, {High Threshold}), widened with @dilateerode ({Radius}) and rounded with @blur; the invert toggle is @invert.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## emboss-with-gloss\nname: Emboss With Gloss\nsrc: /effects/emboss-with-gloss/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Fake baked lighting with a specular highlight, computed from a height input and applied to a colour input.\nk: Highlight Color | Colour of the specular highlight.\nk: Shadow Color | Colour of unlit areas.\nk: Gloss | Size of the gloss highlight.\nk: Intensity | Intensity of the highlight.\nk: Light Angle | Light incidence angle.\nuse: Stylised baked lighting; also a quick way to preview a height with directional light.\ncop: @heighttonormal then @light ({Directional} on, {Light Direction}, {Diffuse}, {Specular}, {Exponent}, {Intensity}) multiplied over the colour layer; shadows via @heighttoshadow.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## uber-emboss\nname: Uber Emboss\nsrc: /effects/uber-emboss/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Feature-rich emboss that fakes diffuse, ambient and specular lighting plus shadows from a height map and a colour input.\nk: Ambient Color | Colour in shadowed areas.\nk: Diffuse Color | Colour in lit areas.\nk: Specular Color | Colour of reflections.\nk: Light Intensity | Intensity of the faked light.\nk: Light Angle | Light incidence angle.\nk: Specular Intensity | Strength of reflections.\nk: Specular Glossiness | Size of the highlight.\nk: Diffuse Roughness | Roughness of the diffuse term.\nk: Shadows Opacity | Blend opacity of the shadows.\nuse: Baked-lighting looks and a fast visual check of a height under a low light.\ncop: @heighttonormal, @light ({Model}=Lambertian or Phong, {Diffuse}, {Specular}, {Exponent}) and @heighttoshadow, composited with @blend (Multiply).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## extend-shape\nname: Extend Shape\nsrc: /effects/extend-shape/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Extends a section of the input over a set direction and distance, as if stretching a slice of the image.\nk: Mode | Defines the parameters used for the extension (bidirectional or from start and end positions).\nk: Extension Distance | Distance over which the section is extended.\nk: Extension Position | Position of the section to extend.\nk: Extension Angle | Angle of the section to extend.\nk: Start Luminance Offset | Luminance offset before the extended section.\nk: End Luminance Offset | Luminance offset after the extended section.\nk: Filtering Mode | Interpolation mode when sampling.\nuse: Stretching a profile to make long extrusions such as beams, rails or grooves from a single slice.\ncop: @distort with a constant direction ({Direction Type}=Angle, {Streak}=Maximum or Blur) restricted by a mask strip through {i:mask}; or sample one row repeatedly with @sample from a UV layer where V is collapsed (UNVERIFIED).\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## diffusion-grayscale\nname: Diffusion Grayscale\nsrc: /effects/diffusion-grayscale/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: medium\npurpose: Diffuses the values of masked pixels outward to create smooth gradations; only masked pixels take part in the result.\nk: Iterations | Number of diffusion passes (more is better but slower).\nk: Distance | Maximum reach of the diffusion.\nk: Enable Dithering | Sampling method that converges in fewer passes but adds noise.\nuse: Filling gaps in sparse height samples, smooth interpolation between known heights, soft inpainting of masked areas.\ncop: @smoothfill (smoothly fills a region of a layer, with {Iterations}) or @extrapolateboundaries with {Exterior}=Diffuse Fill and {Diffuse Iterations}; for exact interpolation use @solvepoisson.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## diffusion-color\nname: Diffusion Color\nsrc: /effects/diffusion-color/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Colour version of Diffusion: smooth gradations between masked colour samples.\nk: Iterations | Number of passes.\nk: Distance | Maximum reach.\nk: Is Normal Map | Normalises values at every step for normal maps.\nk: Use Alpha as Mask | Uses the source alpha as the diffusion mask.\nuse: Filling holes in scanned colour or normal maps.\ncop: @extrapolateboundaries ({Exterior}=Diffuse Fill) or @smoothfill on an RGB layer.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## diffusion-uv\nname: Diffusion UV\nsrc: /effects/diffusion-uv/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Diffuses UV coordinates from masked pixels, interpolating coordinates between the source values.\nk: Iterations | Number of passes.\nuse: Seamless UV fills for atlas padding.\ncop: @adjacency_extrapolate (fills areas outside UV islands from their neighbours) or @extrapolateboundaries on a UV layer.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## glow\nname: Glow\nsrc: /effects/glow/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Outer-glow effect adding a fading gradient outline around the input; made for binary black and white shapes, not for alpha images.\nk: Glow Amount | Global opacity of the glow.\nk: Clear Amount | Threshold to cut off the glow in semi-transparent areas.\nk: Glow Size | How far the glow reaches (0 to 20).\nk: Glow Color | Colour of the glow (colour version).\nuse: Soft halos around masks, softened shape edges, fake light bloom.\ncop: @glow ({Glow Threshold}, {Size}, {Brightness}, {Output Glow Only}) or @dilateerode with {Soft Edge} plus @blur on the mask.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## shape-glow\nname: Shape Glow\nsrc: /effects/shape-glow/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Soft glow around a mask (grayscale) or a shape with alpha (colour), more complete than Glow.\nk: Mode | Soft or precise.\nk: Width | How far the glow reaches.\nk: Spread | Cut-off that makes the glow look solid near the shape.\nk: Opacity | Blend opacity.\nuse: Soft shape halos for masks and stylised looks.\ncop: @monotosdf then @sdftomono with a falling {Remap Ramp} for the glow profile (or @glow).\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## shape-drop-shadow\nname: Shape Drop Shadow\nsrc: /effects/shape-drop-shadow/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Classic drop shadow for a mask (grayscale version) or an image with transparency (colour version).\nk: Angle | Light incidence angle.\nk: Distance | Offset of the shadow from the shape.\nk: Size | Blur of the shadow.\nk: Spread | Cut-off that makes the shadow reach further.\nk: Opacity | Blend opacity of the shadow.\nuse: Raised plates, embossed shapes and faked contact shadows on masks.\ncop: @dropshadow ({Mode}=Angle and Distance, {Angle}, {Distance}, {Blurring}, {Expansion}).\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## shape-stroke\nname: Shape Stroke\nsrc: /effects/shape-stroke/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: medium\npurpose: Adds a stroke or outline around a mask (grayscale) or a shape with alpha (colour); described as a more complete Edge Detect.\nk: Width | Width of the stroke (negative values go inwards).\nk: Opacity | Global opacity of the stroke.\nuse: Outlines, borders and joint lines around tiles or stamps.\ncop: @monotosdf then @sdftomono with {Draw Outline} on ({Outline Width}, {Outline Value}, {Alignment}), or @edgedetect combined with @dilateerode.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## shadows-filter-node\nname: Shadows\nsrc: shadows-filter-node.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Raw grayscale-only version of Shape Drop Shadow that takes binary shapes and returns only the shadow.\nk: Shadow Distance | How far the shadow falls.\nk: Light Angle | Light incidence angle.\nk: Edges Softness | Hardness of the shadow edges.\nk: Samples | Quality for the edge softness.\nuse: Baked-in shadow layers when building your own lighting.\ncop: @dropshadow with {Output Drop Shadow Only} on.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## rt-shadow\nname: RT Shadows\nsrc: /effects/rt-shadow/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Ray-traced shadows from a height map, with a movable light and soft shadows; not meant for the CPU engine.\nk: Samples | Number of rays (smoother with more).\nk: Mode | How shadows are drawn on the surface.\nk: Height Scale | Multiplier of the input height.\nk: Light Position | Position of the light on a sphere around the surface.\nk: Light Intensity | Light intensity.\nk: Light Size | Size of the light source (shaded mode).\nk: Shadow Opacity | Opacity of the shadows.\nk: Shadow Attenuation | Attenuation of shadows with distance from the caster.\nk: Max Shadows Length | Maximum shadow length.\nuse: Cast shadows to read the relief of a height map, shadow masks for dirt in crevices, light studies.\ncop: @heighttoshadow: {Type}=Directional (or Disk or Sphere for soft shadows with {Radius}/{Angular Size}), light direction by {Altitude} and {Azimuth}, {Height Map Scale}, {Single Sided}, {View Radius} and {Step Scale} for reach and accuracy.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## rt-irradiance\nname: RT Irradiance\nsrc: /effects/rt-irradiance/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Ray-traced irradiance on a height map from an environment map and an emissive map, used to bake fake global illumination and glow.\nk: Height Scale | Scale at which the height is interpreted.\nk: Quality | Ray count (more is less noisy).\nk: Compute Bounces | Toggles bounced light.\nk: Environment Rotation | Rotates the environment.\nk: Environment Exposure (EV) | Exposure of the environment.\nk: Emissive Intensity | Multiplier of the emissive input.\nuse: Baked bounce light and glow for stylised or emissive materials.\ncop: No direct node. Approximate with @heighttoambientocclusion for ambient light and @heighttoshadow plus @light for directional components, and @glow for emissive bleeding. UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## curvature-filter-node\nname: Curvature\nsrc: curvature-filter-node.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Simple, harsh single-pass curvature from a normal map; convex areas come out white and concave areas black with pixel-thin lines.\nk: Intensity | Intensity of the effect (increases contrast).\nk: Normal Format | DirectX or OpenGL green channel convention.\nuse: Quick edge highlights and cavity masks (edge wear, dirt in crevices) from a normal map.\ncop: @curvature on the height layer directly ({Curvature Type}, {Output Type}=Convexity or Concavity, {Scale}, {Kernel Size}); from a normal layer first reconstruct a height with @normaltoheight (or compute from the normal derivative). The pixel-thin line character is UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## curvature-sobel\nname: Curvature Sobel\nsrc: /effects/curvature-sobel/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Single-pass curvature from a normal map using a Sobel kernel; similar to Curvature but with thicker lines.\nk: Intensity | Intensity of the effect, adjusts contrast.\nk: Normal type | DirectX or OpenGL.\nuse: Thicker edge-wear masks and highlight maps.\ncop: @curvature with a larger {Kernel Size} (thicker lines) or @edgedetect with {Method}=Sobel on the height.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## curvature-smooth\nname: Curvature Smooth\nsrc: /effects/curvature-smooth/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Smooth curvature computed from a normal map, with separate convexity and concavity outputs; flat areas are 50 percent grey.\nk: Normal format | Format of the input normal map.\nuse: Smooth cavity and edge masks; convexity for edge wear, concavity for dirt accumulation.\ncop: @curvature ({Output Type}=Curvature, Convexity or Concavity, {Method}=Finite Difference or Angle Deficit, {Normalize}, {Minimum}, {Maximum}); the three SD outputs correspond to the three {Output Type} choices.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## cross-section\nname: Cross Section\nsrc: /effects/cross-section/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: medium\npurpose: Draws the cross-sectional profile of an input along a horizontal or vertical slice; useful for inspecting a height profile.\nk: Cross section coordinate | Coordinate of the slice.\nk: Section axis | Vertical or horizontal slice.\nk: Show helper | Overlay showing where the slice is taken.\nk: Height scale | Scales the graph vertically.\nk: Height offset | Shifts the graph up or down.\nk: Drawing style | Solid fill or line.\nuse: Verifying the shape of bevels, grooves and falloffs in a height graph.\ncop: No dedicated node. Read one row with @crop or @sample on a UV line and draw the profile with @wrangle, or inspect with the Composite Viewer pixel probe. UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mosaic\nname: Mosaic\nsrc: /effects/mosaic/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: medium\npurpose: Facetises a smooth, sloping gradient map through a multi-pass warp; with the same map on both inputs it grows and accentuates the brightest areas.\nk: Samples | Multi-sample quality (0 to 16).\nk: Intensity | Strength of the effect.\nuse: Adding definition to blurred heights, turning smooth blobs into faceted stone shapes.\ncop: Iterated @distort passes where the map drives the direction through @slopedir and {Streak}=Maximum, or @dilateerode (grayscale dilation) repeated; the multi-pass warp itself is UNVERIFIED.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## multi-directional-warp\nname: Multi Directional Warp\nsrc: /effects/multi-directional-warp/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Applies Directional Warp several times in opposite directions (1, 2 or 4 directions) while the displaced texture stays in place, which fixes the one-sided smear of a single Directional Warp.\nk: Intensity | How far pixels are pushed (0 to 20).\nk: Warp Angle | Direction of the warp.\nk: Mode | Blend of consecutive passes: Average, Max, Min or Chain.\nk: Directions | Number of axes (1, 2 or 4).\nuse: Wobbling and organic edge breakup of masks and heights, crack widening, eroded outlines.\ncop: @distort (SideFX lists Warp under Distort): per-pass {Direction Type}=Angle and {Scale} (use the negative sign for the opposite direction), merged with @average or @blend {Mode}=Maximum / Minimum; the per-pixel {i:scale} input accepts the Intensity map.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## non-uniform-directional-warp\nname: Non Uniform Directional Warp\nsrc: non-uniform-directional-warp.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Directional Warp whose intensity and direction come from input maps, with trails of adjustable length, fade and blend; comparable in power to Slope Blur.\nk: Intensity | Push distance of the warp (0 to 20).\nk: Warp Angle | Direction of the warp.\nk: Warp Angle Input Multiplier | Strength of the Warp Angle Input map.\nk: Trail Mode | Min, Max or Average blending of trails.\nk: Trail Length | Length of the trails.\nk: Trail Fade | Fade of each trail.\nk: Trail Curve | Behaviour of the fade.\nuse: Flowing streaks, drips and wind-blown relief driven by masks; crack and erosion shaping.\ncop: @distort with a per-pixel direction layer in {i:dir} (made from an angle map with @polartouv or from @slopedir), per-pixel {i:scale} for the intensity map, and {Streak}=Min, Maximum or Blur for the Trail Mode; trail length through {Maximum Steps} and {Pixels per Step}; {Use Streak Weight Ramp} gives the fade.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## vector-warp\nname: Vector Warp\nsrc: /effects/vector-warp/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: medium\npurpose: Distortion driven by a colour vector map (red and green hold the displacement), more powerful and versatile than Warp and Directional Warp.\nk: Intensity | Multiplier of the vector map.\nk: Vector Format | DirectX or OpenGL green channel interpretation.\nuse: Flow-map style displacement, swirling and directed smearing driven by authored vector fields.\ncop: @distort with the vector map's red and green channels as the {i:dir} input (split with @rgbtouv, which outputs a UV layer) and {Scale} as Intensity; or build a UV layer by adding the vector to @uvmap and sample with @sample.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## vector-morph\nname: Vector Morph\nsrc: /effects/vector-morph/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: medium\npurpose: Moves input pixels along vectors stored in the red and green channels of a vector map, like flow-map or normal-map UV distortion.\nk: Amount | Intensity multiplier of the vector map.\nuse: Directed displacement of masks and heights by authored vector fields.\ncop: @distort driven by a UV direction layer (@rgbtouv on the vector map) or @sample with an offset UV layer; {Scale} is Amount.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## swirl\nname: Swirl\nsrc: /effects/swirl/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Warps the image in a swirling direction with a movable centre.\nk: Amount | Strength of the swirl (-16 to 16).\nk: Offset | Offset of the swirl.\nuse: Twisted patterns, vortex shapes and curl-like distortions.\ncop: @swirl (COP node of the same name): {Translation}, {Strength}, {Bulge}, {Radius}, {Blend Region}, {Inner Radius}, {Rotate}.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## reaction-diffusion-fast\nname: Reaction Diffusion Fast\nsrc: /effects/reaction-diffusion-fast/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: medium\npurpose: Fast approximate reaction-diffusion on a grayscale image, producing organic Turing-like patterns such as spots, mazes and corals.\nk: Radius | How far the effect spreads.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the input, acting like a threshold.\nuse: Organic cell and coral relief, lichen, skin pores, giraffe-like spots.\ncop: @turingpatterns ({Iterations}, {Radius}, {Power}, {Gain}) as the single-node approximation, or a real simulation with @reactiondiffusion_block_begin and @reactiondiffusion_block_end (Gray-Scott model with presets such as Spots, Worms and Labyrinth).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## summed-area-table\nname: Summed Area Table\nsrc: summed-area-table.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Returns, for every pixel, the sum of all pixel values from the top-left corner up to that pixel (an integral image).\nnote: The documentation page lists no parameters.\nuse: Fast box filtering and large-radius averages in custom filters.\ncop: @prefixsum applied along both axes in sequence ({Operation}=Add). UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## fxaa\nname: FXAA\nsrc: /effects/fxaa/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Fast approximate anti-aliasing that smooths jagged edges of shapes such as discs.\nnote: The documentation page lists no parameters.\nuse: Cleaning pixelated mask edges before further use.\ncop: No FXAA node. Use a very small @blur, or generate at higher resolution and reduce with @resample; @sdftomono has an {Anti-Aliasing} option for SDF shapes.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## 3d-texture-position\nname: 3D Texture Position\nsrc: 3d-texture-position.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Generates the position slices of a unit cube, usable to bake 3D noises or as a 3D texture atlas.\nnote: The documentation page lists no parameters.\nuse: Baking 3D noise volumes into tileable 2D atlases.\ncop: @posmap with periodic borders per axis, tiled into slices with @contactsheet; evaluation by the 3D noise nodes such as @fractalnoise3d. UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## 3d-texture-sdf\nname: 3D Texture SDF\nsrc: /effects/3d-texture-sdf/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Builds the signed distance field of a shape from a 3D texture mask holding the slices of its volume.\nk: Threshold | Gradient value at which the shape surface is detected.\nk: Output | Type of distance field output.\nuse: Volume SDFs for 3D texture rendering.\ncop: No direct node for 3D slices; for 2D slices use @monotosdf per slice. UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## 3d-texture-surface-render\nname: 3D Texture Surface Render\nsrc: /effects/3d-texture-surface-render/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Renders the surface of a shape stored as a 3D texture distance field, with environment lighting and an optional ground plane.\nk: Output Resolution | Resolution of the render, as a power of two.\nk: Camera Position | Camera orbit around the shape.\nk: Camera Distance | Distance of the camera.\nk: Camera FOV | Field of view in degrees.\nk: Albedo | Surface colour.\nk: Enable Ground Plane | Renders a ground plane.\nuse: Previewing 3D noise volumes and shapes.\ncop: No direct node; preview geometry or volumes in the Scene Viewer or with @rasterizegeo and @light. UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## 3d-texture-volume-render\nname: 3D Texture Volume Render\nsrc: /effects/3d-texture-volume-render/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Renders the volume of a 3D texture shape with absorption and directional lighting.\nk: Output Resolution | Resolution of the render.\nk: Camera Position | Camera orbit.\nk: Light Position | Directional light position.\nk: Absorption | How much light is absorbed in the volume.\nk: Feather | Multiplies the density with the inner distance value.\nuse: Previewing cloud-like 3D noise volumes.\ncop: @rasterizevolume (renders a volume viewed through a camera) with a VDB made by @vdbfromlayer. UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## 3d-viewer\nname: 3D Viewer\nsrc: /effects/3d-viewer/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: New in Designer 16.0: renders a 3D scene described by an SDF or intersection function graph with a custom camera and environment light, mainly to author and debug SDF shapes for Shape splatter v2.\nk: Scene type | Kind of function describing the scene (SDF or intersection).\nk: Output | Type of render output (AOV).\nk: Camera mode | Perspective or other projections.\nk: Ray marching steps | Number of sphere-tracing steps.\nk: Tonemapper | Tonemapping applied to the render.\nk: SDF isolines | Shows isolines of the distance field.\nuse: Inspecting the shapes later scattered in Shape splatter v2.\ncop: Check shapes in the Scene Viewer with geometry from SOPs; there is no SDF function graph equivalent in COP (SDF shapes come from @sdfshape in 2D).\nstatus: unverified\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":626,"cache_read_input_tokens":619615,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":626,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0137pFFYEZPd4gNXE2iZGh3H":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-zenray--claude-Memory1/3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953/scratchpad/work/entries/05a_effects.txt","content":"## flood-fill\nname: Flood Fill\nsrc: /effects/flood-fill/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Analyses a binary tile map and stores, per connected shape, the data (bounding boxes, positions, sizes) that the other Flood Fill nodes turn into random values, gradients, positions or mapped patterns. It is the starting point of the Flood Fill family and is not meant to be used alone.\nk: Safety/Speed trade-off | Chooses the calculation mode for simple or small shapes versus complex or big ones, or a no-failure mode.\nk: Avanced options | Shows or hides the advanced parameters and outputs.\nk: Override Safety/Speed trade-off | Advanced override of internal behaviour for custom effects and debugging.\nuse: Per-tile randomisation of height, tilt, bevel and wear on bricks, tiles and stones; the input must be a clean binary map where tiles are separated by pure black lines (a Tile Generator output is the ideal source).\ncop: @segmentbyconnectivity (SideFX-confirmed) labels each connected region and gives an {o:id} layer ({Connectivity}=Above Threshold with {Threshold}); @uvmapbyid then derives per-island data ({Mode}=UV Map, Center, Minimum, Maximum or Size) and @statisticsbyid gives per-ID area, minimum and maximum. The per-tile variation nodes below are built from these outputs.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## flood-fill-to-random-grayscale\nname: Flood Fill to Random Grayscale\nsrc: flood-fill-to-random-grayscale.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Gives every Flood Fill tile a random grayscale value.\nnote: The documentation page lists no parameters; the seed comes from the node random seed.\nuse: Random per-tile height offsets for bricks, tiles and cobbles.\ncop: @randommono with the island ID wired into its {i:seed} input and a {Range Values} of Min/Max (SideFX lists Random Mono as the Flood Fill to Random Grayscale equivalent); segmentation from @segmentbyconnectivity.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## flood-fill-to-random-color\nname: Flood Fill to Random Color\nsrc: flood-fill-to-random-color.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Gives every Flood Fill tile a random RGB colour.\nnote: The documentation page lists no parameters.\nuse: ID colour maps for masks and visual checks of tile segmentation.\ncop: @randomrgb driven by the island ID (SideFX lists Random RGB as the equivalent), or @idtorgb on the {o:id} output of @segmentbyconnectivity.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## flood-fill-to-grayscale-color\nname: Flood Fill to Grayscale\nsrc: flood-fill-to-grayscale-color.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Uses Flood Fill data to give each tile a grayscale swatch with controllable bias and variation, optionally starting from a value sampled from an extra input map per tile.\nnote: The documentation page covers the grayscale and colour versions together (two icons).\nk: Luminance/Color Adjustment | Bias or base value of each tile; with an input map it offsets the sampled start value.\nk: Luminance/Color Random | Amount of variation between tiles.\nuse: Controlled per-tile height variation where the base height of each tile comes from a mask or a gradient.\ncop: @uvmapbyid with {Mode}=Center gives the centre of each island; @sample (UV Sample) reads the input map at that centre, @randommono (id into {i:seed}) adds variation, and @blend (Add) combines them.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## flood-fill-to-grayscale-color-colour\nname: Flood Fill to Color\nsrc: flood-fill-to-grayscale-color.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Colour swatch version of the Flood Fill to Grayscale node.\nnote: Shares the documentation page with Flood Fill to Grayscale.\nk: Luminance/Color Adjustment | Bias or base colour of each tile.\nk: Luminance/Color Random | Amount of colour variation.\nuse: Colour variation per tile for albedo; not for heights.\ncop: Same chain as Flood Fill to Grayscale with @sample on an RGB layer and @randomrgb for variation, or @hsv with a per-ID hue shift.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## flood-fill-to-gradient\nname: Flood Fill to Gradient\nsrc: /effects/flood-fill-to-gradient/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Turns every Flood Fill tile into a gradient with a random orientation, ideal for heights where tiles are randomly tilted and sloped.\nk: Angle | Uniform angle of all gradients.\nk: Angle Variation | Random angle per tile; the most useful control.\nk: Multiply by Bounding Box Size | Scales the gradient by the tile bounding box so small tiles are darker.\nk: Angle Image Input Multiplier | Influence of the optional angle map.\nk: Slope Image Input Multiplier | Influence of the optional slope map.\nk: Flat Slope Color | Value of flat slopes.\nuse: Tilted flagstones, slate roofs, wood planks with individual tilt; feed the result into Height Blend or add to the base height with a small amplitude.\ncop: @uvmapbyid ({Mode}=UV Map, {Auto Scale}) supplies per-tile UVs in 0 to 1; rotate them per tile with @uvxform ({Rotate} with a random value from the {i:seed} input, {Uniform Scale}); take the U channel with @rgbtouv or @channelextract and treat it as the gradient. UNVERIFIED chain.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## flood-fill-to-bbox-size\nname: Flood Fill to BBox Size\nsrc: flood-fill-to-bbox-size.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: medium\npurpose: Gives each tile a grayscale value tied to the size of its bounding box (relative to the whole canvas), so contrast is often low.\nk: Output | Metric used: width, height or the maximum of both.\nuse: Making large stones higher than small ones, or driving wear amount by tile size.\ncop: @uvmapbyid with {Mode}=Size (per-island bounding size), then split with @rgbtouv or @channelextract and use the maximum of X and Y with @blend {Mode}=Maximum; @statisticsbyid is an alternative for area based values.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## flood-fill-to-index\nname: Flood Fill to Index\nsrc: /effects/flood-fill-to-index/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Converts every tile to a value from its index (starting at 0 in the top-left corner), either normalised to 0 to 1 or as an unclamped integer count.\nk: Output | Normalised (0 to 1) or Integer (0 to n).\nk: Ignore Shape Smaller Than | Ignores tiny shapes.\nk: Show Flood Fill Data Table | Debug output of the Flood Fill data.\nuse: Sequential tile ordering effects, gradient across tiles, counting tiles.\ncop: @idtomono (the {Conversion} option controls casting versus safe packing) on the ID layer from @segmentbyconnectivity; divide by the count from @statistics ({o:maximum}) for the normalised variant.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## flood-fill-to-position\nname: Flood Fill to Position\nsrc: flood-fill-to-position.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: medium\npurpose: Generates a per-tile position map (tile centre in the red and green channels), meant as a base for further calculations.\nnote: The documentation page lists no parameters.\nuse: Per-tile pivots for rotation, distance from a tile centre, directional gradients per tile.\ncop: @uvmapbyid with {Mode}=Center (the output holds the centre position of each ID island).\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## flood-fill-mapper\nname: Flood Fill Mapper\nsrc: /effects/flood-fill-mapper/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Remaps an existing pattern or texture onto every Flood Fill cell, with pattern choice, scale, rotation, position and luminance randomisation; a mix of Flood Fill and Tile Sampler or Shape Mapper.\nk: Pattern Input Number | Number of custom pattern inputs (1 to 8).\nk: Pattern Distribution Mode | How a pattern is picked for a cell (random, shape size, distribution map).\nk: Size Mode | How the size of the pattern in each cell is determined (relative to texture, shape sphere, largest or smallest shape, or fit shape box).\nk: Scale | Global uniform scale.\nk: Scale Random | Random scale variation.\nk: Rotation Random | Random rotation per cell.\nk: Rotation Autoscale | Rescales the pattern to stay inside the cell when rotated.\nk: Position Offset Random | Random position offset per cell.\nk: Luminance Range | Global contrast of the texture in each cell (grayscale version).\nk: Luminance Offset | Brightness offset (grayscale version).\nuse: Putting a stone texture, grain or detail map onto each tile of a tile graph with per-tile variation, so each stone gets its own surface relief.\ncop: @uvmapbyid ({Mode}=UV Map, {Auto Scale}) gives per-cell UVs, @uvxform adds the per-cell random {Rotate}, {Uniform Scale}, {Translate} (its {i:seed} input takes the ID), and @sample (UV Sample) reads the pattern; luminance randomisation with @randommono and @blend.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## ambient-occlusion-hbao\nname: Ambient Occlusion (HBAO)\nsrc: ambient-occlusion-hbao-filter-node.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Generates an ambient occlusion map from a height map with horizon-based ambient occlusion, an algorithm designed for screen-space real-time AO; fast and simple.\nk: Use World Units | Switches from screen-space scale to world-unit controls.\nk: Height Depth | Global height scale (screen-space mode).\nk: Surface Size | Physical size of the surface (world-unit mode).\nk: Height Scale (cm) | Height scale in centimetres (world-unit mode).\nk: Radius | Spread of the AO.\nk: Quality | Number of samples (4, 8 or 16).\nk: GPU Optimization | Internal speed-up.\nuse: Cavity and crevice shading from procedural heights; AO as a mask for dirt in valleys, moss, and darkened joints; essential to judge heights visually.\ncop: @heighttoambientocclusion (SideFX-confirmed): {Height Scale} (Height Depth), {Space} (Local or World, for the world-units option), {View Radius} (Radius), {Sample Count} (Quality), {Step Scale}, {Sample from Hemisphere}, and a {Remap Ramp} to shape the occlusion falloff.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## ambient-occlusion-rtao\nname: Ambient Occlusion (RTAO)\nsrc: /effects/ambient-occlusion-rtao/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Ray-traced ambient occlusion from a height map; more accurate than HBAO but slower and not meant for the CPU engine.\nk: Use Physical Size | Uses physical size settings to determine the height scale.\nk: Physical Size | Real physical size of the surface.\nk: Samples | Number of rays (more gives smoother results).\nk: Height Scale | Multiplier of the height input.\nk: Distribution | Distribution method, affecting falloff toward shadowed areas.\nk: Maximum Distance | Maximum distance rays can travel to be occluded.\nk: Spread Angle | Spread angle of the rays (1 is a full hemisphere).\nuse: Higher-quality AO for final bakes of procedural heights, ambient shadowing for large relief.\ncop: @heighttoambientocclusion with a high {Sample Count} and a large {View Radius} (the node is described as imagining a sphere per pixel and testing how occluded it is). Ray traced alternatives exist through @raytrace on a mesh version of the height. UNVERIFIED equivalence.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## anisotropic-kuwahara\nname: Anisotropic Kuwahara Color\nsrc: /effects/anisotropic-kuwahara/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Directional blur that conforms to image details so the result appears to flow along shapes, with sharpness controls producing flatter, painterly regions.\nk: Radius | Blur radius.\nk: Smoothness | Blending of colours along the computed direction.\nk: Sharpness | Contrast of the blurred areas (flatter, cleaner areas).\nk: Anisotropy | Contribution of the direction map.\nk: Use input direction map | Uses a supplied direction map instead of computing one.\nk: Tensor smoothness | Smoothing of the computed directions.\nk: Anisotropy angle | Extra rotation of the direction map, in turns.\nuse: Painterly flow smoothing of colour scans; of limited use for heights.\ncop: @kuwaharafilter (the isotropic version); flow-aware streaking can be added with @distort driven by @slopedir. UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## anisotropic-kuwahara-grayscale\nname: Anisotropic Kuwahara Grayscale\nsrc: anisotropic-kuwahara-grayscale.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: medium\npurpose: Grayscale version of Anisotropic Kuwahara; flow-following smoothing with sharpening of flat regions.\nk: Radius | Blur radius.\nk: Smoothness | Blending along the direction.\nk: Sharpness | Flattening and sharpness.\nk: Anisotropy | Contribution of the direction map.\nuse: Smoothing scanned heights along their features while keeping ridges defined.\ncop: @kuwaharafilter on the Mono layer; optionally followed by @distort with a direction layer from @slopedir ({Streak}=Blur). UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## bevel-filter-node\nname: Bevel\nsrc: bevel-filter-node.md\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Applies an edge bevel to a grayscale height map (ideally a high-contrast binary one) and returns both the bevelled height and the matching normal map; supports exact custom curve profiles.\nk: Distance | How far the bevel reaches (negative values go the other way).\nk: Corner Type | Round or angular profile.\nk: Smoothing | Extra smoothing (blur) after the bevel.\nk: Use Non-Uniform Blur | Smoothing done non-uniformly.\nk: Use Custom Curve | Uses your own height curve for the profile.\nk: Normal Intensity | Strength of the normal output.\nk: Normal Format | DirectX or OpenGL convention.\nuse: Beveled tiles, bricks, stones and metal plates from a binary mask; the single most frequent way to give hard-surface edges to a height.\ncop: @feather (SideFX-confirmed): {Feather Direction}=Circle for Round corners (Diamond or Octagon for Angular), {Distance for Unit Change} as Distance, {Feather from High to Low} to choose inward or outward growth, then a custom profile with @remap ({Use Ramp}); normals with @heighttonormal ({Normal Type}, {Height Scale}). The SD smoothing option is an extra @blur.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## bevel-smooth\nname: Bevel Smooth\nsrc: /effects/bevel-smooth/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Draws a gradient (or flat colour) from the borders of a mask outwards, inwards or both, keeping the gradient of the nearest border where several overlap; the distance can vary along the border with a distance map.\nk: Output mode | Bevel (gradient) or other dilation modes.\nk: Direction | Which side of the border is dilated (in, out or both).\nk: Maximum distance | Distance of the dilation in normalised image space.\nk: Mask smoothness | Radius of the smoothing applied to the mask.\nk: Mask offset | Moves mask borders inwards or outwards.\nk: Mask threshold | Value used to detect the borders of the mask.\nk: Distance map multiplier | Influence of the optional distance map on the maximum distance.\nuse: Clean, smooth bevel gradients on masks without the stepping of other bevel nodes; variable bevel width from a map.\ncop: @monotosdf ({Iso} = mask threshold) then @sdftomono with a {Remap Ramp} for the bevel profile and {Iso Range} for the maximum distance; or @feather. The variable-width map can drive {Iso Range} through a remap of the SDF. UNVERIFIED chain.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## directional-distance\nname: Directional Distance\nsrc: /effects/directional-distance/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: medium\npurpose: Draws a distance gradient from the borders of a mask in a chosen direction, keeping the nearest border where gradients overlap.\nk: Output mode | How the gradient is drawn (for example inverted normalised distance).\nk: Maximum distance | Distance travelled by the gradient.\nk: Angle | Direction of the gradient in turns.\nk: Distance map multiplier | Influence of the distance map.\nk: Angle map multiplier | Influence of the angle map.\nuse: Directional shadows, drips and soft edges that fall off in one direction.\ncop: @streakblur with {Mode}=Maximum, {Direction Type}=Angle, {Length} as Maximum distance and a falling {Streak Weight} ramp (enable {Use Streak Weight}) to create the distance falloff; the per-pixel {i:direction} and {i:scalelength} inputs replace the angle and distance maps. UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## edge-detect\nname: Edge Detect\nsrc: /effects/edge-detect/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: high\npurpose: Detects contrast in a black and white image and makes a mask of the edges; works best on high-contrast input.\nk: Edge Width | Width of the detected areas around edges (1 to 16).\nk: Edge Roundness | Rounds, blurs and smooths the mask (0 to 16).\nk: Invert | Inverts the result.\nk: Tolerance | Threshold for where edges appear.\nuse: Edge wear masks from a height or tile pattern, outlines for chipping and paint wear; chain with Histogram Scan to control hardness.\ncop: @edgedetect (set {Method} to Sobel, {Blur Before} to soften, {High Threshold}), widened with @dilateerode ({Radius}) and rounded with @blur; the invert toggle is @invert.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## emboss-with-gloss\nname: Emboss With Gloss\nsrc: /effects/emboss-with-gloss/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Fake baked lighting with a specular highlight, computed from a height input and applied to a colour input.\nk: Highlight Color | Colour of the specular highlight.\nk: Shadow Color | Colour of unlit areas.\nk: Gloss | Size of the gloss highlight.\nk: Intensity | Intensity of the highlight.\nk: Light Angle | Light incidence angle.\nuse: Stylised baked lighting; also a quick way to preview a height with directional light.\ncop: @heighttonormal then @light ({Directional} on, {Light Direction}, {Diffuse}, {Specular}, {Exponent}, {Intensity}) multiplied over the colour layer; shadows via @heighttoshadow.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## uber-emboss\nname: Uber Emboss\nsrc: /effects/uber-emboss/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Feature-rich emboss that fakes diffuse, ambient and specular lighting plus shadows from a height map and a colour input.\nk: Ambient Color | Colour in shadowed areas.\nk: Diffuse Color | Colour in lit areas.\nk: Specular Color | Colour of reflections.\nk: Light Intensity | Intensity of the faked light.\nk: Light Angle | Light incidence angle.\nk: Specular Intensity | Strength of reflections.\nk: Specular Glossiness | Size of the highlight.\nk: Diffuse Roughness | Roughness of the diffuse term.\nk: Shadows Opacity | Blend opacity of the shadows.\nuse: Baked-lighting looks and a fast visual check of a height under a low light.\ncop: @heighttonormal, @light ({Model}=Lambertian or Phong, {Diffuse}, {Specular}, {Exponent}) and @heighttoshadow, composited with @blend (Multiply).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## extend-shape\nname: Extend Shape\nsrc: /effects/extend-shape/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: low\npurpose: Extends a section of the input over a set direction and distance, as if stretching a slice of the image.\nk: Mode | Defines the parameters used for the extension (bidirectional or from start and end positions).\nk: Extension Distance | Distance over which the section is extended.\nk: Extension Position | Position of the section to extend.\nk: Extension Angle | Angle of the section to extend.\nk: Start Luminance Offset | Luminance offset before the extended section.\nk: End Luminance Offset | Luminance offset after the extended section.\nk: Filtering Mode | Interpolation mode when sampling.\nuse: Stretching a profile to make long extrusions such as beams, rails or grooves from a single slice.\ncop: @distort with a constant direction ({Direction Type}=Angle, {Streak}=Maximum or Blur) restricted by a mask strip through {i:mask}; or sample one row repeatedly with @sample from a UV layer where V is collapsed (UNVERIFIED).\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## diffusion-grayscale\nname: Diffusion Grayscale\nsrc: /effects/diffusion-grayscale/\ncat: Texture filters > Effects\nrel: medium\npurpose: Diffuses the values of masked pixels outward to create smooth gradations; only masked pixels take part in the result.\nk: Iterations | Number of diffusion passes (more is better but slower).\nk: Distance | Maximum reach of the diffusion.\nk: Enable Dithering | Sampling method that converges in fewer passes but adds noise.\nuse: Filling gaps in sparse height samples, smooth interpolation between known heights, soft inpainting of masked