{"parentUuid":"63ac4e88-4585-4811-900e-48af2528abc5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a9840a94295146d85","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0185zNXC3f7wTtseaRJTLgW9","type":"tool_result","content":"== Normal Combine\n  - Technique | Integer | Sets which internal blending technique to use, trading in speed for quality. *- Whiteout (Low quality) * Channel mixer (High quality) * Detail oriented (High quality)*\n== Normal Sobel\n  - Intensity | 0.0 - 3.0 | Strength of the converted normals.\n  - Normal Format | OpenGL, DirectX | Switches between different Normalmap formats (inverts the green channel).\nNF height-normal-world-units\n#nodes 3\n=== Make It Tile Patch  [filters/tiling/make-it-tile-patch]  (Filters > Tiling)\nD: This node is a grid-based semi-random tiler. It takes an input patch and stamps it around, attempting to turn it into a tiling image without too many repetitions, based on your settings. Useful for when you have a small patch of texture and want to create a larger scale, tiling texture from it. Keep in mind that this is different from Make-It-Tile Photo, which mainly fixes up edges. To do this with an entire mater\n  P: Mask Size {0.0 - 1.0}: Size of the round mask used when stamping the patch.\n  P: Mask Precision {0.0 - 1.0}: Falloff/smoothness precision of the mask.\n  P: Mask Warping {-100.0 - 100.0}: Introduces warping at mask edges. Good for avoiding smooth, undefined transitions between patches.\n  P: Pattern size width {0.0 - 1000.0}: Changes the width of the patch non-uniformly.\n  P: Pattern size height {0.0 - 1000.0}: Changes the height of the patch non-uniformly.\n  P: Disorder {0.0 - 1.0}: Introduces translational randomness, slightly shifting patches around.\n  P: Size Variation {0.0 - 100.0}: Introduces size variation for the mask.\n  P: Octave {0 - 6}: This is the main control that determines the overal size.\n  P: Rotation {-360.0 - 360.0}: Pre-rotate