ate}, {Rotate Random}, {Contrast}, {Falloff}) is the closest COP node; @triplanarhextile applies the same stochastic idea to triplanar projections; as an alternative @shapescatter with soft disc stamps cut from the patch. SideFX lists Make It Tile under Tile Pattern and Feather.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## rgba-split\nname: RGBA Split\nsrc: rgba-split.md\ncat: Texture filters > Channels\nrel: medium\npurpose: Splits an image into separate red, green, blue and alpha grayscale images (unpacks a packed texture).\nnote: The documentation page lists no parameters.\nuse: Separating packed height, roughness and AO channels or isolating the axes of a position or world-space normal map.\ncop: @channelsplit (SideFX-confirmed): one Mono layer per channel.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## rgba-merge\nname: RGBA Merge\nsrc: rgba-merge.md\ncat: Texture filters > Channels\nrel: medium\npurpose: Packs four grayscale inputs into the four channels of one image (channel packing).\nnote: The documentation page lists four grayscale inputs and no parameters.\nuse: Packing height, roughness, metallic and AO into a single texture for engines.\ncop: @channeljoin (inputs {i:red}, {i:green}, {i:blue}, {i:alpha}, output {o:rgba}); @monotorgba is the shortcut for one Mono layer.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## alpha-merge\nname: Alpha Merge\nsrc: alpha-merge.md\ncat: Texture filters > Channels\nrel: low\npurpose: Adds an alpha channel to an RGB image (simpler than RGBA Merge).\nnote: The documentation page lists no parameters.\nuse: Masking out a colour image or giving a result transparency.\ncop: @rgbtorgba, or @channeljoin; SideFX says to use @blend with {Mode}=Add and an alpha wired into the fg or bg input.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## alpha-split\nname: Alpha Split\nsrc: alpha-split.md\ncat: Texture filters > Channels\nrel: low\npurpose: Separates the alpha from an image, returning the image without alpha and the alpha channel on its own.\nnote: The documentation page lists no parameters.\nuse: Extracting masks from images with transparency.\ncop: @rgbatorgb for the colour without alpha and @channelextract for the alpha channel.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## pre-multiplied-to-straight\nname: Pre-Multiplied to Straight\nsrc: pre-multiplied-to-straight.md\ncat: Texture filters > Channels\nrel: low\npurpose: Removes pre-multiplied colour from the RGB of alpha-blended edges, removing fringes (and strips alpha in the process).\nnote: The documentation page lists no parameters.\nuse: Cleaning edges of decals or cut-out shapes.\ncop: @premult with un-premultiply selected.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## straight-to-pre-multiplied\nname: Straight to Pre-multiplied\nsrc: straight-to-pre-multiplied.md\ncat: Texture filters > Channels\nrel: low\npurpose: Converts a straight alpha image to pre-multiplied.\nnote: The documentation page lists no parameters.\nuse: Preparing images for correct alpha blending.\ncop: @premult (premultiply).\nstatus: unverified\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3220,"cache_read_input_tokens":656958,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3220,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01P3qPhFpFC9QFKDy78FGMJZ":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-zenray--claude-Memory1/3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953/scratchpad/work/entries/06_normal_tiling_channels.txt","content":"## normal-sobel\nname: Normal Sobel\nsrc: normal-sobel.md\ncat: Texture filters > Normal map\nrel: high\npurpose: Converts a height map to a normal map with Sobel sampling, a slightly more advanced version of the atomic Normal node.\nk: Intensity | Strength of the converted normals (0 to 3).\nk: Normal Format | OpenGL or DirectX green channel convention.\nuse: Normal map from a procedural