{"parentUuid":"2b239cef-7b47-4f98-b73b-32440eefe464","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a9840a94295146d85","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvdRNHrePH94Dom6SEd3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016sVtk3YVYRhnSdjV1oA7Dq","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-zenray--claude-Memory1/3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953/scratchpad/work/entries/07_transforms_blending.txt","content":"## safe-transform\nname: Safe Transform\nsrc: /transforms/safe-transform/\ncat: Texture filters > Transforms\nrel: high\npurpose: Tiling-safe Transform 2D: scale, rotate and offset without breaking tiling and without losing pixel crispness; useful for transforming noise when sharpness matters.\nk: Tile | Scales the input down by tiling it (1 to 16).\nk: Offset Mode | Manual offset or random offset.\nk: Offset | Translation, snapped so pixels are not interpolated.\nk: Rotation | Rotation of the input.\nk: Tile Safe Rotation | Snaps the rotation to safe values that do not blur pixels.\nk: Symmetry | Optional mirroring (none, X, Y, X+Y).\nk: Mipmap Mode | Automatic or manual mipmapping.\nk: Mipmap Level | Manual mipmap level (0 to 10).\nuse: Varying the scale or offset of a tiling noise or height while staying seamless; the standard way to reuse one noise in several scales.\ncop: @xform2d with {Border}=Wrap (tiling), {Uniform Scale} equal to 1 over Tile, {Translate} for Offset, {Rotate} (multiples of 90 degrees are lossless), and {Filter} set to a point or nearest option to avoid interpolation blur. Mipmap control has no direct switch. Exact snapping behaviour UNVERIFIED.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## non-square-transform\nname: Non-Square Transform\nsrc: /transforms/non-square-transform/\ncat: Texture filters > Transforms\nrel: medium\npurpose: Non-square-safe version of Transform 2D that detects non-square ratios and can place a square input on a non-square canvas.\nk: Tile Mode | Automatic non-square compensation or manual tiling.\nk: Tile | Tiling-safe scale in manual mode (1 to 16).\nk: Offset | Translation.\nk: Rotation | Rotation of the input.\nk: Safe Rotation (Square Only) | Snaps rotation to values that keep pixel sharpness.\nk: Background Color | Fill colour when tiling is off.\nuse: Working with rectangular heights such as planks, panels or road textures.\ncop: @xform2d (its {Units} and {Pivot Translate} help with non-square images, since COP layers carry their own aspect ratio) with {Border}=Wrap for tiling.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## skew\nname: Skew\nsrc: /transforms/skew/\ncat: Texture filters > Transforms\nrel: low\npurpose: Skews an image horizontally or vertically.\nk: Axis | Horizontal or vertical skew.\nk: Amount | Amount of skew (-1 to 1).\nk: Align | Origin of the skew (centre, top left, bottom right).\nuse: Slanting tiles, planks and shingles.\ncop: @xform2d using {Shear} and {Pivot Translate} for the Align origin.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mirror-filter-node\nname: Mirror\nsrc: /transforms/mirror-filter-node/\ncat: Texture filters > Transforms\nrel: medium\npurpose: Mirrors the input over a chosen axis from a chosen side, a quick way to get symmetry.\nk: Mode | Mirror around X, around Y or mirror a corner.\nk: Axis X Offset | Offset of the X axis.\nk: Axis Y Offset | Offset of the Y axis.\nk: Invert Axis X | Flips the X direction.\nk: Invert Axis Y | Flips the Y direction.\nk: Corner Type | Which corner to mirror from.\nuse: Symmetric ornaments, mirrored cracks, making a tile out of half a pattern.\ncop: @mirror ({Mode}=Number and Offset, {Number of Planes}, {Angle}, {Offset}, {Reverse Mirror Plane Direction}) or @flip for a full flip.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## symmetry\nname: Symmetry\nsrc: /transforms/symmetry/\ncat: Texture filters > Transforms\nrel: medium\npurpose: Symmetry operations (mirror X or Y, diagonals, combinations) with a choice of blending mode for the mirrored half; similar to Mirror with extra blending.\nk: Symmetry Mode | Geometry of the symmetry (mirror, diagonal, combined, eightfold).\nk: Transfer Mode | Blending of the mirrored half: Copy, Add, Subtract, Multiply, Add Sub, Max, Min.\nuse: Symmetrical shapes and ornaments in heights, kaleidoscopic patterns.\ncop: @mirror to create the mirrored copy and @blend to merge with {Mode} matching the Transfer Mode (Add, Subtract, Multiply, Maximum, Minimum); the copy mode is a plain overwrite.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## symmetry-slice\nname: Symmetry Slice\nsrc: /transforms/symmetry-slice/\ncat: Texture filters > Transforms\nrel: low\npurpose: Complex symmetry and mirroring node with many geometry options, blend modes and side flips; more options than Mirror and Symmetry.\nk: Symmetry Mode | Symmetry geometry or mirror line (7 options).\nk: Transfer Mode | Blend mode (7 options).\nk: Blend | Blends the original image back into the result.\nk: Flip Side | Reverses which side is the origin.\nuse: Elaborate symmetrical compositions.\ncop: @mirror with several {Number of Planes} and custom planes ({Mode}=Custom Mirror Planes) followed by @blend with {Mask} for the blend factor.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## cartesian-to-polar\nname: Cartesian To Polar\nsrc: /transforms/cartesian-to-polar/\ncat: Texture filters > Transforms\nrel: low\npurpose: Converts an image from Cartesian (X and Y) to polar coordinates (angle and radius); the reverse is Polar To Cartesian.\nnote: The documentation page lists no parameters.\nuse: Turning straight stripes into rings, radial or spiral patterns from linear ones.\ncop: Build the sampling coordinates with @uvmap, convert with @polartouv (inputs {i:angle} and {i:length}, {Angle Units}=Circles) and read the image with @sample (UV Sample); centre and radius normalisation must be matched by hand. UNVERIFIED.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## polar-to-cartesian\nname: Polar to Cartesian\nsrc: /transforms/polar-to-cartesian/\ncat: Texture filters > Transforms\nrel: low\npurpose: Converts an image in polar coordinates (angle and radius) back to Cartesian coordinates.\nnote: The documentation page lists no parameters.\nuse: Unwrapping radial patterns, making straight bands from rings.\ncop: @uvmap into @uvtopolar (outputs {o:angle} and {o:length}), recombine them with @uvtorgb into a lookup UV layer and read the image with @sample. UNVERIFIED.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## quad-transform\nname: Quad Transform\nsrc: /transforms/quad-transform/\ncat: Texture filters > Transforms\nrel: low\npurpose: Transforms the input by dragging the four corners of a quad.\nk: p00 | Top left point.\nk: p01 | Bottom left point.\nk: p10 | Top right point.\nk: p11 | Bottom right point.\nk: Culling | Hiding behaviour when corners cross.\nk: Enable Tiling | Repeats the result.\nk: Sampling | Bilinear or nearest.\nuse: Perspective-like tilting of a tile, fixing scans.\ncop: @cornerpin ({Bottom Left}, {Bottom Right}, {Top Left}, {Top Right}, {Units}).\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## trapezoid-transform\nname: Trapezoid Transform\nsrc: /transforms/trapezoid-transform/\ncat: Texture filters > Transforms\nrel: low\npurpose: Perspective-like trapezoid warp with stretch controls for the top and bottom edges.\nk: Top Stretch | Stretch or squash at the top.\nk: Bottom Stretch | Stretch or squash at the bottom.\nk: Background Color | Fill colour if tiling is off.\nk: Sampling | Bilinear or nearest.\nuse: Perspective-corrected floor tiles or roof shingles.\ncop: @cornerpin with the two top (or bottom) corners moved symmetrically inwards; @bend ({Mode}=Corners) for curved variants.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## clone-filter-node\nname: Clone\nsrc: /transforms/clone-filter-node/\ncat: Texture filters > Transforms\nrel: low\npurpose: Clones the input once to a given offset through a mask, working as a crude clone-stamp.\nk: Offset | Translation of the cloned copy.\nk: Blur Mask | Blur of the mask edge.\nuse: Patching defects in scanned heights.\ncop: @xform2d ({Translate}) on a copy, merged over the original through @blend with the mask on the {i:mask} input (softened with @blur).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## auto-crop\nname: Auto Crop\nsrc: /transforms/auto-crop/\ncat: Texture filters > Transforms\nrel: medium\npurpose: Fits the content of the input (defined by its non-black or non-transparent pixels) to the image, either centred without resizing or resized to fill.\nk: Mode | Crop square (content centred) or other crop methods.\nk: Use alpha | Uses alpha to find the content bounds instead of black pixels.\nk: Filtering Mode | Interpolation when resampling.\nuse: Normalising the framing of a stamp or shape before using it in a splatter node.\ncop: @boundrect finds the bounding rectangle of the mask ({Inside Is}, {Threshold}); then @crop (its {i:bounds} input) with {Mode}=Discard and Reframe to Crop and finally @resample to the desired size.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## noise-upscale-1\nname: Noise Upscale 1\nsrc: /transforms/noise-upscale-1/\ncat: Texture filters > Transforms\nrel: low\npurpose: Scales a noise up to double resolution while hiding tiling with an X-shaped mask and a copy blend; mostly an optimisation for graphs with heavy noises.\nk: Offset1X | Slides the top and bottom parts along X.\nk: Offset1Y | Slides the top and bottom parts along Y.\nk: Offset2X | Slides the left and right parts along X.\nk: Offset2Y | Slides the left and right parts along Y.\nuse: Cheaper large noise from a smaller one in Designer.\ncop: Usually unnecessary in COP because noise generators are resolution independent; if needed use @resample ({Resolution Scale}) and cross-fade shifted copies (@xform2d with {Border}=Wrap) with an X-shaped @ramp mask via @blend.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## noise-upscale-2\nname: Noise Upscale 2\nsrc: /transforms/noise-upscale-2/\ncat: Texture filters > Transforms\nrel: low\npurpose: Same idea as Noise Upscale 1 but blending with Max and Min, giving less contrast than the original.\nk: Offset1X | Slides the top and bottom parts along X.\nk: Offset2X | Slides the left and right parts along X.\nuse: Softer large noise from a smaller noise.\ncop: As Noise Upscale 1 with @blend {Mode}=Maximum and Minimum.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## noise-upscale-3\nname: Noise Upscale 3\nsrc: noise-upscale-3.md\ncat: Texture filters > Transforms\nrel: low\npurpose: Same idea with a user-defined mask for blending the noise on top of its original scale.\nnote: The documentation page lists a Grayscale input and a Mask input and no parameters.\nuse: Custom-masked upscale of noise.\ncop: As Noise Upscale 1 with the user mask on the {i:mask} input of @blend.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## non-uniform-rotation\nname: Non-Uniform Rotation\nsrc: /transforms/non-uniform-rotation/\ncat: Texture filters > Transforms\nrel: low\npurpose: Rotates the input by per-pixel angles from a Rotation Map (values are turns) around a pivot point that can itself come from a map.\nk: Rotation Angle Multiplier | Strength of the Rotation Map.\nk: Rotation Angle Offset | Extra rotation.\nk: Use Pivot Position Map | Uses a bitmap for the pivot position.\nk: PIvot Position | Pivot position of the rotation.\nk: Filtering Mode | Interpolation when sampling.\nuse: Swirled or per-tile rotated patterns, such as rotating each Flood Fill tile around its own centre.\ncop: Compute rotated UVs per pixel in @wrangle from @uvmap, the angle map and the pivot (for example the {Mode}=Center output of @uvmapbyid), then read with @sample. @swirl also has a per-pixel {i:rotate} input but is point based. UNVERIFIED.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## 3d-texture-offset\nname: 3D Texture Offset\nsrc: /transforms/3d-texture-offset/\ncat: Texture filters > Transforms\nrel: low\npurpose: Offsets an object stored as a 3D texture along the X, Y and Z axes.\nk: Offset | Offset in world space.\nuse: 