 a subnetwork.\n   in :  | out: \n   par: \n## input | Input | Fetches the input to a subnetwork.\n   in :  | out: \n   par: \n## rop_image | ROP Image | Writes the output of a COP network to disk.\n   in :  | out: \n   par: \n#type:     node\n#context:  cop\n#internal: monotorgb\n#icon:     COP/monotorgb\n\n= Mono to RGB =\n\n\"\"\"Converts a mono layer, VDB, or attribute into an RGB layer, VDB, or attribute.\"\"\"\n\nThis node converts a mono layer, VDB, or attribute into an RGB layer, VDB, or attribute by passing the values through a color ramp. This node uses either the __Ramp__ parameter or a `ramp` input for the ramp values.\n\nTIP:\n    You can implicitly convert mono layers to RGB by wiring them into the destination node if you don't require ramping or clamping.\n\n@parameters\n\nSignature:\n    #id: signature\n    \n    The layer type that the source accepts.\n\n    See [Signatures|/copernicus/glossary#signatures] for more information.\n\nCompute Range:\n    #id: computerange\n    Sets the __Input Min__ and __Input Max__ parameters to the minimum and maximum values of the `source` input.\n\nInput Min:\n    #id: inputmin\n\n    This value in the input corresponds with the start of the ramp.\n    \nInput Max:\n    #id: inputmax\n\n    This value of the input corresponds with the end of the ramp.\n    \nOutput Min:\n    #id: outputmin\n\n    The ramp is shifted & scaled so black (`0`) in the ramp has this intensity before being applied.\n    \nOutput Max:\n    #id: outputmax\n    \n    The ramp is shifted & scaled so white (`1`) in the ramp has this intensity before being applied.\n\nScale by Value:\n    #id: scalebyvalue","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ec01f7a6-4df7-4b2c-ab7d-1e3e25047352","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:52:13.538Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b63e4c3c-3d9d-45b8-be07-18a22108c7e5","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":fal