{"parentUuid":"0be464e9-d1db-43c5-abbb-414d14ee14f3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a9840a94295146d85","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013NHGSFCp9n6AYskz3YMPyL","type":"tool_result","content":"#type:     node\r\n#context:  cop\r\n#internal: compareblend\r\n#icon:     COP/compareblend\r\n#since:    22.0\r\n\r\n= Compare and Blend =\r\n\r\n\"\"\"Compares two pixel values on a layer, VDB, or attribute and outputs either a true or false input for that pixel.\"\"\"\r\n\r\nThis node blends between two layers, VDBs, or attributes by comparing two layers, VDBs, or attributes on a per-pixel basis.\r\n\r\nIt can be used as a pixel switcher based on specific values.\r\n\r\n\r\n@parameters\r\n\r\nSignature:\r\n    #id: signature\r\n    \r\n    The layer type that the source accepts.\r\n\r\n    See [Signatures|/copernicus/glossary#signatures] for more information.\r\n    \r\nTrue If:\r\n    #id: compare\r\n    \r\n    The condition for which a pixel will be selected from either `true` or `false` inputs.\r\n\r\n    Equal to each other (==):\r\n        If the two pixels have the same value.\r\n        \r\n    Not equal to each other (!=):\r\n        If the two pixels have different values.\r\n        \r\n    A greater than B (>):\r\n        If the first input is strictly greater than the second.\r\n        \r\n    A greater than or equal to B (>=):\r\n        If the first input is greater than or equal to the second.\r\n        \r\n    B greater than A (<):\r\n        If the first input is strictly less than the second.\r\n        \r\n    B greater than or equal to A (<=):\r\n        If the first input is less than or equal to the second.\r\n        \r\nB Value:\r\n    #id: bval\r\n    The value to compare with if the `B` input is not wired.\r\n    \r\nBias:\r\n    #id: bias\r\n    Adds bias towards `true` or `false` inputs.\r\n\r\nTolerance:\r\n    #id: tol\r\n\r\n    :include /nodes/cop/compare#tol/:  \r\n        \r\n    \r\nFalloff:\r\n    #id: falloff\r\n    \r\n    :include /nodes/cop/compare#falloff/:  \r\n        \r\n        \r\n    \r\n@inputs\r\n    true:\r\n        The layer, VDB, or attribute from which to output pixels from if at this pixel, `A` is compared to `B` and produces a true outcome.\r\n\r\n    false:\r\n        The layer, VDB, or attribute from which to output pixels from if at this pixel, `A` is compared to `B` and produces a false outcome.\r\n        \r\n    A:\r\n        A layer, VDB, or attribute.\r\n\r\n    B:\r\n        The layer, VDB, or attribute to compare with `A`.\r\n\r\n    tolerance:\r\n        A mono layer, VDB, or attribute to provide a per-pixel tolerance.\r\n\r\n@outputs\r\n    chosen:\r\n        A mix of `true` or `false` inputs depending on the result of the comparison.\r\n\r\n@related\r\n- [Node:cop/compare]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"94e65127-122e-47db-8be5-25a51950205f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:53:51.936Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b1d0c4f3-e70f-4ec8-9930-1f87b7d7b1d0","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":21,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0be464e9-d1db-43c5-abbb-414d14ee14f3","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-