{"parentUuid":"a5c41ad1-c470-47d9-8809-382a9be48405","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a9840a94295146d85","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfveFyxHt8C2RtaoTwupb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019FuRfqEx42xv9kYxZvVz7Q","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-zenray--claude-Memory1/3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953/scratchpad/work/entries/10_mesh_based.txt","content":"## mg-bottom-to-top\nname: Bottom To Top\nsrc: /mask-generators/bottom-to-top/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Mask that fades from the bottom to the top of a model using the baked position map, optionally varied by a roughness map.\nk: Level | Shifts the average level of the result.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the transition.\nk: Roughness_Variation | Amount of the roughness map blended in for variation.\nuse: Gravity-based dirt or moisture gradient on a prop; heights rarely.\ncop: Bake the position with @bakegeometrytextures (or generate it with @posmap), take the vertical axis with @channelextract and shape it with @remap ({Operation}=Remap with {Use Ramp}).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-cloth-wear\nname: Cloth Wear\nsrc: /mask-generators/cloth-wear/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Mask of frazzled cloth edges driven by a cloth detail height and a curvature map.\nk: Hard Edges Amount | Share of hard edges in the mask.\nk: Wear Softness | Blur of the worn edges.\nuse: Fraying on cloth props.\ncop: Convexity from @curvature ({Output Type}=Convexity) times the cloth height, thresholded with @remap and softened with @blur.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-dirt\nname: Dirt (Mask generator)\nsrc: /mask-generators/dirt/dirt.md\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Mask for dirt in occluded and sunken edges and corners from baked AO and curvature, with built-in or custom grunge and triplanar mapping.\nk: Dirt Level | Main amount of dirt.\nk: Dirt Contrast | Contrast of the dirt.\nk: Grunge Amount | How grungy the dirt is.\nk: Edges Masking | Removes dirt from raised edges (curvature).\nk: Use Triplanar | Triplanar grunge mapping to remove seams.\nuse: Dirt in crevices; for heights, the same logic (AO plus concavity) can drive a deposit layer.\ncop: Combine the inverted AO from @heighttoambientocclusion (or a baked AO) and concavity from @curvature ({Output Type}=Concavity) with @blend Multiply, add grunge from @grunge_layerednoise, and shape with @remap; @triplanar for seamless grunge. UNVERIFIED chain.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-dripping-rust\nname: Dripping Rust\nsrc: /mask-generators/dripping-rust/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Mask of rust flakes and specks with leaks running downwards.\nk: Rust Spreading | Amount of rust.\nk: Rust Contrast | Contrast of the specks.\nk: Spreading Smoothness | Blur of the specks.\nk: Drips Intensity | Strength and length of the drips.\nk: Drips Smoothness | Smoothing of the drips.\nk: Drips Samples Amount | Quality steps of the drips.\nuse: Rust streaks beneath edges and fasteners.\ncop: Specks from curvature and noise via @remap, drips with @distort ({Streak}=Max or Blur and a downward {Angle}) as in the Slope Blur recipe; @grunge_drips is a ready-made drip pattern.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-dust\nname: Dust (Mask generator)\nsrc: /mask-generators/dust/dust.md\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Mask for dust gathered in occluded, lowered areas that face upwards, using AO and the world-space normal.\nk: Level | Total amount of dust.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the dust.\nk: Occlusion Amount | Influence of AO.\nk: Noise Opacity | Visible amount of noise in dusty areas.\nuse: Settled dust on horizontal surfaces.\ncop: Upward facing from the Z component of the world normal (@channelextract), multiplied by AO with @blend {Mode}=Multiply, plus noise from @fractalnoise; @remap for the level and contrast.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-edge-blur\nname: Edge Blur\nsrc: /mask-generators/edge-blur/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Simple edge highlight mask from the curvature map with a blur.\nk: Level | Amount of edge highlighting.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Blur Radius | Blur on the highlighted edges.\nuse: Soft edge highlights.\ncop: @curvature convexity into @remap then @blur.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-edge-damages\nname: Edge Damages\nsrc: /mask-generators/edge-damages/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Mask of damage on raised convex edges from curvature and AO, from chipped to heavily scratched.\nk: Level | Amount of edge damage.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Damages Intensity | Shifts between a chipped, consistent look and a chaotic scratched look.\nuse: Chips on corners.\ncop: Convexity from @curvature masked by AO, broken up with @fractalnoise through @blend and thresholded with @remap.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-edge-dirt\nname: Edge Dirt\nsrc: /mask-generators/edge-dirt/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Dirt accumulating around edges based on curvature alone, with large-scale variation.\nk: Level | Amount of dirt.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Variation | Amount of large-scale breakup.\nk: Override variation mask | Uses a custom variation input.\nuse: Grime on edges.\ncop: @curvature plus a low-frequency @fractalnoise variation multiplied in, then @remap.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-edge-notch\nname: Edge Notch\nsrc: /mask-generators/edge-notch/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Mask of raised edges broken up with a high-frequency noise.\nk: Level | Level of the effect.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nuse: Nicked edges.\ncop: Convexity from @curvature minus fine noise (@fractalnoise with a small {Element Size}) via @blend {Mode}=Subtract.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-edge-select\nname: Edge Select\nsrc: /mask-generators/edge-select/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Selects convex and concave edges from curvature with separate width, softness and intensity.\nk: Level | Total amount of edge highlighting.\nk: Contrast | Contrast for both edge types.\nk: Convex Edges Width | Width of convex edge highlighting.\nk: Convex Softness | Softness of convex edges.\nk: Convex Intensity | Maximum convex intensity.\nk: Concave Edges Width | Width of concave edges.\nk: Concave Softness | Softness of concave edges.\nk: Concave Intensity | Maximum concave intensity.\nuse: Clean masks for edge wear (convex) and cavity dirt (concave).\ncop: @curvature with {Output Type}=Convexity and Concavity (two nodes), each shaped by @remap ({Operation}=Threshold with a {Width} for softness).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-edge-speckle\nname: Edge Speckle\nsrc: /mask-generators/edge-speckle/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Edge highlight mask with a speckle added to break it up.\nk: Level | Total amount of highlighting.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Edge selection | Influence of convex edges.\nk: Variation | Extent to which the variation mask breaks up the effect.\nuse: Chipped paint specks along edges.\ncop: Convexity from @curvature multiplied by a speckle mask from @fractalnoise thresholded with @remap.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-edge-wear\nname: Edge Wear\nsrc: /mask-generators/edge-wear/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: General wear mask on object edges with level, threshold, width and disorder controls.\nk: Level | Total spread of the effect.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Threshold | Similar to level, total spread.\nk: Edges Width | Fullness of the highlighting.\nk: Disorder | Noise blended in to break up the smoothness.\nuse: Edge wear on props, similar logic usable on heights (edge detect of a height plus noise).\ncop: @curvature (convexity) or @edgedetect on the height, @dilateerode for the width, and @fractalnoise broken in via @blend; @remap with {Threshold} for the level.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-fiber-glass-edge-wear\nname: Fiber Glass Edge Wear\nsrc: /mask-generators/fiber-glass-edge-wear/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Wear mask with a fibreglass-like pattern (possibly cloth) along edges, with AO masking and curvature weight.\nk: Wear Level | Progressively reveals the wear.\nk: Wear Contrast | Contrast of the effect.\nk: Edges Smoothness | Bleed from highlighted edges.\nk: Grunge Amount | Amount of fibre pattern between the edges.\nk: Ambient Occlusion Masking | Influence of AO on hiding the effect.\nk: Curvature Weight | Influence of convex edges.\nuse: Composite or fibreglass worn edges.\ncop: Convexity wear as in Edge Wear, multiplied with a fibre pattern made by @streakblur on noise or @weave.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-grease\nname: Grease\nsrc: /mask-generators/grease/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Skin-grease type mask for characters, based on a thickness map and noise.\nk: Level | Total amount of effect.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Thickness Threshold | Minimum thickness at which the effect appears.\nk: Override Noise | Uses a custom noise input.\nuse: Oily skin highlights.\ncop: Thickness threshold with @remap and a noise multiplier through @blend.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-ground-dirt\nname: Ground Dirt\nsrc: /mask-generators/ground-dirt/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Dirt that has accumulated from the ground upwards (opposite of Bottom To Top or Dust), from the position map.\nk: Level | Total appearance level.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Dirt Height | Proportional height up to which dirt appears.\nuse: Muddy lower parts of props.\ncop: Inverted vertical position ramp, as in Bottom To Top, through @remap.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-leaks\nname: Leaks (Mask generator)\nsrc: /mask-generators/leaks/leaks.md\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Leaking streaks of dirt and grime from sharp edges, built with baked position, curvature, AO and world normal.\nk: Level | Total level; also affects streak length.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Variation | Large-scale variation masking the streaks.\nk: Lenght | Length of the streak drips.\nk: Occlude | Direction in which AO affects the streaks.\nuse: Streaks below edges.\ncop: @grunge_leakingstreaks or @distort with a downward angle and {Streak}=Max applied to an edge mask from @curvature.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-leather-wear\nname: Leather Wear\nsrc: /mask-generators/leather-wear/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Wear mask with a leather pattern, stronger on edges based on curvature.\nk: Wear Level | Global wear level.\nk: Wear Contrast | Contrast of the effect.\nk: Grunge Amount | Amount of leather pattern between the edges.\nk: Ambient Occlusion Masking | AO masking of the wear.\nk: Curvature Weight | Influence of the edges.\nuse: Worn leather props.\ncop: Edge wear (convexity) multiplied by a cracked leather pattern from @cellularnoise ({o:border} thresholded).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-light\nname: Light (Mask generator)\nsrc: /mask-generators/light/light.md\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Fake lighting mask purely from the world-space normal map and two light angles.\nk: Horizontal Angle | Horizontal angle of the fake light.\nk: Vertical Angle | Vertical angle of the fake light.\nk: Highlight Glossiness | Falloff spread of the highlight.\nk: Highlight Level | Brightness of the highlight.\nuse: Sun-facing masks.\ncop: @dot of the world normal with a light direction constant, shaped by @remap or @gamma.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-mask-builder\nname: Mask Builder\nsrc: /mask-generators/mask-builder/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: All-in-one mask builder based on baked maps and several grunge inputs (the Designer version of the Painter Mask Builder).\nk: Level | Total level, gradually revealing.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Invert | Inverts the result.\nk: Use Triplanar | Triplanar projection to avoid seams with grunges.\nk: Triplanar Blending Contrast | Contrast of the triplanar blend.\nuse: Layered procedural masks on props.\ncop: A stack of @remap, @blend and @fractalnoise or @grunge_* operations on baked curvature, AO and normal maps; @maskcombine merges several masks into one.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-metal-edge-wear\nname: Metal Edge Wear\nsrc: /mask-generators/metal-edge-wear/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Edge wear mask for metal with scratches and chips on convex edges, masked by AO and grunge.\nk: Wear Level | Total amount of wear, gradually revealed.\nk: Wear Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Edges Smoothness | Smoothness of the falloff from the edges.\nk: Grunge Amount | Grunge blended in between edges.\nk: Grunge Scale | Scale of the grunge.\nk: Ambient Occlusion Masking | AO masking of the effect.\nk: Curvature Weight | Influence of convex edges.\nuse: Painted metal chips.\ncop: As Edge Wear with grunge from @grunge_galvanizedsteel or @grunge_layerednoise.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-paint-wear\nname: Paint Wear\nsrc: /mask-generators/paint-wear/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Paint chipping and wearing away from edges.\nk: Level | Total amount of paint wear.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Occlusion | AO influence preventing wear in dark areas.\nk: Radius | How far the chipping spreads from convex edges.\nk: Variation | Amount of grunge blended in.\nuse: Chipped paint on metal and wood.\ncop: Convexity from @curvature expanded with @dilateerode, broken up by @fractalnoise, thresholded with @remap.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-selective-dirt\nname: Selective Dirt\nsrc: /mask-generators/selective-dirt/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Simple dirt effect on convex edges.\nk: Level | Total level of the effect.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Variation | Grunge blended into the effect.\nuse: Edge grime.\ncop: @curvature convexity multiplied by noise, shaped with @remap.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-sun-bleach\nname: Sun Bleach\nsrc: /mask-generators/sun-bleach/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Light bleaching and fading on top of surfaces, from the world normal with AO support.\nk: Level | Total amount of bleaching.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Occlusion | AO influence.\nuse: Sun-faded colour on props.\ncop: As Light with an AO multiplication (@blend Multiply).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-surface-brush\nname: Surface Brush\nsrc: /mask-generators/surface-brush/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Metal-brushing scratch effect on an object surface occluded by geometry and AO.\nk: Level | Global level.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Scratches Lenght | Length of the scratches.\nk: Occlude Axis | Axis receiving scratches.\nk: Occlusion | AO strength on occluding scratches.\nk: Sharpen Intensity | Post-sharpening of the scratches.\nuse: Brushed metal look in masks.\ncop: @streakblur on noise (long {Length}) masked by AO and the axis component of the position map.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## cracks-weathering\nname: Cracks Weathering\nsrc: /weathering/cracks-weathering/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Weathering\nrel: medium\npurpose: Full-material effect adding a random crack pattern with spread and depth controls across multiple channels.\nk: Cracks Propagation | How far the cracks spread; the main control.\nk: Cracks Depth | Depth of the cracks (mostly height).\nk: Normal Format | DirectX or OpenGL.\nuse: Cracked paint, dry earth and damaged plaster; the crack depth is subtracted from the height channel.\ncop: Crack mask from @cellularnoise ({o:border} thresholded by @remap) or @worleynoise {o:border}; subtract from the height with @blend {Mode}=Subtract and recompute normals with @heighttonormal; channels carried as a cable.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## fabric-weathering\nname: Fabric Weathering\nsrc: /weathering/fabric-weathering/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Weathering\nrel: low\npurpose: Full-material fabric wear effect with age and dirtiness controls (needs baked AO and world-space normals).\nk: Dust | Darker dust on upward-facing areas.\nk: Dirtiness | Global dirt based on occlusion.\nk: Edges Wearing | Intensifies edges.\nk: Used | Very dark accumulated dirt in creases.\nk: Age | Global tiling wear pattern.\nk: Old Fabric Brightness | Brightness of the age effect.\nuse: Worn cloth props.\ncop: Per-channel blends of masks derived from AO and the world normal (see Dust and Dirt mask generators).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## leather-weathering\nname: Leather Weathering\nsrc: /weathering/leather-weathering/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Weathering\nrel: low\npurpose: Full-material leather wear effect (dust, dirt, edges, age, cracks) tuned for leather.\nk: Dust | Upward dust.\nk: Dirtiness | Global dirt.\nk: Age | Wear pattern.\nk: Cracks Scale | Scale of the cracks.\nk: Used Leather Brightness | Brightness of the used leather effect.\nuse: Aged leather props.\ncop: As Fabric Weathering with a crack pattern from @cellularnoise.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## metal-weathering\nname: Metal Weathering\nsrc: /weathering/metal-weathering/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Weathering\nrel: low\npurpose: Full-material metal ageing: dust, dirt, edge wear, paint peeling, rust or verdigris and scratches.\nk: Paint Peeling | Amount of peeled paint.\nk: Rust | Amount of rust.\nk: Rust Peeling | Peeling of the rust layer.\nk: Rust Verdigris | Chooses rust or verdigris.\nk: Paint Cracks Scale | Scale of the paint cracks.\nk: Raw Metal Color | Colour of the exposed metal.\nuse: Aged metal props; peeling paint heights subtract from the paint layer.\ncop: Paint layer height minus a peel mask (cracks plus noise thresholded with @remap) and a rust deposit layer added with @blend; @grunge_rust and @grunge_rustysurface give rust patterns.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## moss-weathering\nname: Moss Weathering\nsrc: /weathering/moss-weathering/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Weathering\nrel: low\npurpose: Overgrown moss full-material effect with a single propagation control, best with baked position and height maps.\nk: Moss Propagation | Spread of the moss.\nk: Normal Format | DirectX or OpenGL.\nuse: Moss on rocks and walls.\ncop: Moss mask from AO, upward normal and noise (@fractalnoise, @heighttoambientocclusion); moss height as a fine noise added over the base with @blend Add.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## rock-weathering\nname: Rock Weathering\nsrc: /weathering/rock-weathering/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Weathering\nrel: low\npurpose: Full-material rock ageing: dust, dirtiness, edge wear, cracks, age and scratches.\nk: Dust | Upward dust.\nk: Dirtiness | Global dirt.\nk: Edges Wearing | Edge intensification.\nk: Used Rock | Dark accumulated dirt in creases.\nk: Cracks Scale | Scale of the cracks.\nk: Cracks Intensity | Strength of the cracks.\nk: Age | Wear pattern.\nuse: Aged stone props.\ncop: As Cracks Weathering plus the dust and dirt masks; edges via @curvature.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## rust-weathering\nname: Rust Weathering\nsrc: /weathering/rust-weathering/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Weathering\nrel: low\npurpose: Full-material rust effect with spreading, varnish damage and drips.\nk: Rust Spreading | Amount of rust.\nk: Spreading Smoothness | Blur of rust specks.\nk: Vernish Damage Scale | Scale of the varnish damage.\nk: Drips Intensity | Strength of rust drips.\nk: Drips Smoothness | Smoothing of drips.\nuse: Rusty metal props.\ncop: @grunge_rust / @grunge_rustysurface patterns with @distort drips, merged into the channels with @blend.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mesh-3d-planar-projection\nname: 3D Planar Projection\nsrc: /utilities-mesh-based-gen/3d-planar-projection/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Utilities\nrel: low\npurpose: Planar projection based on baked position and world normal maps, to place decals across UV seams.\nk: Project Input | Whether the projection position is given in UV or world space.\nk: Rotation | Rotation of the projected texture.\nk: Scale | Global scale.\nk: Maximum Depth | How deep the projection appears.\nk: Normal Threshold | Threshold for surfaces not aligned with the projection.\nuse: Decals and wear overlays across seams.\ncop: @triplanar with only one axis texture, or @possample (samples a texture by position) combined with a mask from @dot of the normal and the projection direction.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mesh-tri-planar\nname: Tri Planar\nsrc: /utilities-mesh-based-gen/tri-planar/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Utilities\nrel: low\npurpose: Triplanar projection in 2D from baked position and world-space normal data, converting UV coordinates into mostly seam-free mapping.\nk: Projection | Which axes are blended.\nk: Image Inputs | One map for all axes or one per axis.\nk: Blending Mode | Linear or advanced blending.\nk: Blending Contrast | Contrast of the transitions.\nk: Texture Tiling | Tiling of the inputs.\nk: Global Rotation | Rotation of all axes.\nuse: Seamless detail on meshes (rock height on a boulder).\ncop: @triplanar (SideFX: textures projected on X, Y, Z onto a position layer; inputs {i:position}, {i:x_texture}, {i:y_texture}, {i:z_texture}) or @triplanarhextile to hide repetition.\ngray: Grayscale version.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mesh-material-mesh-data-blender\nname: Material Mesh Data Blender\nsrc: material-mesh-data-blender\ncat: Mesh based generators > Utilities\nrel: low\npurpose: Modifies a full material with all baked maps (AO, curvature, height, normal, vertex colour, world normal) through many blend sliders.\nk: Channels | Material channels affected.\nk: Diffuse AO | AO blended into diffuse.\nk: Base Color Sharp edges | Curvature blended into base colour.\nk: Normal Material Intensity | Strength of the baked normal.\nk: Height Material Intensity | Blend of baked height with the material height.\nk: Height Material Blending Type | Reinforce or interpolation.\nuse: Adding mesh-level detail to a tiling material.\ncop: Per channel @blend with the baked maps (@combinenormals for the normal, @blend Add or Maximum for heights).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mesh-material-selector\nname: Material Selector\nsrc: /utilities-mesh-based-gen/material-selector/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Utilities\nrel: low\npurpose: Converts a colour ID map into a black and white mask by picking and combining colours.\nk: Materials | Number of materials combined.\nk: Fuzziness | Blend with neighbouring colours.\nk: Padding | Sharpness of the transition.\nuse: Masks from material ID bakes.\ncop: @chromakey or @idtomask per colour, merged with @maskcombine.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mesh-data-combiner\nname: Mesh Data Combiner\nsrc: /utilities-mesh-based-gen/mesh-data-combiner/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Utilities\nrel: low\npurpose: Packs baked mesh data (AO, UV masks, curvature, height, position, thickness, normal, colour ID, world-space direction and normal) into one group for compact material mode.\nk: Ambient Occlusion | Includes the AO map.\nk: Curvature | Includes the curvature map.\nk: Height | Includes the height map.\nk: Position (RGB) | Includes the position map.\nuse: Wiring many baked inputs at once.\ncop: @cablepack combines the baked layers into one cable and @cableunpack extracts them; the baking itself is @bakegeometrytextures.\nstatus: unverified\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2924,"cache_read_input_tokens":773060,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2924,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019FuRfqEx42xv9kYxZvVz7Q":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-zenray--claude-Memory1/3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953/scratchpad/work/entries/10_mesh_based.txt","content":"## mg-bottom-to-top\nname: Bottom To Top\nsrc: /mask-generators/bottom-to-top/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Mask that fades from the bottom to the top of a model using the baked position map, optionally varied by a roughness map.\nk: Level | Shifts the average level of the result.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the transition.\nk: Roughness_Variation | Amount of the roughness map blended in for variation.\nuse: Gravity-based dirt or moisture gradient on a prop; heights rarely.\ncop: Bake the position with @bakegeometrytextures (or generate it with @posmap), take the vertical axis with @channelextract and shape it with @remap ({Operation}=Remap with {Use Ramp}).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-cloth-wear\nname: Cloth Wear\nsrc: /mask-generators/cloth-wear/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Mask of frazzled cloth edges driven by a cloth detail height and a curvature map.\nk: Hard Edges Amount | Share of hard edges in the mask.\nk: Wear Softness | Blur of the worn edges.\nuse: Fraying on cloth props.\ncop: Convexity from @curvature ({Output Type}=Convexity) times the cloth height, thresholded with @remap and softened with @blur.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-dirt\nname: Dirt (Mask generator)\nsrc: /mask-generators/dirt/dirt.md\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Mask for dirt in occluded and sunken edges and corners from baked AO and curvature, with built-in or custom grunge and triplanar mapping.\nk: Dirt Level | Main amount of dirt.\nk: Dirt Contrast | Contrast of the dirt.\nk: Grunge Amount | How grungy the dirt is.\nk: Edges Masking | Removes dirt from raised edges (curvature).\nk: Use Triplanar | Triplanar grunge mapping to remove seams.\nuse: Dirt in crevices; for heights, the same logic (AO plus concavity) can drive a deposit layer.\ncop: Combine the inverted AO from @heighttoambientocclusion (or a baked AO) and concavity from @curvature ({Output Type}=Concavity) with @blend Multiply, add grunge from @grunge_layerednoise, and shape with @remap; @triplanar for seamless grunge. UNVERIFIED chain.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-dripping-rust\nname: Dripping Rust\nsrc: /mask-generators/dripping-rust/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Mask of rust flakes and specks with leaks running downwards.\nk: Rust Spreading | Amount of rust.\nk: Rust Contrast | Contrast of the specks.\nk: Spreading Smoothness | Blur of the specks.\nk: Drips Intensity | Strength and length of the drips.\nk: Drips Smoothness | Smoothing of the drips.\nk: Drips Samples Amount | Quality steps of the drips.\nuse: Rust streaks beneath edges and fasteners.\ncop: Specks from curvature and noise via @remap, drips with @distort ({Streak}=Max or Blur and a downward {Angle}) as in the Slope Blur recipe; @grunge_drips is a ready-made drip pattern.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-dust\nname: Dust (Mask generator)\nsrc: /mask-generators/dust/dust.md\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Mask for dust gathered in occluded, lowered areas that face upwards, using AO and the world-space normal.\nk: Level | Total amount of dust.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the dust.\nk: Occlusion Amount | Influence of AO.\nk: Noise Opacity | Visible amount of noise in dusty areas.\nuse: Settled dust on horizontal surfaces.\ncop: Upward facing from the Z component of the world normal (@channelextract), multiplied by AO with @blend {Mode}=Multiply, plus noise from @fractalnoise; @remap for the level and contrast.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-edge-blur\nname: Edge Blur\nsrc: /mask-generators/edge-blur/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Simple edge highlight mask from the curvature map with a blur.\nk: Level | Amount of edge highlighting.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Blur Radius | Blur on the highlighted edges.\nuse: Soft edge highlights.\ncop: @curvature convexity into @remap then @blur.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-edge-damages\nname: Edge Damages\nsrc: /mask-generators/edge-damages/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Mask of damage on raised convex edges from curvature and AO, from chipped to heavily scratched.\nk: Level | Amount of edge damage.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Damages Intensity | Shifts between a chipped, consistent look and a chaotic scratched look.\nuse: Chips on corners.\ncop: Convexity from @curvature masked by AO, broken up with @fractalnoise through @blend and thresholded with @remap.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-edge-dirt\nname: Edge Dirt\nsrc: /mask-generators/edge-dirt/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Dirt accumulating around edges based on curvature alone, with large-scale variation.\nk: Level | Amount of dirt.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Variation | Amount of large-scale breakup.\nk: Override variation mask | Uses a custom variation input.\nuse: Grime on edges.\ncop: @curvature plus a low-frequency @fractalnoise variation multiplied in, then @remap.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-edge-notch\nname: Edge Notch\nsrc: /mask-generators/edge-notch/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Mask of raised edges broken up with a high-frequency noise.\nk: Level | Level of the effect.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nuse: Nicked edges.\ncop: Convexity from @curvature minus fine noise (@fractalnoise with a small {Element Size}) via @blend {Mode}=Subtract.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-edge-select\nname: Edge Select\nsrc: /mask-generators/edge-select/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Selects convex and concave edges from curvature with separate width, softness and intensity.\nk: Level | Total amount of edge highlighting.\nk: Contrast | Contrast for both edge types.\nk: Convex Edges Width | Width of convex edge highlighting.\nk: Convex Softness | Softness of convex edges.\nk: Convex Intensity | Maximum convex intensity.\nk: Concave Edges Width | Width of concave edges.\nk: Concave Softness | Softness of concave edges.\nk: Concave Intensity | Maximum concave intensity.\nuse: Clean masks for edge wear (convex) and cavity dirt (concave).\ncop: @curvature with {Output Type}=Convexity and Concavity (two nodes), each shaped by @remap ({Operation}=Threshold with a {Width} for softness).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-edge-speckle\nname: Edge Speckle\nsrc: /mask-generators/edge-speckle/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: Edge highlight mask with a speckle added to break it up.\nk: Level | Total amount of highlighting.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Edge selection | Influence of convex edges.\nk: Variation | Extent to which the variation mask breaks up the effect.\nuse: Chipped paint specks along edges.\ncop: Convexity from @curvature multiplied by a speckle mask from @fractalnoise thresholded with @remap.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mg-edge-wear\nname: Edge Wear\nsrc: /mask-generators/edge-wear/\ncat: Mesh based generators > Mask generators\nrel: low\npurpose: General wear mask on object edges with level, threshold, width and disorder controls.\nk: Level | Total spread of the effect.\nk: Contrast | Contrast of the result.\nk: Threshold | Similar to level, total spread.\nk: Edges Width | Fullness of the highlighting.\nk: Disorder | Noise blended in to break up the smoothness.\nuse: Edge wear on props, similar logic usable on heights (edge detect of a height plus noise).\ncop: @curvature (convexity) or @edgedetect on the height, @dila