{"parentUuid":"29bc1c9b-43b7-4500-99c3-2d8c5478c5d9","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a9840a94295146d85","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfveNmiY94BUkYZ77WAgK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SLCxKESdathptYgDHy2s1M","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-zenray--claude-Memory1/3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953/scratchpad/work/entries/11_spline_path.txt","content":"## spline-render\nname: Spline Render\nsrc: /spline-tools/spline-render/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: medium\npurpose: Draws strings of segments along the input splines over a background, with thickness, joints and an envelope; the basic way to turn splines into an image.\nk: Mode | Which splines are drawn (all, one index or a range).\nk: Segments Amount | Segments used to draw each spline.\nk: Thickness (px) | Line thickness in pixels (or relative to the image).\nk: Enable Joints | Rounds the joints between segments.\nk: Non-Square Correction | Keeps the spline shape on non-square images.\nuse: Cracks, rivers, roads, rails and scratches drawn along hand-authored or generated curves, to subtract from or add to a height.\ncop: @rasterizecurves (draws curves with {Width}, {Joints}, {Endpoints}, {Units}) or @layerfromcurves (also gives profile, UV and ID outputs); the curves come from @curve3d or from SOP geometry via @sopimport.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## spline-fill\nname: Spline Fill\nsrc: spline-fill.md\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: medium\npurpose: Fills the interior of input splines with white and the exterior with black (open splines are closed by a straight line).\nnote: The documentation page lists three spline inputs and no parameters.\nuse: Region masks from drawn outlines, such as pond shapes or plateau outlines for height edits.\ncop: @maskfromcurves ({Output Type}=Mask or SDF, {Invert}, {Blur}).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## spline-circle\nname: Spline Circle\nsrc: /spline-tools/spline-circle/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Generates a single spline in the shape of a circle (also spirals), with thickness and height along it.\nk: Circle Radius | Radius of the circle.\nk: Circle Position | Centre position.\nk: Start Thickness | Thickness at the start.\nk: End Thickness | Thickness at the end.\nk: Trim | Trims a part of the circle.\nk: Spiral | Turns the circle into a spiral.\nuse: Rings, craters rims and circular grooves.\ncop: A circle curve from @curve3d or a SOP circle brought in through @sopimport, drawn with @rasterizecurves; or @sdfshape (Circle with thickness) for a direct raster.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## spline-cubic\nname: Spline (Cubic)\nsrc: /spline-tools/spline-cubic/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Generates a spline between two points with tangents and per-end thickness and height.\nk: Flip Direction | Reverses the spline direction.\nk: Start Height | Height at the start.\nk: End Height | Height at the end.\nk: Start Thickness | Thickness at the start.\nk: End Thickness | Thickness at the end.\nuse: Hand-placed curved cracks or road segments.\ncop: A Bezier curve drawn with @curve3d (Bezier primitive) with point widths, rendered by @rasterizecurves ({Width Attribute}).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## spline-quadratic\nname: Spline (Quadratic)\nsrc: /spline-tools/spline-quadratic/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Generates a quadratic spline between two points controlled by a third point, with adjustable arc span, height and thickness.\nk: Smoothness | Smoothness of the arc.\nk: Start height | Height at the start.\nk: End height | Height at the end.\nk: Start thickness | Thickness at the start.\nk: End thickness | Thickness at the end.\nuse: Arched cracks, bridges and curved roads.\ncop: @curve3d with a three point Bezier or NURBS curve, drawn with @rasterizecurves.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## spline-poly-quadratic\nname: Spline (Poly Quadratic)\nsrc: /spline-tools/spline-poly-quadratic/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Generates a smooth spline through several points, which can come from a Point List node.\nk: Points Amount | Number of points.\nk: Close Spline | Closes the spline.\nk: Flip Direction | Reverses the direction.\nk: Use Input Point List | Takes the points from a Point List.\nuse: Rivers and winding paths through placed waypoints.\ncop: @curve3d with several points (NURBS or Bezier) or a polyline resampled in SOPs and smoothed; drawn with @rasterizecurves.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## point-list\nname: Point List\nsrc: /spline-tools/point-list/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Generates a list of points (with height, thickness and smoothness properties) that a spline can traverse; appends to an existing list if connected.\nk: Point Number | Number of generated points.\nk: Global Smoothness Adjustment | Uniform offset of the smoothness of all points.\nk: Show Labels | Shows point names in the preview.\nk: Show Points | Shows the points in the preview.\nuse: Waypoints for rivers and paths.\ncop: A point cloud from SOPs (@sopimport) or @pointgenerate and the curve built through them (SOP curve from points).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## spline-merge-list\nname: Spline Merge List\nsrc: /spline-tools/spline-merge-list/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Merges all splines of a list into a single spline.\nk: Closed Spline Distance Threshold | Distance under which closed splines are joined.\nk: Segments Amount | Segments used for the preview.\nuse: Combining separate pieces into one path.\ncop: Merge and join curves in SOPs (Merge, then Fuse and Join) before @sopimport.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## spline-append\nname: Spline Append\nsrc: /spline-tools/spline-append/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Appends one list of splines onto another, preserving order.\nk: Flip Spline #1 Direction | Reverses the first list.\nk: Flip Spline #2 Direction | Reverses the second list.\nuse: Building one list from several sources.\ncop: Merge in SOPs (Merge node) or merge curve geometry through @pointmerge only for point clouds; curves themselves merge in SOPs.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## spline-select\nname: Spline Select\nsrc: /spline-tools/spline-select/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Selects splines of a list by index or range, optionally trimmed, and outputs a new list.\nk: Selection Mode | How splines are selected.\nk: Spline Index | Index of the selected spline.\nk: Range Start | First index of the range.\nk: Range End | Last index of the range.\nuse: Isolating curves for separate rendering.\ncop: Group and Blast nodes in SOPs before @sopimport.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## spline-2d-transform\nname: Spline 2D Transform\nsrc: /spline-tools/spline-2d-transform/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Applies a global 2D transformation to all splines, including reversing their direction.\nk: Flip Direction | Reverses the direction of all splines.\nk: Transform Matrix | Rotation and scale.\nk: Offset | Translation.\nuse: Positioning a set of curves.\ncop: A Transform SOP before @sopimport, or @curve3d with its own transform.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## spline-warp\nname: Spline Warp\nsrc: /spline-tools/spline-warp/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Displaces splines using an intensity map or a vector map with attenuation along the spline.\nk: Warp Intensity | Strength of the displacement.\nk: Warp Center | Neutral value of the map.\nk: Use Vector Map | Uses a vector map instead of the slopes of an intensity map.\nk: Use Attenuation Curve | Attenuates the warp along the spline.\nk: Recompute Tangents | Recomputes tangents after displacement.\nuse: Organic wandering of cracks and rivers following a noise.\ncop: Displace the curve points in SOPs with a noise (Mountain or Attribute Noise), or sample a COP layer at the points with @attribfromlayer and @geoattribfromlayer.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## spline-sample-height\nname: Spline Sample Height\nsrc: /spline-tools/spline-sample-height/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Modifies the height of splines by sampling a height map on them, with blending mode and opacity.\nk: Sampling Mode | How the map is mapped on the splines.\nk: Opacity | Strength of the effect.\nk: Blending Mode | Blend mode of the sampled height.\nuse: Making rivers follow terrain height or bridges follow a profile.\ncop: Sample the height layer at curve points in SOPs through a COP-to-SOP attribute transfer (@attribfromlayer, @geoattribfromlayer).\nstatus: unverified\n\n## spline-sample-thickness\nname: Spline Sample Thickness\nsrc: /spline-tools/spline-sample-thickness/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Modifies the thickness of splines by sampling a thickness map.\nk: Sampling Mode | How the map is mapped on the splines.\nk: Opacity | Strength of the effect.\nk: Blending Mode | Blend mode of the sampled thickness.\nuse: Variable-width cracks and paths driven by a noise.\ncop: A width attribute on the curve points set from a noise or layer, drawn with @rasterizecurves using {Width Attribute}.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## spline-bridge-2-splines\nname: Spline Bridge (2 Splines)\nsrc: /spline-tools/spline-bridge-2-splines/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Generates splines running from the first spline to the second, linear or cubic Bezier.\nk: Bridge Splines Amount | Number of generated bridges.\nk: Bridge Splines Type | Linear or Bezier.\nk: Offset Random Start | Random offset at the start.\nk: Offset Random End | Random offset at the end.\nuse: Cables, hairs, roots and connecting cracks.\ncop: Build lines between matched points of two curves in SOPs (Add or Connect Adjacent Pieces) and render with @rasterizecurves.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## spline-bridge-list\nname: Spline Bridge (List)\nsrc: /spline-tools/spline-bridge-list/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Generates splines traversing all splines of a list.\nk: Bridge Spline Amount | Number of generated bridges.\nk: Bridge Splines Type | Linear or quadratic Bezier.\nk: Input Splines are Closed | Treats the inputs as closed.\nk: Close Bridge Spline | Closes the generated spline.\nuse: Rope strands, cable bundles and lofted ribs.\ncop: SOP lofting (Skin or Loft) of the input curves, rendered with @rasterizecurves.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## spline-bridge-mapper-grayscale\nname: Spline Bridge Mapper Grayscale\nsrc: /spline-tools/spline-bridge-mapper-grayscale/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Maps a grayscale image across a list of splines so the image traverses the splines in order.\nk: Segments Amount | Segments of the mapping.\nk: Reduce UVs Stretching | Reduces stretching of the UVs.\nk: UV Scale | Scale of the mapping.\nk: UV Rotation | Rotation of the mapping.\nuse: Strand and braid details along curves.\ncop: @layerfromcurves ({Profile}, {Color along Length}, {Color across Width}, {UV Twist Rate}) and its {o:uv} output, then @sample (UV Sample) of the pattern.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## spline-bridge-mapper-color\nname: Spline Bridge Mapper Color\nsrc: /spline-tools/spline-bridge-mapper-color/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Colour version of the Spline Bridge Mapper.\nk: Segments Amount | Segments of the mapping.\nk: UV Scale | Scale of the mapping.\nuse: Coloured strand details.\ncop: Same as the grayscale mapper with an RGB pattern in @sample.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## spline-mapper-grayscale\nname: Spline Mapper Grayscale\nsrc: /spline-tools/spline-mapper-grayscale/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: medium\npurpose: Maps a grayscale image onto a primitive shape (plane, half-cylinder or cylinder) stretched along splines, with optional twist; outputs colour, height, UV and ID.\nk: Segments Amount | Segments of the mapping.\nk: Auto Scale UVs | Scales the UVs automatically.\nk: Mode | Which splines are drawn.\nk: Thickness | Thickness of the shape.\nk: Shape | Plane, half-cylinder or cylinder.\nk: Cylinder Height Multiplier | Height of the cylinder profile.\nuse: Pipes, cables, rope and tubular details with a texture running along them.\ncop: @layerfromcurves ({Width}, {Profile} for the cylinder cross-section, {UV Twist Rate}) with its {o:uv} output driving @sample for the texture, and its {o:profile} output as the height.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## spline-mapper-color\nname: Spline Mapper Color\nsrc: /spline-tools/spline-mapper-color/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Colour version of the Spline Mapper.\nk: Segments Amount | Segments of the mapping.\nk: Shape | Plane, half-cylinder or cylinder.\nuse: Textured tubes in colour.\ncop: As the grayscale mapper with an RGB pattern.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## spline-flow-mapper\nname: Spline Flow Mapper\nsrc: /spline-tools/spline-flow-mapper/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: medium\npurpose: Draws a flow map along splines (direction, trajectory, intensity and thickness of the flow with an attenuation profile).\nk: Segments Amount | Segments used to draw.\nk: Mode | Which splines are drawn.\nk: Thickness Mode | How thickness is determined.\nk: Direction | Flow direction relative to the spline.\nk: Attenuation Profile | Fade of the flow towards the neutral background.\nuse: Flow maps that drive Vector Warp (water running along a river curve), directional smearing along a path.\ncop: @layerfromcurves ({Profile}, {Color across Width}) with tangent directions encoded by an attribute and rasterised by @rasterizecurves; the result feeds @distort through {i:dir}.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## scatter-on-spline-grayscale\nname: Scatter on Spline Grayscale\nsrc: /spline-tools/scatter-spline-grayscale/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: medium\npurpose: Draws patterns along input splines over a background, with spacing, duplicates, size, position, rotation and masking controls.\nk: Shape Amount | Number of evenly spaced patterns on each spline.\nk: Shape Spacing | Minimum spacing along the spline.\nk: Pattern | Pattern or input image scattered.\nk: Duplicates Amount | Number of duplicated patterns.\nk: Scale | Global size of the patterns.\nk: Scale Random | Random scale.\nk: Align with Tangent | Rotates patterns to follow the spline.\nk: Mask Random | Random masking of patterns.\nuse: Stones along a path, studs along a seam, leaves along a branch, chain links and rivet lines in heights.\ncop: @curvescatter: {Distribution} (Distance, Scatter, By Count), {Segment Length}, {Angles Relative to Curve Direction}, {Scale Variance}, {Jitter}, {Offset along Curve}, {Max Count}, and the stamps on {i:stamps}; blend with {Blend Method}=Maximum.\ngray: Grayscale pattern version.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## scatter-on-spline-color\nname: Scatter on Spline Color\nsrc: /spline-tools/scatter-on-spline-color/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Colour version of Scatter on Spline.\nk: Shape Amount | Number of evenly spaced patterns on each spline.\nk: Blend Mode | How pattern colours blend with the background.\nk: Color Mode | How the colour of each pattern is chosen.\nuse: Coloured scatters along paths.\ncop: @curvescatter with {Stamp Color} controls and RGBA stamps.\nstatus: sidefx\n\n## scatter-splines-on-splines\nname: Scatter Splines on Splines\nsrc: /spline-tools/scatter-splines-on-splines/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Places splines along parent splines to build intricate structures (hair, branches, veins).\nk: Side | Side of the parent spline used.\nk: Amount Mode | How the number of child splines is determined.\nk: Spline Amount Per Spline | Number of children per parent.\nk: Spline Spacing | Spacing of children.\nk: Spline Type | Type of child splines.\nk: Flip Direction | Reverses the child direction.\nuse: Veins in leaves, branching cracks, hair strands.\ncop: Branching built in SOPs (scatter points on the parent curves and copy child curves oriented to the tangent) before @sopimport and @rasterizecurves.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## uv-mapper-grayscale\nname: UV Mapper Grayscale\nsrc: uv-mapper-grayscale.md\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: medium\npurpose: Maps a grayscale input image using coordinates supplied in a UV input (a generic warp lookup).\nnote: The documentation page lists a UV input and an Input image and no parameters.\nuse: Applying a computed UV remap, for example the UV output of a mapper, polar transforms or lattice deformations.\ncop: @sample (UV Sample): {i:uv} and {i:texture} inputs, {Filter}, {UV Space}.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## uv-mapper-color\nname: UV Mapper Color\nsrc: /spline-tools/uv-mapper-color/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Maps a colour input image using coordinates supplied in a UV input.\nk: Background Color | Colour used where the UV does not point to the image.\nuse: Colour lookups through a UV remap.\ncop: @sample with an RGB texture.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## mask-to-paths\nname: Mask to Paths\nsrc: /path-tools/mask-to-paths/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Path tools\nrel: medium\npurpose: Converts a grayscale mask into a list of path segments, with control over start positions, ordering and smoothing.\nk: Smooth Mask | Smooths the mask before tracing.\nk: Mask Threshold Value | Threshold used to find the outlines.\nk: Decimate Path | Reduces the number of path points.\nk: Close opened Paths | Closes open paths.\nk: Corner Threshold | Angle threshold for corners.\nk: Order Mode | How paths are ordered in the list.\nuse: Vectorising a mask (for instance crack outlines) so they can be warped, transformed and re-rendered with a stroke width.\ncop: No tracing node; the SOP side offers contouring from volumes (Isosurface of a height volume brought in with @layertogeo-style conversion). The practical COP path is @edgedetect or @sdfadjust ({Outline}) for outlines. UNVERIFIED.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## paths-polygon\nname: Paths Polygon\nsrc: /path-tools/paths-polygon/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Path tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Generates a polygon primitive in the Paths format.\nk: Number of Sides | Number of sides of the polygon.\nuse: Polygonal outlines.\ncop: @sdfshape (Regular Polygon, {Number of Sides}) or a SOP circle with few divisions.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## paths-select\nname: Paths Select\nsrc: /path-tools/paths-select/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Path tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Isolates one path among several in a Paths list.\nk: Selection Mode | How a path is chosen.\nk: Path ID | Index of the path.\nk: Target Length | Length used for the length-based selection.\nuse: Picking specific outlines.\ncop: Group by attribute or length in SOPs.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## path-2d-transform\nname: Path 2D Transform\nsrc: /path-tools/path-2d-transform/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Path tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Transforms Paths with a gizmo.\nk: Transform matrix | Rotation and scale.\nk: Offset | Translation.\nuse: Positioning vectorised outlines.\ncop: Transform SOP, or @xform2d on the rasterised result.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## paths-warp\nname: Paths Warp\nsrc: /path-tools/paths-warp/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Path tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Deforms Paths according to a gradient input, like the Warp node but on vectors.\nk: Intensity | Strength of the deformation.\nk: Number of steps | Steps of the warp integration.\nuse: Organic distortion of vector outlines.\ncop: Displace the points in SOPs with a field sampled from the layer, or warp the raster result with @distort.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## paths-to-spline\nname: Paths to Spline\nsrc: /path-tools/paths-to-spline/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Path tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Converts Paths into splines that Spline Render and the Spline nodes can use.\nk: Splines Precision | Precision of the conversion.\nuse: Bridging the path tools to the spline tools.\ncop: Not needed in Houdini: curves are the same geometry type in SOPs and are drawn with @rasterizecurves.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## paths-vertex-processor\nname: Paths Vertex Processor\nsrc: /path-tools/paths-vertex-processor/paths-vertex-processor.md\ncat: Spline and path tools > Path tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Transforms the vertices of Paths with a function graph that can read the previous and next vertices.\nk: Previous Vertices Accessed | Number of previous vertices readable by the function.\nk: Next Vertices Accessed | Number of next vertices readable.\nk: Per Vertex Function | The function graph run per vertex.\nuse: Custom path deformations.\ncop: Wrangle SOP (VEX) on the curve points.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## paths-vertex-processor-simple\nname: Paths Vertex Processor Simple\nsrc: paths-vertex-processor-simple.md\ncat: Spline and path tools > Path tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Simplified vertex processor that works on the vertex position only.\nk: Image Input Count | Number of image inputs.\nk: Per Vertex Function | The function graph run per vertex.\nuse: Scaling or offsetting path vertices.\ncop: Wrangle SOP (VEX) on the curve points.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## preview-paths\nname: Preview Paths\nsrc: /path-tools/preview-paths/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Path tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Draws the segments and vertices of Paths over a background with one random colour per path.\nk: Show Corners | Shows corner points.\nk: Show Vertices | Shows vertices.\nk: Segments Thickness (px) | Thickness of the drawn segments.\nuse: Debugging path lists.\ncop: @rasterizecurves over the background with a random colour attribute (@randomrgb on the ID), or the Scene Viewer.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## quad-transform-on-path\nname: Quad Transform on Path\nsrc: /path-tools/quad-transform-on-path/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Path tools\nrel: low\npurpose: Deforms Paths using four handles.\nk: p00 | First handle.\nk: p01 | Second handle.\nk: p02 | Third handle.\nk: p03 | Fourth handle.\nuse: Perspective-like deformation of vector outlines.\ncop: Bend or Lattice SOP on the curves, or @cornerpin on the raster result.\nstatus: unverified\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1795,"cache_read_input_tokens":802651,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1795,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SLCxKESdathptYgDHy2s1M":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-zenray--claude-Memory1/3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953/scratchpad/work/entries/11_spline_path.txt","content":"## spline-render\nname: Spline Render\nsrc: /spline-tools/spline-render/\ncat: Spline and path tools > Spline tools\nrel: medium\npurpose: Draws strings of segments along the input splines over a background, with thickness, joints and an envelope; the basic way to turn splines into an image.\nk: Mode | Which splines are drawn (all, one index or a range).\nk: Segments Amount | Segments used to draw each spline.\nk: Thickness (px) | Line thickness in pixels (or relative to the image).\nk: Enable Joints | Rounds the joints between segments.\nk: Non-Square Correction | Keeps the spline shape on non-square images.\nuse: Cracks, rivers, roads, rails and scratches drawn along hand-authored or generated curves, to subtract from or add to a height.\ncop: @rasterizecurves (draws curves with {Width}, {Joints}, {Endpoints}, {Units}) or @layerfromcurves (also gives profile, UV and ID outputs); the curves come from @curve3d or from SOP geometry via @sopimport.\nstatus: unverified\n\n## spline-fill\nname: Spline Fill\nsrc: spline-fill.md\ncat: Spline an