{"parentUuid":"c9d30189-0278-4e34-825b-b530c7b38a65","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a9840a94295146d85","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016R2aGp3tyrtndodVN8ghRi","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"The Quadrant Node\" FX-Map Substance 3D Designer experienceleague.adobe.com\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"FXMaps\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-function-graphs/fx-maps/fxmaps\"},{\"title\":\"The Quadrant Node\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-function-graphs/fx-maps/the-quadrant-node\"},{\"title\":\"How it works\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-function-graphs/fx-maps/how-it-works\"},{\"title\":\"The Iterate Node\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-function-graphs/fx-maps/the-iterate-node\"},{\"title\":\"Using the Sampler nodes\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-function-graphs/fx-maps/using-substance-function-graphs-in-fx-maps/using-the-sampler-nodes\"},{\"title\":\"FX-Map\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/atomic-nodes/fx-map\"},{\"title\":\"Using the SetSequence nodes\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-function-graphs/fx-maps/using-substance-function-graphs-in-fx-maps/using-the-set-sequence-nodes\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters not working as expected\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/technical-issues/parameters-not-working-as-expected\"},{\"title\":\"Exposing a parameter\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/manage-parameters/exposing-a-parameter\"},{\"title\":\"Version 14.1\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/release-notes/version-14-1\"}]\n\nThe Adobe documentation page for **The Quadrant Node** covers this topic directly. Its main points:\n\n- **Core function:** The node divides the FX-Map image into four parts for the next node in the chain, and it is the only node type that adds depth to the underlying quad-tree. The Quadrant node merely subdivides the FX-Map image, splitting it into four for the next node in the chain. It is the only node which can increase the depth or octave of the FX-Map graph.\n- **Parameters:** Settings include Branch Offset, Pattern, Pattern Offset, Pattern Size, Pattern Rotation, Pattern Variation, Blending Mode, Random Seed, and Inherit Random. Several of these can be driven by a Dynamic Function. Branch Offset, for example, moves the node's image and every image rendered below it in the same branch.\n- **Patterns:** By default no pattern is drawn. You can instead supply an input image or pick one of the built-in shapes, which include Square, Disc, Bell, Gaussian, Thorn, Pyramid, Brick, Waves, and Capsule, among others.\n- **Color limitation:** A Quadrant node can only render a grayscale input image in a grayscale FX-Map, and a color input only in a color FX-Map. Mixing types requires converting the inputs earlier in the graph.\n- **Random seeds:** The node's seed produces a repeatable sequence of pseudo-random values, and Inherit Random can pass the seed down from the node above it.\n\nThe same documentation section also explains how the FX-Map system fits together. The FX-Map node itself is described on a separate reference page, and the Iterate node is documented as a companion to Quadrant for repeating images.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e1a23497-df1c-4f62-8c6e-ef52e86417b6","timestamp":"2026-10-1