ze; Bevel is Feather; Distance is Feather plus Extrapolate Boundaries; Directional Blur is Streak Blur; Warp is Distort; Slope Blur is the Distort by Slope recipe; Flood Fill is Segment by Connectivity plus UV Map by ID (Random Mono and Random RGB replace the random Flood Fill nodes); Perlin Noise is Fractal Noise; Shape is SDF Shape wired into SDF to Mono; Min Max is Statistics; Splatter and Tile Sampler correspond to Scatter Shapes and Scatter on Curves; Tile Generator is Tile Pattern; Uniform Color is Constant; HSL is HSV Adjust; RGBA Split is Channel Split; Alpha Merge is Blend with Mode Add; Output is Null plus ROP Image; Ambient Occlusion (HBAO) is Height to Ambient Occlusion; Base Material is Preview Material; Make It Tile is Tile Pattern plus Feather.\n- Value range: Designer grayscale values live in 0 to 1 (with optional 16 or 32 bit float precision); COP layers are floating point and may be negative or above 1. Noise generators produce values from Center minus Amplitude to Center plus Amplitude (local COP help), the Post Processing group of generators (Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum, applied in that order) reshapes the histogram, and Clamp Minimum and Clamp Maximum or the Clamp COP bring values back to the 0 to 1 range. In this mapping Fold is an absolute value, Complement is one minus x (Designer Invert), Contrast and Gamma match the Designer controls of the same names (UNVERIFIED for exact curves).\n- Tiling: Designer noises and patterns tile by default. In COP, generators expose Tile Size (the noise repeats with that period; Element Size and Lacunarity are rounded or clamped when it is on), and filters that sample neighbours should use Wrap as the border (Read Pixels outside Image for derivative based nodes) so seams stay closed; Make It Tile style edge repair is only needed for photographic input.\n- Feature size: Designer Scale is a grid subdivision count (more cells means smaller features); COP uses Element Size in image coordinates (smaller number means smaller features), so Element Size is roughly one over Scale for a unit canvas (UNVERIFIED for the exact factor of each noise).\n- Units: Designer blur and distance parameters are resolution independent numbers; COP blur, dilate, sharpen and streak nodes offer Units (Image, Pixels, Local); choose Image to keep results independent of the resolution. The numeric relation between a Designer Intensity and a COP size is not documented.\n- Randomness: Designer nodes expose a Random Seed; COP generators expose Seed and Offset; per-tile or per-island randomness is built by wiring an ID layer (from Tile Pattern, Segment by Connectivity or Cellular Noise) into the seed input of Random Mono, Random RGB or UV Transform.\n- Height scale: a COP height layer is nominal. Normals, ambient occlusion, shadows, curvature and slope direction all take an explicit Height Scale (or Space) setting and need tuning to reproduce the look of the Designer graph.\n- Normals: COP stores normals as Signed (-1 to 1) or Offset (0 to 1) through Normal Type, with Convert Normal to switch; the DirectX versus OpenGL green flip of Designer is a separate channel inversion in COP (check the engine convention of the target).\n- Multi-channel materials: Designer material filters work on bundled channels; COP carries bundles as cables (Cable Pack, Cable Unpack, Cable Split, Cable Merge, Cable Switch). Whether each filter processes every wire of a cable should be checked per node in Houdini.\n- Custom per-pixel code: Pixel Processor and Value Processor functions become OpenCL (preferred, GPU) or VEX Wrangle (CPU) snippets; FX-Map recursion becomes point generation in SOPs or code followed by Scatter Shapes, Stamp Points or Copy and Transform.\n- Colour management: Convert To Linear and Convert to sRGB correspond to the OCIO Transform COP; height, mask and normal data should be read with the Raw colour space when loaded from files.\n- A typical Designer height graph and its Copernicus rebuild: base noise (Fractal Noise) or tiles (Tile Pattern with Draw As Distance for bevels), per-tile variation (Segment by Connectivity then UV Map by ID and Random Mono), shape control (Remap with Operation Threshold), organic breakup (Distort driven by a noise or by Slope Direction), edge detail (Feather, Edge Detect, Dilate Erode), combination (Blend with Maximum, Add or Subtract, or Compare and Blend for height blends), then outputs (Height to Normal, Height to Ambient Occlusion, Curvature) and export (Null plus ROP Image).\n- Gaps with no direct COP node (as far as the Houdini 22.0.368 node list shows): the Grunge Map 001 to 015 family (bake them instead), true histogram equalisation, the Height Blend family (rebuild with Compare and Blend), Shape Splatter v2 collision-free packing, FX-Map as such, mesh-based mask generators (rebuild from baked maps), the Spline and Path tool graph (use SOP curves with Rasterize Curves) and Substance function graph nodes (use OpenCL or VEX).\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b31b2ddd-c0ac-4145-9b4e-eec1794692e0","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfvepHSuinagb5hnxdXUG","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","attributionSkill":"zenray-houdini","type":"assistant","uuid":"8e560d52-1484-48a3-9779-86fbb340230f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T15:03:20.061Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
