rial Height Blend and a changed triangulation method in Triangle Grid.\n- Version 15.0 (15 July 2025): new 3D renderer and USD scene editing (no new compositing nodes).\n- Version 15.1 (11 December 2025): noise rework: Anisotropic Noise v2, BnW Spots 1 to 3 v2, Cells 1 to 4 v2, Clouds 1 to 3 v2, Directional Noise 1 to 4 v2, Directional Scratches v2, Dirt 1 to 5 v2, Dirt Gradient v2, Fractal Sum Base and Fractal Sum 1 to 4 v2 and others now offer the Disorder controls, a default output format and no forced tiling, plus hash functions, a Color to Mask v2 and a node menu hierarchy.\n- Version 16.0 (14 April 2026): Shape splatter v2 and its mapper and mask companions, the Grid atlas nodes, the 3D viewer node, the 3D SDF function node family and OpenPBR support. All of these are included here.\n\n## Nodes not documented in this file\n\n- Every compositing graph node page of the Adobe node library, atomic nodes, graph items and function graph essentials is covered. The only parsed page without a section is the index page of the mesh generator utilities.\n- Not documented: the individual Substance function graph library nodes beyond the families described (for example Average float, Cross product, Distance, Smoothstep, Parity and Conversion helpers, Hash 11 to Hash 32, and each of the roughly 60 SDF function primitives, operators, transforms and material setters, which are covered as one family entry); the Substance model graph nodes (scene management and curve editing); the MDL graph nodes; the bakers (not graph nodes); and any Designer plugin or user library content.\n- The documentation pages of some nodes (for example the grunge maps and the Clouds, Dirt and Directional noise variants) do not describe their visual character; their entries state this and avoid inventing it.\n- Equivalences marked UNVERIFIED have not been tested in Houdini by me (no Houdini session was opened); they were built from the Houdini 22.0.368 local node help, which lists COP node names, inputs,