{"parentUuid":"45a7ca29-46b1-4d4a-af46-ea4ff361836f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a9840a94295146d85","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HKfpEoKmxiU1pPQkrnXdqo","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Spline Render\" Substance 3D Designer experienceleague.adobe.com node library spline tools\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Spline Tools\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/node-library/spline-path-tools/spline-tools/spline-tools\"},{\"title\":\"Working with Path Spline tools\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/node-library/spline-path-tools/working-with-path-and-spline-tools\"},{\"title\":\"Spline Render\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/node-library/spline-path-tools/spline-tools/spline-render\"},{\"title\":\"Paths to Spline\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/node-library/spline-path-tools/paths-to-spline\"},{\"title\":\"All changes\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/release-notes/all-changes\"}]\n\nThe Adobe documentation for Spline Render is in the Substance 3D Designer node library under Spline Tools.\n\n**What it does:** The node is listed among the spline tools for generating, adjusting, and rendering splines. According to its page, it turns splines into textures, with control over width, color, and blend behavior. The Spline Render or Spline Fill node renders a spline using its shape and properties.\n\n**Inputs and output:** It takes a grayscale Background, which the splines are drawn over. Splines come in through Spline Coords and Spline Data color inputs, plus a Spline Amount integer. Its output is a grayscale image of the splines drawn on the background.\n\n**Key parameters:**\n- **Mode:** You can draw all splines in the list, a single spline by index, or a range of indexes.\n- **Segments Amount:** Controls how many segments make up each drawn spline. A higher value results in smoother lines. The guide also notes that a higher value results in smoother curves at the cost of performance.\n- **Thickness Size Mode:** Thickness can be set relative to the texture (Image) or as an absolute pixel count (Pixel).\n- **Spline Style:** Solid, Gradient, or Height, which determines how grayscale values are applied along the splines.\n- **Blend Mode:** Max keeps the brightest value where segments overlap, and Add sums them.\n- **Random Segments and Random Offset:** These cut segments at random and displace the pieces along their normals.\n- **Show Direction Helper:** Marks each spline's start with a dot and its end with an arrowhead.\n\n**Version history:** The node was added in version 13.0.0 of the release notes. Later 13.0.x releases fixed issues such as the last segment not being drawn and the output being clamped to the 0–1 range in 13.0.2.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b2bd5820-35ae-4207-b8f2-793db9b0a3f4","timestamp":"2026-10-11T15:07:09.433Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8925f9c9-8672-47e9-94a8-5058f551533c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":19,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory