{"parentUuid":"c5cf9eb7-eda7-43a6-bcee-befd422dcfb7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a9840a94295146d85","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017a1F8ZHTJBtwcEjnCeDmLo","type":"tool_result","content":"#type:     node\n#context:  cop\n#internal: gamma\n#icon:     COP/gamma\n\n= Gamma =\n\n\"\"\"Applies gamma correction to a layer, VDB, or attribute.\"\"\"\n\nThis node applies a [gamma correction|Wp:Gamma_correction], which is an exponential mapping, to a layer, VDB, or attribute. Since the eye is not linear, if you have a limited number of grayscale values it's best to have closer spacing near black and farther spacing near white. This is less necessary\n\nThe common gamma encountered is 2.2 or 1/2.2, though you can also use gamma for artistic effects.\n\n@parameters\n\nSignature:\n    #id: signature\n    \n    The layer type that the source accepts.\n\n    See [Signatures|/copernicus/glossary#signatures] for more information.\n    \n:include /nodes/cop/_parameter_descriptions#mask/:\n    \nGamma:\n    #id: gamma\n    \n    The gamma correction factor to use.  The common sRGB conversion is\n    `2.2`.  By default this is an encoding gamma, so the color values\n    are raised to the inverse of this exponent.\n    \nInvert:\n    #id: invert\n\n    Switches from an encoding gamma to a decoding gamma. This does the\n    opposite operation by inverting the gamma exponent.\n    \nTreat RGBA as Premultiplied:\n    #id: ispremult\n\n    Un-premultiplies the RGBA layers before applying the contrast and then premultiplies the RGBA layers.\n    \n    RGBA layers are often premultiplied, so using an exponentiation that doesn't consider the alpha causes low coverage areas to be considered dark. This parameter makes the exponentiation work as expected.\n\n@inputs\n    source:\n        The layer, VDB, or attribute to apply gamma correction to.\n\n    gamma:\n        An optional layer, VDB, or attribute that provides a per-pixel gamma correction. This value is multiplied with the __Gamma__ parameter and then inverted if __Invert__ is on.\n\n    :include /nodes/cop/_input_descriptions#mask/:\n\n@outputs\n    gamma:\n        The layer, VDB, or attribute with gamma correction.\n\n@related\n- [Node:cop/contrast]\n- [Node:cop/bright]\n#type:     node\n#context:  cop\n#internal: contrast\n#icon:     COP/contrast\n\n= Contrast =\n\n\"\"\"Applies contrast to a layer, VDB, or attribute.\"\"\"\n\nThis node applies contrast to a layer, VDB, or attribute.  This pushes values away from a\ncentral value when contrast is increased, or pulls them back to that\nvalue when contrast is decreased.\n\n@parameters\n\nSignature:\n    #id: signature\n    \n    The layer type that the source accepts.\n\n    See [Signatures|/copernicus/glossary#signatures] for more information.\n\n:include /nodes/cop/_parameter_descriptions#mask/:  \n    \nContrast:\n    #id: contrast\n    \n    How much contrast to apply.  `1` will leave the image unchanged.\n    Larger values will brighten light areas and darken dark areas, and\n    lower values will do the opposite.  `0` will cause all values to\n    be the contrast center.\n    \nContrast Center:\n    #id: center\n\n    The pivot around which contrast will occur.\n    \nRed:\n    #id: contrastred\n\n    Contrast and offset pair to apply to the red channel.\n    \n    \nGreen:\n    #id: contrastgreen\n    \n    Contrast and offset pair to apply to the green channel.\n    \nBlue:\n    #id: contrastblue","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"9fe363f8-6d4e-4e3d-9aea-6469c9de7936","timestamp":"2026-10-11T15:09:28.589Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5b1aefb6-0cd5-422a-a952-560101d45fbb","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":22,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"vi