deFX-confirmed): **Height Scale** (Height Depth), **Space** (Local or World, for the world-units option), **View Radius** (Radius), **Sample Count** (Quality), **Step Scale**, **Sample from Hemisphere**, and a **Remap Ramp** to shape the occlusion falloff. (11 October 2026)\n- Equivalence status: SideFX-confirmed at node level (the SideFX Copernicus for Substance 3D Designer users page lists this correspondence), parameter setup read from the local Houdini 22.0.368 node help (11 October 2026)\n##### Edge Detect\n- Copernicus 22 equivalent: `edgedetect` (set **Method** to Sobel, **Blur Before** to soften, **High Threshold**), widened with `dilateerode` (**Radius**) and rounded with `blur`; the invert toggle is `invert`. (11 October 2026)\n- Equivalence status: UNVERIFIED (mapping and parameter values inferred by me; COP node names checked against the Houdini 22.0.368 node list, parameter labels read in the local node help) (11 October 2026)\n##### Curvature\n- Copernicus 22 equivalent: `curvature` on the height layer directly (**Curvature Type**, **Output Type**=Convexity or Concavity, **Scale**, **Kernel Size**); from a normal layer first reconstruct a height with `normaltoheight` (or compute from the normal derivative). The pixel-thin line character is UNVERIFIED. (11 October 2026)\n- Equivalence status: UNVERIFIED (mapping and parameter values inferred by me; COP node names checked against the Houdini 22.0.368 node list, parameter labels read in the local node help) (11 October 2026)\n##### Tile Generator\n- Copernicus 22 equivalent: `tilepattern`. Set **Mode** to Tile Count and fill **Rows**/**Columns** (X Amount, Y Amount), or Seamless with **Divisions** for guaranteed tiling; **Pattern Type**=Stack Bond gives a square grid, Stretcher Bond gives the brick offset (also **Row Slide Offset** with a **Variation**); **Inset** is the interstice; **Draw As** chooses Filled, Distance (bevel-like falloff with **Fade Distance**), Gradient (with **Gradient Ramp** and **Rot