e** for seamless tiling. (11 October 2026)\n- Equivalence status: UNVERIFIED (mapping and parameter values inferred by me; COP node names checked against the Houdini 22.0.368 node list, parameter labels read in the local node help) (11 October 2026)\n##### Directional Noise 1\n- Copernicus 22 equivalent: `fractalnoise` with unequal **Element Scale** (turn on Per-Component Controls) to stretch it, rotated with `xform2d`; or `streakblur` (**Angle**, **Length**) on `randommono` for fine streaks. (11 October 2026)\n- Equivalence status: UNVERIFIED (mapping and parameter values inferred by me; COP node names checked against the Houdini 22.0.368 node list, parameter labels read in the local node help) (11 October 2026)\n##### Blend\n- Copernicus 22 equivalent: `blend`. SD mode to COP **Mode**: Copy is Over (or Blend with the mask), Add is Add, Subtract is Subtract (check operand order, or use **Swap FG and BG**), Multiply is Multiply, Max is Maximum, Min is Minimum, Divide is Divide, Overlay is Overlay, Screen is Screen, Soft light is SoftLight; Add Sub (foreground above 0.5 adds, below subtracts) has no mode: remap the foreground from 0..1 to -1..1 with `remap` and use Add (UNVERIFIED). Opacity is the **Mask** amount and the `mask` input; Switch is `switch`. (11 October 2026)\n- Equivalence status: UNVERIFIED (mapping and parameter values inferred by me; COP node names checked against the Houdini 22.0.368 node list, parameter labels read in the local node help) (11 October 2026)\n##### Auto Levels\n- Copernicus 22 equivalent: `equalize` with **Equalize By**=Stretch to Black and White (SideFX-confirmed correspondence); **Fit Method** chooses Shifting or Scaling values; **Black** and **White** set the target range. (11 October 2026)\n- Equivalence status: SideFX-confirmed at node level (the SideFX Copernicus for Substance 3D Designer users page lists this correspondence), parameter setup read from the local Houdini 22.0.368 node help (11 October 2026)","is_error":false}]},