{"parentUuid":"d6e30746-059f-4fd9-8a6d-464e2599b550","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a9840a94295146d85","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rh4qE873qi2kPeASYoJX6s","type":"tool_result","content":"##### Gradient Map Grayscale\n##### Warp Grayscale\n##### Directional Warp Grayscale\n##### Non Uniform Directional Warp Grayscale\n- Copernicus 22 equivalent: `distort` with a per-pixel direction layer in `dir` input (made from an angle map with `polartouv` or from `slopedir`), per-pixel `scale` input for the intensity map, and **Streak**=Min, Max or Blur for the Trail Mode; trail length through **Maximum Steps** and **Pixels per Step**; **Use Streak Weight Ramp** gives the fade. Keep the layers at the Mono signature for the grayscale node. (11 October 2026)\n##### Blur HQ Grayscale\n- Copernicus 22 equivalent: `blur` with **Filter**=Gaussian (default) and **Size** for the radius; **Units**=Image keeps the result resolution independent like Designer. The relation between Intensity and **Size** is not documented (UNVERIFIED), so match visually. Keep the layers at the Mono signature for the grayscale node. (11 October 2026)\n##### Non Uniform Blur Grayscale\n- Copernicus 22 equivalent: `blur` has a per-pixel `size` input: wire the blur map there (scaled by the **Size** parameter or **Scale Size**). Directional variants use `streakblur` with its `scalelength` input. UNVERIFIED for the anisotropy and asymmetry controls. Keep the layers at the Mono signature for the grayscale node. (11 October 2026)\n##### Histogram Select\n- Copernicus 22 equivalent: `remap` with **Use Ramp** on and a bump-shaped mono **Ramp** (peak at Position, base width Range, steepness set by interpolation); or two `remap` threshold passes (greater than lower edge, less than upper edge) merged with `blend` **Mode**=Minimum. UNVERIFIED. (11 October 2026)\n##### Levels\n- Copernicus 22 equivalent: `remap` (SideFX: Levels node is Remap): **Input Min** and **Input Max** are Level in low and high, **Output Min** and **Output Max** are Level out low and high, **Outside Range**=Clamp at End is the intermediary clamp; the midpoint is a separate `gamma` (which raises values to the inverse of **Gamma**) with **Gamma** equal to ln(m) divided by ln(0.5), where m is the mid level normalised between low and high, so that m maps to 0.5 (UNVERIFIED formula). (11 October 2026)\n##### Normal\n- Copernicus 22 equivalent: `heighttonormal`: **Height Scale** for Intensity, **Normal Type**=Offset (0 to 1) for an exportable normal map, **Kernel Size** to smooth stepping artefacts; the Y flip for DirectX is a green channel inversion (`channelswap` or `invert` on green only). (11 October 2026)\n##### Height to Normal World Units\n- Copernicus 22 equivalent: `heighttonormal` with **Height Scale** derived from the ratio Height Depth over Surface Size (the exact definition of the COP scale is relative to the image coordinate system, so verify visually; UNVERIFIED); the `slopedir` **Space** option (Image, Pixel, Local) shows that COP can also compute slopes in local (world pixel) units. (11 October 2026)\n##### Normal to Height HQ\n##### Emboss Grayscale\n##### Distance\n- Copernicus 22 equivalent: SideFX-confirmed: `feather` and `extrapolateboundaries` (the Distance page of SideFX). Set **Feather Direction**=Circle (Euclidean), Diamond (Manhattan) or Square (Chebyshev), **Distance for Unit Change** equal to the Maximum distance, and enable **Feather from High to Low** to grow bright shapes outward (off shrinks them inward); for tileable results turn **Include Border** on and apply the feather twice, as the COP help advises; for exact Euclidean distance an alternative is `monotosdf` then `sdftomono` with **Iso Range**. The colour-from-nearest-pixel mode is `extrapolateboundaries`. (11 October 2026)\n##### Bevel\n- Copernicus 22 equivalent: `feather` (SideFX-confirmed): **Feather Direction**=Circle for Round corners (Square or Octagon should give angular corners, UNVERIFIED), **Distance for Unit Change** as Distance, **Feather from High to Low** to choose outward growth of bright shapes (off shrinks them inward), **Include Border** on and a second pass for tileable results, then a custom profile with `remap` (**Use Ramp**); normals with `heighttonormal` (**Normal Type**, **Height Scale**). The SD smoothing option is an extra `blur`. (11 October 2026)\n##### Flood Fill\n- Copernicus 22 equivalent: `segmentbyconnectivity` (SideFX-confirmed) labels each connected region and gives an `id` output layer (**Connectivity**=Above Threshold with **Threshold**; pixels that fail the rule, such as grout, get ID -1 and alpha 0, and **Collapse IDs** renumbers from zero); `uvmapbyid` then derives per-island data (**Mode**=UV Map, Center, Minimum, Maximum or Size) and `statisticsbyid` gives per-ID area, minimum and maximum. The per-tile variation nodes below are built from these outputs. (11 October 2026)\n##### Flood Fill to Random Grayscale\n- Copernicus 22 equivalent: `randommono` with the island ID wired into its `seed` input and a **Range Values** of Min/Max (SideFX lists Random Mono as the Flood Fill to Random Grayscale equivalent); segmentation from `segmentbyconnectivity`. (11 October 2026)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ec1d0217-3316-47ac-92f9-fd5ea8fc24e5","timestamp":"2026-10-11T15:13:56.375Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"afd7765e-a98e-462e-b404-81683e2ec7ed","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d6e30746-059f-4fd9-8a6d-464e2599b550","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","vers